Royal Government of Cambodia launches National Action Plan for Disaster Risk Reduction 2019-2023
(Kandal): The Royal Government of Cambodia, through the National Committee for Disaster Management, has launched a National Action Plan for Disaster Risk Reduction 2021-2023 to help reduce the impact of disasters to a higher level.
The National Action Plan for Disaster Risk Reduction 2019-2023 will be officially launched on February 17, 2021 under the chairmanship of Senior Minister Kun Kim, First Vice President of the National Committee for Disaster Management, High Representative of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia and Chairman of the National Committee for Disaster Management.
The event was also attended by leaders of relevant ministries and technical officials of the National Committee for Disaster Management.
Disaster is an issue that the world is paying close attention to because it affects the lives of people and the national economy. The Royal Government of Cambodia has also paid close attention to addressing the impact of this disaster.
The National Action Plan for Disaster Risk Reduction 2019-2023 is another new achievement of the Royal Government of Cambodia under the leadership of Samdech Techo Hun Sen to promote the benefits and provide strategic direction for the planned activities for the next 5 years. 2019-2023 to reduce the level of vulnerability and vulnerability, prevent risks and dangers arising from disasters.
The National Action Plan for Disaster Risk Reduction 2019-2023 shows increased responsibility at all levels, starting to address disaster risk issues related to climate change: drought, lack of rainfall, insufficient flooding Floods, floods, riverbanks, rivers, infectious diseases, epidemics, etc.
Senior Minister Kun Kim reminded at the ceremony that disaster risk reduction is a cellular work that can not be carried out by any institution alone, there must be good coordination, efforts in all areas to implement together. By Ministries, Government Institutions, Private Sector Development Partners and Civil Society Organizations.
The National Action Plan for Disaster Risk Reduction 2019-2023 has four key strategic points, including: Disaster risk awareness, strengthening disaster risk governance, investing in disaster risk reduction for resilience and promotion. Elevation of disaster preparedness, response to recovery and better reconstruction.
On this occasion, on behalf of Samdech Techo Prime Minister, Senior Minister Kun Kim called on all Ministries, Government Institutions, Private Sector Development Partners, Civil Society, and NGOs to continue to cooperate in implementing the activities set out in the National Action Plan for Risk Reduction. Disaster 2019-2023 to be active and successful.
Senior Minister Kun Kim also thanked the relevant ministries, institutions of the Cambodian Red Cross, the Armed Forces, the provincial administration, philanthropists, national and international organizations and all stakeholders who have participated in responding to disasters effectively in the past. Tomorrow morning, the Royal Government Spokesperson Unit will hold a press conference on "Local Progress of Communes, Sangkats and Ongoing Directions of Siem Reap Province".
The press conference was chaired and coordinated by Mr. Phay Siphan, Minister Delegate to the Prime Minister and Chairman of the Royal Government Spokesperson Unit. Separately, the speaker who will participate is the representative of Siem Reap Provincial Administration.
