UV radiation rises in Ho Chi Minh City and coastal provinces (Video inside) (Phnom Penh): The Cambodian Embassy in Vietnam has announced that UV radiation, a deadly radiation, is on the rise in Ho Chi Minh City. And some coastal provinces. The peak of UV radiation occurred from 17 to 19 February 2021.
An UV index of 8 to 10 means that a high level of UV radiation can pass through a cloud of glasses and cause burns within 25 minutes. An index of 11 or more, UV rays can damage the skin and eyes in 15 minutes if exposed to direct sunlight.
Through this announcement, the Embassy called on students, trainees and Cambodians who are present in Vietnam, especially in the provinces and cities listed above, to be careful to wear protective clothing, heat, masks, Neck, ears and wear sunglasses, apply sunscreen when outdoors, even when it is cloudy and drink plenty of water and get enough vitamin C supplements.
General Vong Pisen: Training work plays an important role in capacity development, contributing to the reform of the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces
(Kampong Speu): On the morning of February 17, 2021, General Vong Pisen, Commander-in-Chief of the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces, presided over the closing ceremony of the 21st Generation Active Officers Training Course, which was held at the Active Officers' School. With the participation of officers from the Ministry of National Defense, the Commander-in-Chief and the Joint Chiefs of Staff of the Armed Forces of some friendly countries in Cambodia.
According to Lt. Gen. But Sopheap, Director of the Active Officers' Training School, the 21st Generation Officers Training Course had a total of 114 participants, and the course was nicknamed "Techo Generation, Founder of Peace".
Speaking on that occasion, General Vong Pisen praised and appreciated the active military academy and relevant institutions that have worked together responsibly to improve the curriculum and content of the four-year course. Undergraduate human resource training in the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces has proceeded successfully as planned.
The Commander-in-Chief emphasized that the Royal Government of Cambodia, under the wise leadership of Samdech Akka Moha Sena Padei Techo Hun Sen, has been implementing an in-depth reform plan in all areas, prioritizing education to train human resources. Vocational education for the next generation.
In this spirit, the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces (RCAF) has focused on training professional soldiers, building young officers, improving the quality of training, updating and promoting the implementation of strategic plans on defense, which are the most important factors in the construction and development process. Cambodian Army.
According to the Commander-in-Chief, "Training has played an important role in developing skills, contributing to the reform of the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces and strengthening the defense sector." Therefore, the training course that has been focused on training until the end of this course really responds to the current of increasing the human resource capacity of the Cambodian army.
General Vong Pisen instructed the trainees to be completely loyal to the nation, religion, the King, to raise the conscience of patriotism, to dare to make all kinds of sacrifices to defend the nation, defend the territorial integrity and protect the people, and at any cost to participate in the defense. Achieve the hard-earned peace, protect the legitimate government, oppose the color revolution and extremist movements that destroy peace and create social unrest.
At the same time, must strictly abide by the rules, regulations, general rules of the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces, state laws, and be united, respect each other, maintain military secrecy and be responsible in their work.
In addition, take the knowledge gained from the study and experience of the past 4 years to turn it into practical application and learn from the seniors, study the work experience, grasp the actual geography to reflect with the theory learned to develop themselves. Succeeded in fulfilling the tasks assigned by the unit.
On that occasion, General Vong Pisen also called on the leaders, officers, deputies and soldiers to continue to cooperate with the Royal Government to effectively prevent the spread of Kovid-19 and prepare for the upcoming vaccination. In the future.
