Two Disabled People in Banteay Meanchey Province Receive Homes from the Disability Fund Under the Care of the Royal Government
(Banteay Meanchey): Two poor people with disabilities living in Ta An 1 village, Srah Reang commune, Mongkul Borei district and Ta Phok village, Changha commune, O'Chrov district, Banteay Meanchey province received two houses from the Disability Fund. The handover program took place on February 16, 2021.
The Disability Foundation decided to provide a new house for one person, made of 4x6 meters of galvanized iron, so that they can have a suitable shelter.
Mr. Khun Vuthy, Director of Banteay Meanchey Provincial Department of Social Affairs, Veterans and Youth Rehabilitation, thanked the Disability Foundation for its efforts to raise funds for the construction of poor people with disabilities in Banteay Meanchey Province. Provide opportunities for people with disabilities to access better welfare.
Mr. Sim Sothoun, Director of the Disability Foundation, said that the Disability Foundation has already handed over eight houses to poor families in Battambang, Siem Reap, Takeo, Kampong Chhnang, Svay Rieng, Tbong Khmum, Pursat and Pailin. This time, the Disability Foundation organized the handing over ceremony of the 9th and 10th houses to the poor in Banteay Meanchey province and the handing over of the 11th house to another poor family in Oddar Meanchey province on February 17, 2021.
Ms. Pok Nady, Deputy Governor of Banteay Meanchey Province, on behalf of Mr. Oum Rath, Governor of Banteay Meanchey Province, stated that the Royal Government of Cambodia has taken great care of the disabled, not leaving the disabled alone, the Royal Government as well as the provincial leaders facilitated the reception Get support.
She also thanked the Disability Foundation for organizing this charity event aimed at improving the lives of poor people with disabilities. She also urged all citizens to participate in preventing the transmission of Kovid 19 through the implementation of protective measures of the Ministry of Health, as well as to cooperate in providing information related to travel from Thailand to Cambodia to the authorities.
In this ceremony, in addition to this new house, the Disability Foundation also donated a charity gift of the Disability Foundation to provide the families who received these two new houses with a budget of 100,000 Riels, 25 kg of rice under the fish. 2 sticks of soy sauce, 1 stick of fish sauce, 1 stick of salt, 2 bags and 1 box of noodles. People who participate in this program also receive 20,000 Riels per person from the Disability Fund.
