(Kratie): Mr. Net Pheaktra, Secretary of State and Spokesman for the Ministry of Environment, said that now the world and the people of Cambodia are beginning to turn to the use of wood processed from plantations and they do not value furniture and Materials made from natural wood, because all people understand the importance of preserving natural forests.
While natural resources play an important role in preserving the planet's ecosystems, people around the world today, such as in Europe and the United States, have opted not to use furniture made of natural wood but to support the use of manufactured furniture. From raw materials from plantations, experts believe that it reduces the pressure on the use of natural wood and the conservation of forest resources.
A spokesman for the Ministry of Environment said: "Many countries around the world are now starting to turn to the use of processed wood, and they do not value the furniture and materials that Made from natural wood, obviously, foreigners or our Cambodian people are also beginning to see this trend a lot, while hotels or guesthouses with beautiful wood are not very popular.
Mr. Neth Pheaktra made this remark during an interview with national and international journalists on the occasion of leading more than 300 youths to a two-day camp on February 14-15. 2021 at the Customs Headquarters in Prey Lang Wildlife Sanctuary, Kratie Province and visit the plantation of Sing Bay Otec (Cambodia).
Therefore, if all Cambodians refuse to use furniture made from natural wood, it will be part of reducing the pressure on natural resources, a spokesman for the Ministry of Environment said.
Mr. Neth Pheaktra pointed out that for any furniture processing business that has a legitimate business, the officials are respectful, but the park officials of the Ministry of Environment have cooperated with the relevant authorities and institutions to crack down on unlicensed wood depots or handicrafts.
A senior official of the Ministry of Environment stated that on behalf of the Royal Government and the Ministry of Environment, the plantation investment should be extended to other areas located in degraded forest areas or vacant land that can be cultivated. And can supply domestic market and foreign market.
Currently, the development of plantations is valuable in the supply of wood raw materials for the wood processing industry, while construction in Cambodia has been growing and growing, especially in Phnom Penh and Sihanoukville, where new building projects. A lot happens.
Due to insufficient domestic production, Cambodia also imports processed wood from abroad. Plantation plantations provide benefits for many people in the process of planting and harvesting as well as processing. As in Vietnam, they plant plantations, export to Europe each year, earn billions of dollars and create a lot of jobs for the people.
Vietnam's success in earning $ 10 billion a year from the wood processing industry and lessons for Cambodia. Vietnam has been very successful in exporting processed wood products. The global timber market is estimated at $ 200 billion.
