In front of the US Ambassador, the Minister of Commerce of Cambodia highlighted the improved economic and trade relations between Cambodia and the United States. The Minister claimed that although the Kovid-19 crisis affected the trade and lifestyle of countries around the world, the volume of trade between Cambodia and the United States will continue to increase in 2020.
The minister also recalled the Agreement on Trade Relations and the Protection of Intellectual Property, which the two countries signed in 1996, after which the intellectual property sector has made significant progress. Cambodia has recently joined and is studying to become a member of several other important international intellectual property treaties.
The Minister of Commerce also mentioned the Royal Government of Cambodia's efforts to renew trade facilitation, which recently launched the Business Registration Information System (CamDX) to facilitate business registration and attract. Invest more.
During the meeting, Minister Pan Sosak and the US Ambassador also discussed the possibility of further expanding trade between the two countries, drafting laws and regulations related to the digital sector.
Mr. Pan Sosak and Mr. Patrick Murphy also discussed other priority issues related to Cambodia's readiness to chair ASEAN 2022 and reaffirmed the need for closer cooperation.
It should be noted that throughout 2020, the trade volume between Cambodia and the United States reached a total of 5,509 million US dollars, an increase of 16.89 percent compared to 2019, which was more than 4,713 million US dollars.
