"The head of the working group of the Royal Government at the district level must go to train, guide and assist those who serve the people in the four roles, including: first, the commune chief / sangkat chief, second, the commune clerk / commune clerk, and third, the commune chief / police. And fourth, village chiefs in both urban and rural areas. This is the confirmation of Prince Sar Kheng.
Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng continued that to serve the people well is to provide good public services, which is in the policy of safe villages, communes, including commune chiefs / commune chiefs, commune clerks / commune clerks, police chiefs / commune police. And the village chief provides the people with the necessary services such as identity card, birth certificate, family book, residence book, marriage certificate and many other important documents.
Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng also encouraged to pay more attention to the implementation of the policy of safe villages, communes, sangkats, with relevant officials to perform their duties well and especially to disseminate this policy more widely. Also.
Please be informed that on the occasion of presiding over the official launch of the "National Action Plan on the Prevention of Violence against Women 2019-2023" on January 19, 2021, Samdech Krala Hom said that in 10 years since 2010-2020 is the result of the implementation of this policy of safe villages and communes is very successful.
According to Sar Kheng, although well implemented, there are still some issues that are still a problem and could be even bigger. Samdech Krala Hom gave the example that the drug problem is in a program of safe village and commune policy in the past, the relevant institutions have made great efforts, but due to the drug market, it is spreading and the number of arrests of criminals or exhibits. Drugs come to punish more and more, but they are not relieved.
Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng proposed to Samdech Techo Prime Minister to raise the level of the policy of safe villages and communes not to belong to the Ministry of Interior alone, but to the Royal Government, which must have many parties to help implement. Case of two former opposition members who insulted the King will be announced early next month
(Phnom Penh): The cases of former active members of the opposition, Kong Bunheang and Hang Seng, related to insulting the King will be announced in early March 2021. This is according to the results of the trial of the two accused, which took place on the afternoon of February 16, 2021, court officials told Fresh News.
"During the hearing from the beginning to the end, both defendants admitted that they had indeed acted in accordance with the allegations, so Trial Judge Kol Kampoul decided to raise the issue," the official said. "This insulting case will be announced on March 2, 2021."
Please be informed that Mr. KET Socheat, Investigating Judge of the Phnom Penh Municipal Court, on the morning of October 20, 2020, issued an order to bring the accused Kong Bun Heang and Hang Seng to Prey Sor (M1) Prison temporarily. To await the sentencing of the procedure related to insulting the King.
On the afternoon of October 19, 2020, Deputy Prosecutor Seng Heang opened an investigation and decided to charge them with insulting the King in accordance with Article 437 (duplicate) of the Penal Code. This was confirmed by Deputy Prosecutor Kuch Kimlong, spokesman for the Phnom Penh Municipal Court, adding that according to the above charges, the accused could face up to one year in prison. To 5 years and a fine of 2 million to 10 million riels.
It should be reminded that the accused Kong Bunheang, 66 years old, a former executive member of the former CNRP in Battambang province, was arrested by the specialized police force of the Ministry of Interior in cooperation with the police of Kampong Preah commune, Sangke district, Battambang province on the night of the 17th. October 2020. The accused, Hang Seng, a former executive member of the former CNRP in Battambang province, was arrested on October 18, 2020.
The arrest of the two defendants came after they insulted His Majesty King Norodom Sihamoni, King of Cambodia.
"The King can not be abused by anyone." This is according to Article 7 of the Constitution of the Kingdom of Cambodia.
