Authorities and Officials Solve Problems for Nearly 1,000 Workers at Garment Factory in Chilou Special Economic Zone, Svay Rieng City
(Svay Rieng): At least 1,000 workers at the Van Jia Hunting Co., Ltd. factory in Chilu Special Economic Zone, Svay Toeu Village, Svay Toeur Sangkat, Svay Rieng City, went on strike to demand three conditions for the factory owners as well as Specialized department authorities find a solution.
* Condition 1: Ask the company to pay the remaining annual leave to the workers at the end of the contract
* Condition 3: Ask the company to cut the end of the year for pregnant women to go for a pregnancy test one day a month.
After the strike on the morning of February 16, 2021, Svay Rieng Municipality authorities led by Mr. Sor Sodany, Deputy Mayor and Mr. Ou Sokhoeun, Director of Svay Rieng Provincial Department of Labor and Vocational Training, as well as representatives of companies, factories and workers' representatives mediated. Reconciliation to find a solution for workers with good results, workers agree to return to work as usual this afternoon.
Mr. Sor Sodany told Fresh News that this morning, both the authorities, the specialized departments and the representatives of the factory side, the representatives of the workers' side, discussed and found a solution in accordance with the policy of the Royal Government and made concessions to the workers to reach an agreement in Conditions By the first condition, the company will issue a declaration to implement the end of the year.
For the second condition: the company can not provide $ 5 health care because the health care salary is not limited in the law, on the other hand, the company also pays compensation on behalf of all workers. S) Already, so the company asked the workers to go to the hospital, which is a partner of (CP).
Condition 3: Both parties have agreed for pregnant women to go for a pregnancy test one day a month, the company will allow, keeping wages and other benefits the same, there is no end-of-year deduction. Or no wages.
He added that the situation of workers' strikes is peaceful and non-violent, and on the day of the strike on the afternoon of February 15, 2021, the company will cut the end of the year for workers at the end of the year.
According to Mr. Ou Sokhoeun, Director of the Department of Labor and Vocational Training of Svay Rieng Province, this afternoon, more than 600 workers returned to work this afternoon, while another 300 workers have not returned to work due to They went home without knowing the information that the authorities and the specialized department have reconciled, so on February 17, tomorrow, all workers will return to work as usual.
