Police Chief of Sre Thmey Commune, Kampong Chhnang Province, died in the station alone due to a physical illness
(Kampong Chhnang): There was a surprise on the morning of February 16 because the police chief of Sre Thmei commune, Rolea Bier district, Kampong Chhnang province, died in the police station alone, where the police suspected that the victim died of disease. Physical.
The above incident happened at 8:30 in the morning at the police station in Santouch village, Sre Thmei commune, Rolea Bier district, Kampong Chhnang province.
According to the police, the victim was Keo Sophang, 55, his wife Pen Sokny, 53, and their seven children living in Koul Kob village, Sre Thmei commune, Rolea Bier district, Kampong Chhnang province. .
Prior to the incident, at around 1 am on February 16, the victim was talking to the district police inspector in the room alone with the key locked inside. In the morning, a police officer Woke up the postmaster to go to a meeting at the police station in Rolear Bier district, but did not see a response, he looked outside the room and saw the victim lying naked on the bag.
With suspicion, he informed the commune chief and Sre Thmei commune councilor and the deputy police chief to help check because the victim closed the door and put the key from inside and also reported to the police inspector of Rolea Bier district about the situation. This is also an immediate surprise.
Later, a window was opened to find out that the postmaster had been lying on his back for an unknown period of time. Separately, according to the autopsy from the competent experts and doctors and judges of Kampong Chhnang Provincial Court, it was concluded that the victim may have died between 2 and 3 o'clock in the morning, may have been caused by high blood pressure and had suffered a stroke. The victim had high blood pressure and was taking medication regularly.
After the examination, the bodies of the victims were handed over to their families by the provincial police commissioner's car to their homes to prepare for the traditional ceremony.
