(Kratie): Mr. Neth Pheaktra, Secretary of State and Spokesperson of the Ministry of Environment, presented three crimes that continue to harass natural resources: illegal encroachment on forest land, illegal logging and poaching. Minor crimes continue to occur in protected areas, while major crimes are completely suppressed.
Mr. Neth Pheaktra's presentation on the crime of destroying natural resources in such a small format was made during an interview with national and international journalists on the occasion of leading more than 300 youths to a two-day camp. From 14 to 15 February 2021 at the Customs Headquarters in Prey Lang Wildlife Sanctuary, Kratie Province.
The spokesman for the Ministry of Environment stated: "This situation arises: First, the main reasons related to the livelihood of the people around the natural resource protection area, Second: Some traders have incited people. "People living around the natural resource area cut down trees to sell to themselves, and thirdly, it is related to local demand, which means that people want furniture made of luxury wood and natural wood."
Meanwhile, a senior official of the Ministry of Environment stated that to address this challenge, the Ministry of Environment, provincial authorities and partner organizations have created new businesses, strengthening the role of communities around natural resource protection areas for them to understand. From the effects of deforestation and wildlife hunting.
Mr. Neth Pheaktra continued that for traders to provide money to people to cut the natural forest is due to the demand in the local market, while the export of timber is not there, so the demand for natural wood in the country. Has become a challenge that puts pressure on natural resources.
(Preah Sihanouk): Three deputies of the Ninth Committee of the National Assembly, including Mr. Kep Chuktema, Mr. Tat Vantha and Mr. Nong Veasna with a delegation from the Ministry of Mines and Energy, a representative of the Ministry of Economy and Finance and a representative of the Preah Sihanouk Provincial Administration traveled. Visit to find out about oil pump activities in Block A off the coast of Cambodia.
Mr. Veasna said they were the first lawmakers to reach the Cambodian oil rig. He is very happy.
Please be informed that Samdech Techo Hun Sen on December 29, 2020 delivered a happy news and a source of pride for the people of Cambodia, the first drop of Cambodia's oil has been successfully pumped. The achievement of peace born of win-win politics has brought a new achievement, the first drop of oil in the history of Cambodia.
The Prime Minister of the Royal Government of Cambodia has made it clear that the first drop of oil in the history of Cambodia is a blessing for the people and the nation, not a curse, as some unscrupulous people claim. Revenues from the sale of Cambodia's oil will be used for two priority sectors: education and health.
On February 1, 2021, Samdech Techo Hun Sen confirmed that the pumping of oil from Block A in the Apsara area was going smoothly, leading to the pumping of oil from the second well, while the other three wells will continue to operate.
The five oil wells in the Apsara region are expected to be operational in 2021 and are estimated to receive more than 7,000 barrels a day, a small amount. Although this amount is small, Samdech Techo said it was a good start to the oil and gas industry in Cambodia.
According to estimates, if the price of oil is $ 55 per barrel, oil revenue per year is about $ 30 million.
Cambodia divides oil exploration blocks into 25 offshore and inland areas. In that, 6 sea blocks, 19 land blocks and 4 areas in the sea claim to overlap between Cambodia and Thailand.
