(Phnom Penh): Mr. Chea Chanto, Governor of the National Bank of Cambodia, thanked the International Monetary Fund (IMF) for its support and technical assistance to develop the banking sector.
Please be informed that this Staff Visit is part of the IMF's role in annual consultations with ministries, government agencies, international institutions and the private sector to gather relevant data and information for monitoring and evaluation of the situation. Macroeconomic and financial member countries for Article 4 consultative mission scheduled for November 2021.
The Governor thanked the International Monetary Fund for supporting the Royal Government of Cambodia and the National Bank of Cambodia, as well as providing the necessary technical assistance to develop the banking sector.
The Governor welcomed the consultative meeting of the International Monetary Fund, which is important in assessing the economic situation in Cambodia during the time when Cambodia was affected by the 19 diseases that affect the economy.
Mr. Chea Chanto informed about the Royal Government's strict measures to effectively prevent and prevent the spread of Kovid 19 in Cambodia and the introduction of a series of measures to support the business activities and the affected poor people. . At the same time, the National Bank of Cambodia has also implemented monetary policy, revised and relaxed some regulations to increase liquidity in the banking system to support economic activity.
In addition, the National Bank of Cambodia has allowed credit restructuring, which has helped address the plight of clients facing declining revenues.
He said that the International Monetary Fund (IMF) highly appreciates the policies of the Royal Government and the National Bank of Cambodia, which have made significant contributions to macroeconomic stability, confidence in the Cambodian economy and support in the face of crisis and economic assistance. The poor.
After a three-week discussion, the mission will gather additional data and information to provide recommendations for boosting economic activity and growth, especially after the end of the Kovid-19 crisis.
