Cambodia Takes More Strict Measures as Three New Kovid 19 Discovery Cases Discovered
The move comes after the Ministry of Health observed that Cambodians seem to be unaware of the enormous risk of transmission of the KV-19 virus, especially in the context of the devastating mutations of the deadly virus. With large gatherings at parties, weddings, festivals, and trips to hometowns or resorts without following the frequent guidelines of the Ministry of Health.
In order to prevent the transmission of Kovid 19 more effectively, the Ministry of Health urges all citizens to remember and participate in the implementation of simple self-protection measures and to continue to be vigilant against Kovid-19 infection by implementing Only the "three do's and don'ts of protection" measures are as follows:
* Must implement three preventive measures on a regular basis:
* Must implement 3 measures:
1: To increase the attention and deploy competent forces to guard and strictly monitor the implementation of 14 days of measures for all travelers from abroad at the entrance to Cambodia. Borders across the country (air, land and sea).
2. All competent authorities who are responsible for standing at the entrance to Cambodia must carry out strict and clear control of passengers entering Cambodia, without allowing "brokers" to take passengers to escape from any entrance. One without doing that.
3: There must be regular education by placing a microphone on the need for 14 days for travelers to enter Cambodia and disseminate the penalties stated in Sub-Decree No. 129, dated 17 September. 2015, which will be implemented when any person does not follow the health measures at this entrance.
4: To find this "broker" if there is the disappearance of any passenger or group of passengers into the country of passengers who have not been vaccinated for 14 days in the province or district where the entrance Come to Cambodia to take legal action.
6: To monitor the health of passengers who have been sedated by the medical team of the Capital-Provincial Health Department in accordance with the technical procedures and accurate records.
9: Citizens and authorities of Sangkat, Commune, and Village, please report to the relevant authorities to prevent the transmission of Kovid-19 virus to individuals to their families and to prevent transmission in their communities.
