Ministry of Environment and Hundreds of Youth Planting Trees at Prey Lang Wildlife Sanctuary Demonstrate Commitment to Natural Resources Conservation
This is the third camp program under the theme "We love Prey Lang" in 2021, organized by the Ministry of Environment with the participation of stakeholders.
Mr. Neth Pheaktra stated that the annual February 14 tent camp program was held for the purpose
First, show love for natural resources, biodiversity and the environment at Prey Lang Wildlife Sanctuary, as well as other protected areas in Cambodia.
Second: Disseminate understanding and share experiences in natural resource management
Third: Inspire and inspire people, especially young people to love and participate in the conservation of natural resources.
Fourth, to increase the communication of people from all walks of life to jointly protect and conserve natural resources, biodiversity and the environment.
The Secretary of State of the Ministry of Environment emphasized that through this program, together with the dissemination of other messages related to natural resources, the Ministry of Environment believes that it will participate in cultivating the spirit of Cambodians to love natural resources and participate more actively to conserve forests and wildlife.
Mr. Neth Pheaktra said that every citizen can participate in protecting the environment and natural resources anytime and anywhere, sometimes just saving water, saving electricity, not eating wild meat, planting trees. These are all respect and love for natural resources.
He added that the Royal Government of Cambodia has taken great care and commitment to protect these protected areas until it has received international praise for the establishment of conservation areas and the sale of carbon credits in the voluntary market.
It should be noted that the Ministry of Environment organized a two-day camp program under the theme "We love Prey Lang" in the Prey Lang Wildlife Sanctuary in Kratie province, with more than 300 participants from all walks of life, including officials. Officials from the Ministry of Environment and other ministries, state institutions, provincial authorities, civil society organizations, community development partners, community networks, monks, youth, community members and journalists.
Please note that "Prey Lang" Wildlife Sanctuary was established by the Royal Government in 2016 and is under the conservation management of the Ministry of Environment. Prey Lang covers a total area of more than 430,000 hectares and covers four provinces: Stung Treng, Preah Vihear, Kampong Thom and Kratie.
In 2019, the Ministry of Environment announced the recognition of 19 protected areas that have the legal right to participate in activities to protect and conserve natural resources in important wildlife sanctuaries.
China continues to crack down on counterfeit vaccine production and distribution
BEIJING (Reuters) - China is cracking down on the production and distribution of counterfeit COVID-19 vaccine as dozens of suspects have been arrested, police said on Monday. . This is according to the release by CNA on Monday evening, February 15, 2021.
As of Wednesday last week, Chinese police had arrested 70 suspects, 21 of whom were involved in the production and distribution of counterfeit vaccines, most of them in the early stages of vaccine distribution. .
One of the suspects arrested earned about 18 million yuan ($ 2.8 million) from distributing counterfeit vaccines. In other cases, counterfeit vaccines are sold at high prices, including for export.
Chinese investigators have urged local agencies to work with police to step up their efforts to prevent such incidents.
