(Phnom Penh): The General Department of Taxation has set out 14 main policy and administrative measures to ensure the effective implementation of the management of tax collection in accordance with the financial law plan for 9,084.42 management. Billion riel (about 2,243.07 million US dollars) for 2021.
This measure was introduced in the meeting to summarize the results of tax revenue collection in January 2021 and the direction for further implementation of the General Department of Taxation under the chairmanship of Mr. Kong Vibol, Minister Delegate to the Prime Minister and the Royal Government Delegate in charge of the Director General of General Department of Taxation on February 15, 2021. This is according to a press release obtained by Fresh News today.
Mr. Kong Vibol said that for 2021, to ensure the effective implementation of the management of tax revenue collection in accordance with the financial law plan for the management of 9,084.42 billion Riels (approximately 2,243.07 million General Department of Taxation will continue to strengthen the implementation of fiscal policy and administrative measures, including the following key measures:
* Second: Disseminate and prepare to effectively implement the rules and procedures governing the use of locally produced beer and / or non-alcoholic beverages and strengthen the management of all types of tax collection in accordance with the declaration. No. 010 MEF.Prak dated 12 January 2021 on the obligation to install beer and non-alcoholic beverages of local production enterprises.
* Fourth: Continue to promote and mainstream the culture of paying taxes, strengthen the dissemination and implementation of new tax-related regulations to taxpayers and the public to explain and solve the difficulties and questions of the people, especially in preparation for the workshop. To taxpayers on "Update on the income tax return form for 2020".
* Fifth: Strengthen the implementation of tax debt collection and measures to tighten tax debt, especially large tax debt, potentially identified as priority debt and enterprises in areas not affected by the Kovid Outbreak 19.
* Sixth, continue and strengthen cooperation with all relevant ministries and institutions in sharing data and implementing necessary measures to strengthen the implementation of tax revenue management.
* 7th: Continue to strengthen the inspection of the declaration of tax on means of transportation and all types of vehicles in 2020, which started on February 1, 2021.
* 9th: Continue to strengthen the management of the enterprise, request for temporary suspension or request for reopening
* 11th: Continue to strengthen and promote real estate survey and business registration in Phnom Penh and other provinces to register and update in order to strengthen taxpayer services.
* Twelfth: Continue the work of human resource reform by promoting and striving to strengthen the implementation of labor laws and regulations, and be gentle but firm, based on the legal aspects of providing services to taxpayers and revenue collection management.
* 13th: Continue to strengthen the effective implementation of the Royal Government's emergency intervention measures to support tourism, aviation, agriculture and animal husbandry, and the general entertainment sector, and intervention measures to promote economic growth.
* 14th: Continue to implement the necessary measures as set out in the circular on the implementation of the Law on Finance 2021 and continue to implement carefully the revenue collection strategy 2019-2023.
