(Phnom Penh): The Ministry of Health and the Ministry of Justice will meet on the morning of February 16, 2021 to discuss, review and revise the sub-decree on health rules to prevent and respond to the international spread of diseases at the entrance.
According to Kim Santepheap, Secretary of State and spokesman for the Ministry of Justice, the review and revision of this sub-decree is in response to the actual situation of the spread of Kovid-19 virus in Cambodia.
The meeting to review and revise the above sub-decree took place after the instruction of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the Prime Minister of Cambodia, in order to increase the level of punishment or punishment for those who evade the sub-decree while the sub-decree Older, the level of penalties and fines is small.
On 15 February 2021, Samdech Techo Hun Sen yesterday requested for a review and revision of Article 8 of Chapter 5 of the "Sub-Decree on Health Rules to Prevent and Respond to the International Outbreak of Diseases in Cambodia". "Through the entrance."
Samdech Techo stated that the level of penalties and penalties stated in Article 8 is still small, which can make those who have resources not afraid and still violate this sub-decree.
In this article, it is stated that receiving this transitional penalty does not exempt the person who commits the crime from the criminal liability stipulated in the law and the criminal provisions in force. Anyone who falsifies health-related documents in order to evade the implementation of the Tactical measures shall be punished in accordance with the criminal law in force.
