International Condom Day 2021 is organized under the theme "Always up to date" with condoms!
AHF, in partnership with governments and civil society organizations around the world, has organized events, including live events and social events, with safety gaps to commemorate those who have died of HIV / AIDS and to raise public awareness. About the importance of using condoms properly to prevent AIDS and other prophylaxis.
The AIDS Health Care Foundation has been celebrating International Condom Day since 2008 and has been innovative in promoting condoms and their use because condoms are primarily important for protecting themselves from HIV infection and preventing pregnancy. Unplanned pregnancy.
This International Day is celebrated in conjunction with Valentine's Day every year. AHF teams based in various countries around the world are organizing various entertainment and educational events on social media and directly under the theme "Always up to date" for Condom Day 2021!
The AIDS Health Care Foundation is still working to ensure that all people receive free and on-demand condoms, and for International Condom Day, focus on "always up to date" for Condom Day 2021! In the 45 countries where the AIDS Health Care Foundation (AHF) operates, it organizes the nearest entertainment event and continues to promote the importance of condoms available to everyone.
International Condom Day provides a forum to call on governments and public health institutions to ensure that people have the tools to protect themselves and their loved ones, especially when new HIV infections occur. 1.7 million people every year. It's commonplace when there are ways to distribute condoms to people around the world to protect them from preventable diseases.
(Phnom Penh): The Ministry of Labor and Vocational Training on February 15, 2021 issued a notice on fines on Cambodian workers who evade proper health measures.
This announcement is made in accordance with the recommendation of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia and Sub-Decree No. 129 dated 15 September 2015 on Health Measures to Prevent and Respond to the International Outbreak of Diseases in Cambodia. Entrance.
According to the announcement of the Ministry of Labor, which was received by Fresh News, in order to maintain public safety and prevent the spread of Kovid-19 disease into the community, especially for the health of workers and their families, the Ministry of Labor requires both workers All apply as follows:
1: Do not smuggle illegally into Cambodia, which can pose a high risk to personal life and the transmission of infectious diseases into Cambodia.
2: In the case of entering Cambodia, it is necessary to properly perform the rituals according to the health measures, without having to avoid it. Failure to do so properly will result in a fine of 1,000,000 Riels or more and criminal penalties as stipulated in the applicable laws and regulations.
3. Cooperate in providing information to embassies or relevant authorities that are close to the brokers who promise to bring migrant workers into and out of Cambodia illegally.
In the letter, the Ministry of Health recalled some of the sanctions that will be imposed on those who evade the practice under Article 8 of Chapter 5.
In this article, it is stated that receiving this transitional penalty does not exempt the person who commits the crime from the criminal liability stipulated in the law and the criminal provisions in force. Anyone who falsifies health-related documents for the purpose of evading compulsory measures shall be punished in accordance with the criminal law in force.
In this letter, the Ministry of Health also reminded that in case the passenger or operator of the transport vehicle refuses to comply with the provisions of the above paragraph, the customs officer must cooperate with the relevant authorities to deny entry and exit to Cambodia.
It should be noted that in connection with the evasion, this morning, Samdech Techo Hun Sen also issued an order via voicemail to strictly enforce the implementation of legal measures under this sub-decree. Samdech Techo Hun Sen also recommended that the fine be revised because it is currently low. Kamrieng District Police Inspector Suspended on Suspicion of Release of Brokers Who Illegally Bring Workers to Thailand
