China no longer allows BBC news coverage in the country
BEIJING (Reuters) - China's media censorship authority on Thursday ruled that the UK's BBC World News could no longer operate in China on the grounds that it violated Chinese media coverage. . This was released by CNA on Friday, February 12, 2021.
China's state-run TV and Radio Administration says BBC World News' coverage of China has been found to be in serious violation of China's broadcasting principles, including requiring media outlets to be honest and transparent. Etc. and does not affect China's national interests. Therefore, the BBC is no longer allowed to continue its coverage in China.
The decision comes just days after British authorities revoked the CGTN Chinese media license on the grounds that CGTN had violated British law.
