(Phnom Penh): The Royal Academy of Cambodia and the Cambodian Chamber of Commerce and Industry have organized a discussion on "Inter-Institutional Cooperation" on February 11, 2021 at the Royal Academy of Cambodia.
The discussion was chaired by Mr. Son Kunthor, Senior Minister, Minister Delegate to the Prime Minister in charge of Small and Medium Enterprises and Microfinance Institutions and President of the Cambodian Chamber of Commerce and Industry, and Dr. Sok Touch, President of the Royal Academy of Cambodia at the Royal Academy of Cambodia.
The purpose of this discussion is to share information between the work of the Cambodian Chamber of Commerce and Micro-Enterprises and the work of the Royal Academy of Cambodia to seek cooperation between the two institutions to help entrepreneurs and informal micro-enterprises that are facing problems. In the Kovid stage and in the future.
The discussion was completed as follows:
1: After understanding the history, roles, tasks, structure and vision of the two institutions, the discussion found that the two institutions can cooperate to study and understand the challenges that the people are facing and contribute to the recommendation to the Royal Government.
2. Establish a working group to prepare a draft memorandum of understanding between the two institutions, which may be signed at an appropriate time.
3. Organize technical working groups on some priority areas for future cooperation.
