(Phnom Penh): Recently, the Secretariat of the National Committee of Experts of the Ministry of Tourism won the Innovation Project Competition on the Development of a Digital Expert Assessment Program in Accordance with ASEAN Standards Digital from the Innovation Project Competition. One in Cambodia under the auspices of the United Nations in Cambodia and the Ministry of Labor and Vocational Training.
The first skills competition in Cambodia aims to promote the development and integration of digital technology in skills training. The Ministry of Tourism has won the second prize for the ASEAN Pre-Education Assessment (RPL) Digital Nursery Project.
Since the outbreak of Kovid 19, the Ministry of Tourism has launched an online training program for affected workers and is preparing a digital nursery for skills training.
Winning shows that the design initiative is in line with the digital age, both in form and content. In addition, the Ministry of Tourism will receive digital technical assistance from a team of UN experts.
A digital nursery training and capacity assessment through ASEAN mechanisms will also be launched to ASEAN member countries, which can be officially announced on the occasion of ASEAN Tourism Day 2022 in Cambodia, which is the host country.
