European Chamber of Commerce launches 2021 "Social Responsibility" Awards
As the nation's leading competition, the European Chamber of Commerce's CSR competition is well-known, which includes well-known brands and large companies recognized across the country, as well as diversified businesses. Too many types.
What is new and interesting development for this year is that the competition program is open to all Cambodian and foreign businesses that meet the specific conditions of the program (conditions include businesses that are present in Cambodia and are committed). Sharply on social responsibility programs).
While the promotion of social responsibility is usually considered only for large enterprises, the growth of small and medium enterprises has helped small companies increase their commitment to positive change for society and the environment.
That is why the European Chamber of Commerce encourages small and medium enterprises to participate in this program, as they will compete in the category for small and medium enterprises only, which is different from the competition for large enterprises.
Through this initiative, the European Chamber of Commerce is helping to inspire the next generation of innovators by building relationships with current industry leaders.
While the competition program has a total of 14 prizes on two main categories, the company category is divided into 4 sub-chapters and 12 prizes. And the new category competition for youth category will have 1 chapter with 2 prizes.
Companies registered in Cambodia, youth associations or individuals under the age of 25 and present in Cambodia who wish to be recognized for work, social responsibility or community involvement are welcome to apply. Words before March 31, 2021.
The program provides a unique opportunity for the private sector in Cambodia to demonstrate their efforts and social responsibility solutions to be part of a platform that encourages innovation and helps businesses build resilience and overcome barriers. .
The competition is open to businesses in Cambodia and companies that are committed to social responsibility and are not required to register through the European Chamber of Commerce (EuroCham).
The event will be presided over by Mr. Sok Chenda Sophea, Minister Delegate to the Prime Minister and Secretary-General of the Council for the Development of Cambodia, and Ms. Carmen Moreno, Ambassador of the European Union to Cambodia.
Other jurisdictions include senior experts and representatives from international organizations, the Board and the Green Business Committee of the European Chamber of Commerce, experts from education and the private sector.
Registration for the competition will start on March 1, 2021 and will end on March 31, 2021. In addition to seeking candidates, the European Chamber of Commerce in Cambodia is also looking for partners, scorers and technical assistants in various fields.
