In addition, Senior Minister Chhay Thorn stated that the number of households engaged in agriculture (engaged in agriculture) is more than 1.7 million households, of which more than 61% are engaged in farming for household use and farming for sale. The market is about 39%. 98% of agricultural households own agricultural land, while only 19% of registered households own agricultural land.
According to Dr. Kith Setha, Dr. Chhay Thorn, 88% of the households are engaged in crop production, more than 75% of the households are engaged in livestock and / or poultry, more than 15% are engaged in aquaculture and / or fishing activities, and more than 15% are engaged in agriculture. Forest activities (non-timber forest products) account for 11% of total agricultural households.
Senior Minister Chhay Thorn said that the average size of a family engaged in agriculture is 4 people. 51% of female households are engaged in agricultural work and 49% of men are male. Most of the family members involved in agriculture are in the 25-44 age group. For children under the age of 15, they are involved in family work and farming.
