(Phnom Penh): In the closing ceremony of the meeting to summarize the results of the implementation of the roles and responsibilities of the Gendarmerie Reform in 2020 and the direction of the action plan for 2021 on the afternoon of February 9, 2021. Samdech Pich Sena Tea Banh, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of National Defense, gave some recommendations to the Gendarmerie to achieve more new achievements for 2021.
The 10 recommendations of Samdech Pich Sena Tea Banh include the following:
Tasks ahead:
* First, to effectively implement the message of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, on February 4, 2021, on the prevention of the import of Kovid-19 disease from Vietnam and from neighboring countries into the community of such countries. This unit under the Border Army and the Gendarmerie must cooperate with the provincial administration, ministries, institutions and relevant authorities to prevent in time.
Reform and implementation of roles and responsibilities:
* First: Experience the remaining work challenges in 2020 as an opportunity to improve the shortcomings, as well as strengthen effective leadership. Care must be taken to implement the policies and strategic measures of the Royal Government, which have set out to respect and strictly implement the high recommendations of Samdech Techo Hun Sen in order to strengthen security, safety, order and social order.
In the current situation, we must promote the spirit of national unity in order to overcome all the difficulties caused by Kovid-19 and other natural disasters in order to achieve our goals, serve our country and our people successfully.
* Third: Continue to pay attention to education, training and training of all units in the Royal Gendarmerie to increase capacity, quality and efficiency, because human resources are the most important element in the development of the unit, so we need to prepare development programs. Capacity for officers and deputies with new knowledge and skills related to roles, duties and reforms in line with the defense sector.
* Fifth: Strengthen the maintenance of weapons to ensure safety in accordance with technical standards and to enhance the capacity of officers, deputies and soldiers of the Royal Gendarmerie to take ownership of the use and control of weapons. Equipment, weapons and ammunition to prevent fire, damage, loss, maintain good quality, considered as a valuable asset of our nation and people.
