Therefore, as the Chinese New Year approaches, we recall the warm wishes of Xi Jinping over the years through the following pictures: From Banana Eggs 4 cultivars expand cultivation to 13 hectares in more than 3 years to help a farmer in Pailin province have a better life
(Pailin): Until the beginning of February 2021, a farmer named Hem Netra, alias Pet, 58 years old, living in Thnal Toteung village, O'Andong commune, Sala Krao district, Pailin province, has been planting bananas for 13 hectares since 2018. To date, he has benefited by cutting sales once a week and earning a living.
He added that the planting of banana eggs is asking for seeds from others, initially only 4 clumps. Later, it grows until it can grow many clumps at once.
The farmer added that he sells 1 kg of bananas for 3,000 to 3,500 riel, but during the festive season, such as Chinese New Year, his sales increase slightly by 1 kg. From 4,000 Riel to 4,500 Riel. On the other hand, the total harvest of bananas and eggs per month can be cut to sell about 8 to 9 tons, he transported himself to sell at the stalls rented in Pom Puy market, Battambang province.
As for selling bananas in Pailin province, Mr. Hem Netra stated that there is not much market because people buy only 200 to 300 kilograms per month. Therefore, because of its large number of bananas, it is willing to cut and transport it to sell in Battambang province.
He added that not only that, his bananas were also Thai people came to buy packaging to resell in China, when stuck in the crisis Kovid 19 was suspended, only the Cambodian market. For his bananas, there are bags packed from the young bananas so that the color is clear and easy to sell.
He added that the provincial Department of Agriculture also provides training to farmers to understand how to maintain and bring companies from outside to contact to buy bananas to sell in Thailand. In fact, in the farm of a farmer named Him Netra, who produced banana eggs, he was able to make a significant profit, as he could produce and sell in Pailin province and sell as far as Battambang province.
The Provincial Department of Agriculture also brought some pesticides for the plantation owners to spray on the banana plantations to prevent and control pests from eating bananas, and the purpose of the Department of Agriculture is to expand the plantation owners and the people. Growing more bananas as standard to export to foreign markets as well. This is according to Mr. Say Sophat.
