Ministry of Environment Spokesperson: Civil society groups that boast of their love for justice should acknowledge the truth and not protect lawless people
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Neth Pheaktra, Secretary of State and Spokesman of the Ministry of Environment, on February 9, 2021, said that some civil society groups that claim to be champions of justice and respect for human rights should learn to recognize Some facts, and do not try to protect the lawless group.
A senior Ministry of Environment official's reaction came after a number of associations and civil society groups issued a joint statement calling on the Ministry of Environment to stop arresting and persecuting forest activists.
Mr. Neth Pheaktra said: "Civil society organizations that boast of loving justice, respecting human rights should learn to recognize the truth and not be a human rights and love of natural resources, and do not try to protect people. "Who do not respect the law and do not carry out work embedded in any corrupt agenda and should be honest in cooperation with the competent ministry."
The senior official confirmed that according to the confession of a group of people claiming to be environmental activists in front of the authorities in Kratie province that they were aware that sneaking in and operating in the protected area without permission is It is illegal to sneak into Prey Lang, they act and take pictures to show their donors and to raise funds only.
Mr. Neth Pheaktra added that the Ministry of Environment still emphasizes the implementation of the law without exception to any perpetrators in its jurisdiction to effectively protect and conserve existing natural resources.
At the same time, the Secretary of State called on and encouraged some donors to provide support to associations and non-governmental organizations that are properly registered and respect the law to promote law enforcement and encourage respective associations and non-governmental organizations. The law is fair and honest in cooperating for the cause of the environment and natural resources.
He added that the Ministry of Environment always welcomes the participation of associations and non-governmental organizations in the protection and conservation of natural resources, but must enter through the legal channels in force, not stealing activities from the law. People who take refuge under the label of environmentalists and always insult the national law should learn to respect the law because Cambodia is the rule of law and do not consider themselves an outlaw group.
(Phnom Penh): The Phnom Penh Municipal Police is looking for the owner of the Facebook account named "Ly Sororn" to comment on the posting of completely false information, which confuses the people and the general public by taking the actions of officials. The law on reversing motorcyclists is ridiculous.
According to the official Facebook page of the Phnom Penh Municipal Police, posted on the afternoon of February 9, 2021, "The explanation of the Information and Quick Reaction Team of the Phnom Penh Municipal Police regarding the Facebook account of Ly Sororn Who published completely untrue information that confused the people and the general public
In fact, it is the case of the law enforcement of the law against the motorcyclists in the opposite direction, where the police office always organizes order on Street 336 for the unruly traders who cause congestion and arrests the motorcyclists riding in the opposite direction to send them for safekeeping. Keep it at the public order office and work according to the law. Instead, the owner of the Facebook account took the actions of law enforcement officials as a joke.
At this time, the team of information and quick reaction has cooperated with the competent authorities to search for the owner of the Facebook account that leaked this false information to come in and explain and apologize for posting this false information.
