Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng stated: "Local officials must disseminate the policy of safe village-commune to the people and civil servants at the lower level and call for support and implementation of the village-commune policy. "It is safe to do that. I dare guarantee that it is not wrong because our people want what we want to do."
Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng gave the example: "People shout that there are drugs, there are thieves, there are gambling. We must be considered as a mirror, reflecting the political theory that the masses and the people are a mirror." Therefore, the demands and requests of the people must be considered as a mirror and we reflect to serve them.
Samdech also instructed the local working group, the authorities and some other stakeholders to immediately address the requests of the people, because they are a mirror that reflects the aspects of their lives.
At the same time, Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng also confirmed that whatever you do, as long as you follow the requests of the people, you will be successful. Samdech Krala Hom continued that if done against the will of the people will not be successful, no matter how strong. The Royal Government will hold the 9th Sea Festival in Sihanoukville at the end of 2021 after one year
(Preah Sihanouk): The Royal Government of Cambodia has authorized the Ministry of Tourism and relevant ministries and institutions to cooperate with the Preah Sihanouk Provincial Administration to re-organize the 9th Sea Festival (Round 3) at the end of 2021 after one year. In 2020, due to the severe impact of the Kovid-19 crisis, as this year's Sea Festival, the leaders set a goal to be more special than in previous years.
In order to better prepare for this big annual tourism event, Mr. Thong Khon, Minister of Tourism, together with Mr. Kouch Chamroeun, Governor of Preah Sihanouk Province, chaired a special meeting at Preah Sihanouk Provincial Administration on the morning of 9 February. 2021 In order to discuss with ministries, institutions, departments, specialized units to prepare some work gradually.
On that occasion, Minister Thong Khon instructed the working group to start establishing an inter-ministerial working group to work on each arrow in order to organize the whole festival smoothly and successfully. There will be performances, arts, sports events, peacekeeping, landscaping in public places, beaches and other important locations. As for the arrangement of the food street, it was also supported by Minister Thong Khon.
He encouraged the bringing of agricultural products, handicrafts and local commercial products to the festival as much as possible. In addition, to promote tourism products, tourism potential, which is available in resorts, community tourism, potential eco-tourism sites, coastal areas, islands and the sea to be widely disseminated during the festival.
Minister Thong Khon also encouraged the participation of performing arts, commercial products and the participation of neighboring countries and local foreign tourists (domestic tourists).
Minister Thong Khon stated that although the Royal Government is organizing the ninth round of the 9th Sea Festival, the organizing committee must strictly adhere to the Ministry of Tourism's tourism safety rules and the Ministry of Health's hygiene rules. For example, the three-pronged and three-pronged recommendations of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the Prime Minister, must be strictly implemented together.
Mr. Kouch Chamroeun Provincial Governor has committed to work with the Ministry of Tourism and relevant ministries and institutions by assigning professional officers in the provincial administration, relevant departments and units to carry out their respective functions, including site preparation, ceremonies, preparation, problem prevention. Security, leaders, program organizers, citizens and tourists, decorating, improving the beauty of the city on public roads and so on.
Mr. Kouch Chamroeun suggested writing a story or performing arts at this tourism event, which describes the history of Sihanoukville, or the old name of Kampong Som, as a cultural treasure of the province as well as for the nation.
For the location of major festivals and other programs, the team will continue to discuss more clearly.
On that occasion, Mr. Thong Khon and Mr. Kouch Chamroeun also continued to lead the discussion to prepare for the official opening ceremony of 37 roads in Sihanoukville, which will be held under the presidency of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister on April 9. The year 2021 is coming. In addition, there is also a meeting to prepare for the event of Valentine's Day in Sihanoukville on February 14, 2021.
(Kampong Chhnang): Kampong Leng district, Kampong Chhnang province, is one of the eight districts with the most historical stories and ancient temples in the eight districts in the province adjacent to the Tonle Sap Lake. Last week, Fresh News agency visited two of the temples in Kampong Leng district, Kampong Chhnang province, Prasat Pros and Prasat Srey.
Prasat Pros, now known as Prasat Sakl, is located in Kang Kep village, Chronok commune, Kampong Leng district, built on a hill in the middle of a rice field, more than 30 kilometers from Kampong Leng district town. This temple has a real name, Prasat Pros, but later the locals called it Prasat Sakol according to legend.
According to legend, the construction of these two temples was originally a bet between a man and a woman. If the man wins, the woman must go to the man, but if the woman wins, the man must go to the woman. At that time, the men built a temple located at the top of the temple, while the women built a temple in Wat Prasat in Da commune, Kampong Leng district today.
Please be informed that at that time, the woman used her wisdom by raising the lantern and posted it, while the man saw the lantern and thought that the morning star was rising, so they stopped building the temple. The women continued to build until the morning was finished before the men and the men won.
Therefore, it is only then that the Khmer tradition of men marrying women, and from that time on, some of the remaining temples have become known as Prasat Sakl, or means temples that have not been completed. As for Prasat Srey, it is currently located in Wat Prasat, Khum Da, Kampong Leng District, about 3 kilometers away from Prasat Pros, a temple that has already been completed.
Prasat Pros or Prasat Sakol and Prasat Srey above were built between the 8th and 9th centuries, both of which were built in the style of Kampong Preah. From the past to the present, these two temples have not been visited by many visitors, and from time to time foreign visitors have come to study the history of these temples.
Mr. Sok Thuok, Director of Kampong Chhnang Provincial Department of Culture and Fine Arts, told Fresh News this morning, February 9, 2021, that the two temples were built between the 8th and 9th centuries in the style of Kampong Preah temple at that time. There is also a queen named Chey Devi. Both temples are located in a good environment and have roads for visitors to visit the temple easily.
