Ministry of Education Introduces 6 Measures to Prevent Irregular Valentine's Day Activities in Public and Private Schools
(Phnom Penh): In order to continue to strengthen the implementation of internal regulations for all public educational institutions and to participate in preventing the spread of Kovid-19 disease, the Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports has introduced 6 guidelines to prevent irregular activities on Valentine's Day. (February 14) In public and private educational institutions.
* First: To disseminate to students by all means through meetings when saluting the flag, so as not to misunderstand the meaning of Valentine's Day.
* Second: Strictly enforce discipline, especially on moral management, by monitoring the presence of students consistently.
* Third: To promote the process of children's councils, youth councils in schools through "peer education" activities.
* Fourth: Educate students about the importance of safety measures to study health to prevent the spread of Kovid 19.
* Fifth, to have close contact with parents, guardians and the community to provide and receive information related to irregular activities committed by students in order to cooperate in preventing and educating and improving in a timely manner.
* Sixth: To continue to strengthen the implementation of Prakas No. 1258 IEC Proclamation dated March 27, 2009 on Internal Rules for Primary Institutions and Prakas No. 2786 IEC Prok dated October 22, 2009 on Internal Regulations For public secondary education institutions.
