Please read the press release of the Ministry of Health as follows: CRC Svay Rieng branch educates citizens, students and traders to understand traffic laws.
(Svay Rieng): Ms. Duong Vanna, Honorary President of the Cambodian Red Cross Branch in Svay Rieng Province, said that traffic accidents have caused serious difficulties to the society, destroying both property and lives and leaving victims, the disabled, orphans and women. Widow of a poor family.
Ms. Duong Vanna said this on the morning of February 9, 2021, while educating people, students, business people to understand the road traffic law to wear a helmet properly when driving. Tolerate not driving under the influence of alcohol and speeding to reduce the rate of disability, death and serious injuries due to traffic accidents.
This visit was attended by Mr. Men Vibol, Chairman of the Branch Committee, and Ms. Hao Chan Serey Tepi, Chairman of the Branch Committee, and Mr. Phirun, Vice Chairman of the Branch Committee, as well as members of the Branch Committee, Branch Executive Team, Advisors and CRC Youth Volunteers. The Red Cross cooperates with the provincial Department of Public Works and Transport and a total of 80 road traffic police.
She added that people must respect traffic laws, do not drive too fast and meet the conditions of their vehicles adequately, such as rear view mirrors, headlights, turn signals and so on.
She added that traffic accidents are becoming the deadliest on public roads and seriously affecting public health in Cambodia, with many dead and thousands injured. Cambodia loses hundreds of millions of dollars.
Seeing the situation of traffic accidents from year to year, the provincial branch of the Cambodian Red Cross has encouraged volunteers and youth of the Cambodian Red Cross to cooperate with road traffic officials at the target points to disseminate the results. Affected by traffic accidents and advise all drivers to wear helmets, seat belts and driving under the influence of alcohol.
Please note that in this campaign, relevant documents and leaflets related to the law on road safety are distributed, and there is a question and answer program on the law on road safety and road safety. From the branch team and the Department of Public Works and Transport.
At the same time, the working group also disseminated the message of the Ministry of Health regarding measures to prevent Kovid-19 to the general public who are traveling on public roads at the Suon Tady traffic light at the roundabout in front of Svay Rieng City Hall. And at the corner of Ta Neng Dam as well. General Sao Sokha Holds a Meeting to Review the Work of the Gendarmerie in 2020 and to Orient the Action Plan of the Gendarmerie in 2021
