According to Lt. Gen. Lim Sokharasmey, so far, the Department of Private Security Management has conducted 31 refresher courses for private security agents, with a total of 5,733 participants. To Siem Reap, don't forget to visit the Museum of Asian Traditional Textiles to learn about the country's cultural heritage along the Mekong and Ganges rivers.
(Siem Reap): The Museum of Asian Traditional Textiles is a museum that showcases the textiles, culture and commerce of the people living along the Mekong and Ganges rivers, located in Boeung Don Pa village along Samdech Vibol Panha Sok An Street (60 meters). ) Sangkat Slor Kram, Siem Reap city.
The museum was built in 2010-2011 and opened in April 2014 under the Mekong-Ganges Cooperation, with six countries participating: Cambodia, India, Laos, Myanmar, Thailand and Vietnam.
The purpose of building the Museum of Asian Traditional Textiles is to preserve the tradition of textile production, as well as to show the relationship between civilizations, cultures and trade of member countries that have existed for centuries.
After opening, the museum exhibits a number of important collections from its member countries in the museum's four galleries, including the Information Gallery, the Gallery of Materials and the Production Process of the Ancient Textiles and the Co-Textile Gallery. Session.
The museum is open to the public from Wednesday to Monday from 8:30 am to 4:00 pm, especially free of charge for monks, nuns and children under 12 years of age. The museum also has expert guides waiting to explain to all national and international guests for free. Mr. Pich Sophoan: Currently, there are 12 institutions training vocational skills, the labor market is in high demand now and in the future.
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Pech Sophoan, Minister Delegate to the Prime Minister and Permanent Secretary of the Ministry of Labor and Vocational Training, stated that there are currently 12 technical and vocational education and training institutions that are providing technical and vocational training. Bio: such as construction, electricity, mechanics, manufacturing, business and information technology and tourism, where the labor market is in high demand now and in the future.
Mr. Pech Sophoan said this at the opening ceremony of the Technical and Vocational Diploma (C1) training course for workers affected by the closure or suspension of enterprises due to the spread of Kovid-19 disease. February 9, 2021 at the meeting hall of the National Technical Training Institute.
At present, there are 12 technical and vocational education and training institutions that are providing training for the above program and have recruited 3,360 students (1,903 females) compared to the total training plan of 6,500 People.
All the tasks and measures taken by the Ministry are to contribute to the building of skilled and competent human resources in Cambodia based on the principles of transparency, accountability, the rule of law and the commitment to create a capable, productive, productive and conscientious workforce. And high professional ethics, resilient to changes in economic and social structure.
