Leaders of the Ministry of National Defense and the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces will start vaccinating against Kovid 19 tomorrow
(Phnom Penh): Leaders of institutions under the Ministry of National Defense and the General Command of the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces, aged 18 to over 59, will start vaccinating against Kovid 19 at 2:00 pm on the 10th. February 2021, tomorrow at Ketomealea Hospital. This is according to the announcement of the Ministry of National Defense signed by General Neang Phat, Permanent Secretary of the Ministry of National Defense.
Vaccination of military leaders was carried out on the recommendation of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, and under the direct supervision of Samdech Pich Sena Tea Banh, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of National Defense, and on a voluntary basis.
On behalf of the Kovid 19 Vaccine Group, the Ministry of National Defense, General Neang Phat, has invited the leadership, officers, deputies and soldiers of the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces to participate in this voluntary vaccination campaign to support the Royal Government's goal of health protection and promotion. The well-being of our troops.
