19 killed, more than 200 missing after devastating iceberg in Himalayan Valley - India on Sunday
New Delhi: Rescuers continue to search for more than 200 people still missing in India's Himalayan Valley on Monday, with some believed to be trapped in a cave. An underground mountain after a devastating iceberg occurred on Sunday. According to a release by CNA.
It should be noted that this natural disaster is caused by the collapse of large glaciers on the top of the Himalayas, which are adjacent to the Tibetan plateau. The glacier caused large amounts of rubble and mud to flow into nearby river valleys. So far, 19 people have been reported dead.
In 2013, floods caused by avalanches had already occurred in the same area. At that time, thousands of people died due to this horrible natural disaster.
