(Pursat): Mr. Pan Sosak, Minister of Commerce, pointed out 5 priority tasks to the officials of the Department of Commerce and the branch officials of Consumer Protection, Competition and Fraud Suppression (CPPCC) in Pursat Province. Take care to implement highly effective to provide convenience and confidence to the people.
The launch of these priorities took place on the occasion of the Minister's meeting with officials of the Department of Commerce and Pursat branch of the CPP on the afternoon of February 08, 2021, with the participation of the Ministry. Trade Officials of the Department of Commerce and many other branches of the CPP.
On that occasion, the Minister pointed out five important tasks to the officials of the Department of Commerce and the branch officials of the CPP to pay attention to achieve. The five jobs include:
First, civil servants of the Department of Commerce and the KOP branch must strictly avoid demanding informal fees from traders, traders, producers, exporters and other services that are contrary to the content of the joint proclamation on the public service package: between the Ministry of Commerce and the Ministry of Economy and Finance.
Second, civil servants of the Department of Commerce and the KPR branch must continue to work hard to further expand their knowledge, both in terms of skills and foreign languages, through further study, research and experience from competent and special officers. Collaborate on marketing, inspecting the safety of food products to be more energetic to protect the health of the people as well as protect the health of their own children.
Third, we must continue to strengthen mechanisms to monitor and control the management of business, services, trade, prices and stockpiles of rice, oil, fuel and trade in goods at the border using information technology systems. And promote mechanisms to solve all problems for farmers and producers by focusing on five potential products: chicken, rice, vegetables, potatoes, luxury rice and silk by setting up a weekend market.
Fourthly, during the performance of work and in daily life in the new situation of Kovid-19, I would like to ask you, Excellencies, Lok Chumteavs, to always be vigilant and to implement correctly according to the instructions of the Ministry of Health.
Fifth: Civil servants of the Department of Commerce and KPR branch Continue to cooperate more closely with local authorities to participate in widely disseminating all policies, regulations and in-depth reform programs of the Royal Government, especially the Ministry of Commerce to facilitate trade, promote exports and provide public services. To the people better.
(Phnom Penh): Currently, the two great powers, the United States and China, are using their influence to gain popularity from the world as well as seize the economy by mobilizing other countries to support them with barter. Something useful for all those countries to return.
For Cambodia is being seen as a bride that is of interest to China and the United States, with both powers using various means to attract this bride. But the policy of the Royal Government of Cambodia does not take any country as an enemy, it always wants to ally with all countries.
So far, Cambodia-China relations have been seen as a flood-proof one, while Cambodia-US relations do not seem as good as those with China. The reason for this is that the United States has always put pressure on Cambodia when providing aid and focusing on democracy and freedom, in contrast to China, which often provides unconditional assistance.
Through a roundtable discussion organized by the Royal Academy of Cambodia on the morning of February 8, 2021, five international geopolitical experts shared their experiences on how Cambodia can escape the influence of superpowers but can Maintain the benefits for this one nation.
He felt that this dynasty was not a Cold War dynasty and that the ideology was not as big as it was during the Cold War era, because this dynasty was an economic dynasty and in order to strengthen Cambodia's neutrality, it was first necessary to develop the country.
In particular, Meas Ny, an analyst and monitor of social development, claimed that trusting a superpower is all dangerous because the superpower does anything for its own benefit. For Cambodia, it depends on Cambodia's ability to challenge and work with all those great powers.
For Puy Kea, a correspondent for the Japanese news agency Kyodo in Cambodia, he believes that so far the eyes of the United States or Europe seem to be leaning towards China, and Cambodia itself has shown that Cambodia is trying to capture the United States. But the United States refuses to accept what Cambodia has tried.
Puy Kea, who has experience in geopolitics, also stressed that the escape from the influence of superpowers depends on human resources and political currents in the region and in the world.
In particular, for the relationship between Cambodia and China, he stressed that there is a good relationship because China throws a lot of interests and there are many other countries that are good with China, because China provides many benefits is not different from Cambodia.
But what is important for him is that he insists that the Cambodian people should stop prejudice against any country and accuse the Royal Government of Cambodia of taking sides with the United States or China, because this is nonsense. Useful. What is important is which country has provided more benefits to Cambodia in the development of all areas to the Cambodian people.
For Dr. Sok Touch, President of the Royal Academy of Cambodia, said that Cambodia is like a bride and the Royal Government uses a colorful policy of any country to benefit, because all countries need benefits for the development of the country.
Dr. Sok Touch, what Cambodia needs to prepare is to strengthen its human resources, to be politically strong, which in the past the Royal Government has been right in a colorful policy. In addition, it needs to increase its products and support what it produces. International Analysis: The Coup in Myanmar is a Test of Joe Biden's "Foreign Policy"
SINGAPORE: A military coup in Myanmar on Feb. 1 closed the Southeast Asian nation on the path to democracy. One of the first tests of the foreign policy of the new administration of US President Joe Biden, which has pledged to stand shoulder to shoulder with allies to protect democracy and human rights around the world.
Joe Biden and his foreign policy advisers have often stressed the importance of strengthening ties with allies and working with them to curb the spread of dictatorships around the world. But the setbacks of democracy in Myanmar, as well as the promise of a response, will be a test of the ability of the new US administration of Joe Biden to achieve such a concerted effort.
Thus, both the United States and its allies may have known in advance that threats or economic sanctions may be merely symbolic. That is, they have no saliva or any influence on the decisions of the Myanmar military. But the real influencer is China, which is a huge backbone and has always come forward to defend Myanmar from sanctions or condemnation by the international community.
So like it or not, the Biden administration will impose sanctions on the Myanmar military for two main purposes: First, it is a message to the world that the United States, the protector of democratic values and human rights, has returned, and it is Warn other countries not to follow Myanmar's example. Because if the United States remains silent or does not take action, what is happening in Myanmar may continue to happen elsewhere around the world in the future.
Second, Biden wants to use the coup case in Myanmar to mobilize allied forces as well as restore the United States' image as a world democratic leader, telling the allies that sanctions are not just about the Myanmar military. There are also arrows blocking the expansion of Chinese influence in the whole region. Australia, Canada and Britain, which are already at odds with China, could join Washington.
While the United Nations and most Western European countries, including the United States, have condemned the coup in Myanmar and called on the military to release the detainees, China has acted cautiously. What has been happening is Myanmar's internal affairs.
Experts believe that ASEAN member states may be cautious in issuing any statement regarding Myanmar. Because the current situation could drag them to the center of tensions between the United States and China, which could jeopardize national interests, including their economic recovery efforts and the COVID-19 crisis resolution.
