Samdech Techo Hun Sen allows journalists to be among the priority people to be vaccinated against Kovid 19 (Video inside) (Phnom Penh): Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, on February 7, 2021 The press is one of the top 19 people to be vaccinated against Kovid in Cambodia, as journalists are active and mobile everywhere to hunt for information to the public.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen's announcement was made at a press conference at Phnom Penh International Airport shortly after receiving 600,000 doses of Kovid 19 vaccine, a first step Chinese aid for Cambodia, arrived at the airport.
Answering questions from the media during the conference, Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated: "Let the Ministry of Health consider this group of reporters to be vaccinated because they search everywhere and do not know where to go. "Some, so I ask all journalists under the age of 59 to get vaccinated."
Samdech Techo Hun Sen added that professional journalists who want to receive the 19 Kovid vaccine must register and check the conditions of the Sinopharm vaccine, including those between the ages of 18 and 59. Samdech advised the Ministry of Health to cooperate with the Ministry of Information to arrange for journalists to receive the vaccine. In addition, to get the vaccine quickly, some media outlets can also contact the Ministry of Health directly.
Mr. Pen Bona, President of the Club of Cambodian Journalists, congratulated Samdech Techo Hun Sen on his sympathy for the media. He thanked and considered that this is an encouraging contribution to journalists who work for the public and show the care of Samdech Techo Hun Sen to journalists.
According to the Ministry of Information, Cambodia currently has 310 print media, 400 online websites and TV stations, 200 television stations, 221 radio stations and 22 representative offices of foreign news agencies, television and radio, including the Voice of America (VOA). . The Ministry of Information has issued more than 3,000 newsletters to national journalists.
