Five suspects sent to court after being arrested for trespassing on Lang Wildlife Sanctuary
(Phnom Penh): The ranger of the Ministry of Environment of Kratie Province on February 7, 2021, sent 5 suspects to court for legal proceedings after being arrested on February 5, 2021 by them. They broke into criminal activities in the Prey Lang area of Kratie province without permission. This is according to a press release from the Office of the Spokesperson of the Ministry of Environment.
The five perpetrators are: 1: Ouch Leng, President of the Cambodian Human Rights Task Force (unregistered), 2: Mr. Heng Sros, 3: Mr. Phay Sophon alias Man Mat, 4: Mr. Tang Cheang and 5: Mr. Heron, who was temporarily detained by the park rangers on the afternoon of February 5, 2021, was subjected to two legal procedures on February 7, 2021, after questioning and gathering evidence.
It should be noted that Mr. Ouch Leng, President of the Cambodian Human Rights Task Force and his accomplices, has been operating illegally under the label of the Cambodian Human Rights Task Force, which is not legally registered with the Ministry of Interior.
The ranger officer is a judicial police officer who has the duty to protect and conserve natural resources in accordance with the Law on Protected Areas in preventing and suppressing illegal activities that take place in the protected area, no matter who the person is. Found that the act is not in accordance with the law, must comply with the law in force.
It should be recalled that in March 2020, the Cambodian Human Rights Task Force had already acted illegally and was ordered by the court to suspend its activities until Mr. Ouch Leng, the organization's president, registered his organization with the Ministry of Interior. Surface first before proceeding further.
Some perpetrators take refuge under the label of associations and non-governmental organizations that are not registered with the Ministry of Interior by law or without permission and agreement with the Ministry of Environment. The report produces a variety of images, in particular the creation of images and defamation reports of Cambodia to seek financial support and to mobilize support for its factions.
According to a press release from the Office of the Spokesman for the Ministry of Environment, the perpetrators' answers confirmed that they were operating in the protected area to take pictures to seek financial support from donors. This clearly shows the malicious intent of some groups who take refuge under the label of environmentalists and forest activists who use dirty methods to benefit their party and serve a corrupt agenda.
The Ministry of Environment calls on and encourages some donors to provide support to associations and NGOs that are properly registered and law-abiding to promote law enforcement and encourage law-abiding associations and NGOs. And do not feed any illegal movement.
The Ministry of Environment always welcomes the participation of associations and non-governmental organizations in the protection and conservation of natural resources, but must enter through the legal channels in force, not stealing activities from the law in force. People who take refuge under the label of environmentalists and always insult the national law should learn to respect the law because Cambodia is the rule of law and do not consider themselves an outlaw group.
