Professor Dr. Rector continued that Asia-Europe University always pays attention to the quality of training, especially to promote and enhance research in all forms, with modern materials and a clear curriculum in accordance with the standards and There is increasing support from scholars from all walks of life, especially recognition from the Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports and development partners, both domestic and foreign.
In addition, Professor Dr. Chea Sopheap instructed all students to take the opportunity to continue learning to develop their skills as well as future careers. In particular, there is no graduation, so all winning students should continue to study for a master's degree.
(Phnom Penh): A female trout, one of the most endangered species in the world, has to save the life of a hunter trapped in the Lumphat Wildlife Sanctuary in Ratanakkiri Province. This is what Mr. Net Pheaktra, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Environment said on February 6, 2021.
Last January, conservation officials discovered the nests of five endangered species in the Lumphat Wildlife Sanctuary in Ratanakkiri province, a sign of Cambodia's rare bird presence. There is a recurrence.
According to the Secretary of State, the rescued giant trout has now been handed over to the Cambodian Animal Life Organization in collaboration with ACCB to help care for and treat the trapped wounds.
Mr. Neth Pheaktra stated, "Cambodia is the only major sanctuary in the world for the giant endemic and endemic species, the most endangered species in the world." Mr. "Cambodia is proud to have this rare animal and we all need to work together to protect and conserve this rare species for generations to come for the benefit of the world's biodiversity."
At the same time, Mr. Net Pheaktra pointed out that in 2005, the giant trout was designated by Royal Decree as the national symbol bird of Cambodia. The giant trout is an endangered species and is protected by the laws of the Kingdom of Cambodia. That is why the Royal Government of Cambodia pays great attention to the protection and conservation of the endangered species.
Mr. Neth Pheaktra stated that in order to improve the efficiency of the management and conservation of natural resources and wildlife biodiversity of all kinds, the Ministry of Environment has prepared policies and action plans on the local economy of the protected area communities in and around. Protected areas for a prosperous life.
A senior official of the Ministry of Environment stressed that "At the same time, the authorities will enforce the strictest laws to protect and conserve giant trout and white-tailed deer for the benefit of biodiversity and for attracting tourists." "Also."
