(Phnom Penh): As the world as well as the region has not yet recovered from the Kovid 19 crisis, the ASEAN member states and the ASEAN Secretary-General have been consulting carefully and agreed to promote their respective domestic tourism movements, especially Encourage tourists to visit the tourism community, eco-tourism sites as well as rural tourism areas more strongly.
This was stated by Mr. Try Chhiv, Director of the Department of International and ASEAN Cooperation of the Ministry of Tourism after the 24th ASEAN Tourism Ministers' Meeting and related meetings held from 04-05 February 2021. Organized by the Ministry of Tourism of Cambodia at Sofitee Hotel Phnom Penh Phuket.
Mr. Try Chhiv said that among the plans put forward by ASEAN to restore tourism, there is also an important direction is to promote the movement of domestic tourism, especially to encourage tourists to visit the community. Eco-tourism as well as rural tourism to be stronger.
He said ASEAN has promoted the development of small and medium enterprises (SMEs) in the tourism sector, which is a strategy to create job opportunities, especially in rural areas. This strategy is focused on developing ecotourism products in communities and tourism events such as tourism festivals.
He added that ASEAN members also agreed to exchange experiences in promoting domestic tourism in their respective countries to share experiences and best practices.
In the past, Cambodia, as well as ASEAN, has also paid close attention to the development of tourism or ecotourism associations, which is considered a priority, but in the wake of the Kovid 19 crisis, ASEAN sees it as an opportunity because it can not Travel abroad, so it is an opportunity to encourage domestic tourism, and this promotion can also help those working in tourism in the community or in rural areas.
It is clear that domestic tourism can not compensate for the loss of international tourism, but it is a way to help him survive, they can continue his work.
According to Mr. Try Chhiv, ASEAN has paid more attention to the development of local tourism through the sharing of experiences and there will be more meetings in the future.
Normally, Cambodia has to host the ASEAN Tourism Forum 2021 in Cambodia, but due to the issue of Kovid, ASEAN could not organize face to face, including the exhibition, which is a big event, so ASEAN members also supported Cambodia to organize the forum. This full-service tour will be held in 2022.
As a result of the expectations of ASEAN member countries from now until 2022, all member countries trust Cambodia to lead various meetings to restore tourism in the region.
