The tradition of fishing together to prepare for the sky of Angkor residents continue to practice steadily
(Siem Reap): In the Angkor resort area, there is a rich collection of living heritage, both intangible and tangible, and has been consistently practiced by the people of Angkor to this day.
In fact, every year for many generations, until the month of Meak, the residents of Bangkong village, Ampil commune, Prasat Bakong district, Siem Reap province, never miss and always come together to celebrate fishing as a community to prepare for the ascension ceremony according to the traditional tradition. .
The joint fishing took place in Trapeang Beong, an ancient pond with water and rain, and the locals have preserved it. The festival is pre-arranged and a joint fishing day is set so that the villagers can go and catch it, but must use traditional fishing gear, including fishing nets.
Mr. Pich Khin, village chief of Bongkong village, said that the fish caught was partly for family cooking, partly for making water, noodles and cooking together for the Ascension or Ascension Ceremony according to the traditional tradition.
The people of Bang Kong village, Mr. Yoeun Dara, who got up to catch fish in the early morning, expressed their happiness to come fishing together, which shows the solidarity of the people in the village, especially to maintain the tradition that has existed for a long time. And. As a young man, he wanted this tradition to continue for the next generation to know forever.
