(Svay Rieng): There was a surprise all night when a woman was found dead under a barn, the people reported to the local authorities to examine the body immediately. This case happened at 7:40 pm on February 6, 2021 at a villager's house in Chek village, Samrong commune, Chantrea district, Svay Rieng province.
According to the district police, the woman was named Tuok Sara, 40 years old, a buffalo herder, residing in Kandal village, Prasat commune, Bavet city, Svay Rieng province. At the time of the incident, the villagers found the victim lying dead in the buffalo stall of Kong Rap, male, 47 years old, farmer, residing in Chek village, Samrong commune, Chantrea district.
