(Phnom Penh): Mr. Sok Chenda Sophea, Minister Delegate to the Prime Minister and Secretary General of the Council for Rural Development (CDC), revealed that the new investment law will allow the Capital-Provincial Board of Governors to review and decide on a wider range of investment projects. Before and with a capital of more than $ 2 million, this is good news for sub-national authorities and investors in the provinces as well.
Currently, the new investment law has not yet come into force, is in the process of preparation, which is expected to pass in the first half of 2021.
"Now, in relation to past investments, Cambodia has failed, and the Capital, Provincial and Municipal Sub-Committees are in charge of this investment," he said. Previously, projects with less than $ 2 million were handed over to the sub-national level, but the new investment law will set a larger limit. This is good news for sub-national authorities and investors in these provinces, a clear policy of the Royal Government to push the decision closer to the people.
This senior official expressed Cambodia's strong position that there is no concern and insecurity for foreign investors because Cambodia is a country of peace and good political stability.
"For both Cambodian and foreign investors, please have faith in the Royal Government of Cambodia because of investment and business," he said. "Factors that investors come to invest in Cambodia because of peace and stability in Cambodia over the last 20 years, Cambodia has high economic growth, with results that are pleasing to everyone.
He added that these are the benefits of peace and stability that come from the efforts of the Royal Government of Cambodia.
