Full Outcome of the 24th ASEAN Tourism Ministers' Meeting and Related Meetings 4-5 February
The following are the key outcomes of the 24th ASEAN Tourism Ministers' Meeting:
First: Restoring trust and confidence
Vaccination Program: All Ministers welcome the launch of the Vaccination Program in ASEAN Member States and encourage all travelers to ASEAN and intra-ASEAN to be vaccinated against Kovid-19 to Ensure health and safety, increase trust, confidence and resilience for a safe and responsible tourism restoration.
Second: Rehabilitation after the Kovid-19 crisis: Preparing for ASEAN as a single tourism destination
* ASEAN Tourism Marketing Strategy: The Minister welcomes the updated ASEAN Tourism Marketing Strategy 2021-2025, which sets out a roadmap for the next five years (2021-2025), including marketing activities to promote tourism during During and after the Kovid-19 crisis, focusing on the health and safety of the people.
ASEAN Tourism Investment Portfolio: The Minister approved the ASEAN Tourism Investment Portfolio, which continues to attract and facilitate international investors and businesses in the ASEAN tourism sector. This portfolio will encourage more tourism investment to ASEAN member countries, which will create more jobs and opportunities for local people, especially the rehabilitation process.
* ASEAN Statement on Digital Tourism: The Minister emphasized the importance of the ASEAN Statement on Digital Tourism adopted by the ASEAN Leaders at the 37th ASEAN Summit and instructed the ASEAN National Tourism Officials to implement the plan. The ASEAN Tourism Strategy 2016-2025 has been updated with the vision of promoting digital transformation in the ASEAN tourism industry.
* Phnom Penh Statement: The ASEAN Ministers also adopted the Phnom Penh Declaration on ASEAN Tourism in a Sustainable and Strong Environment and instructed the officials to strengthen close cooperation with ASEAN stakeholders, international organizations, the private sector and other stakeholders in the tourism sector. To implement this statement effectively.
The ASEAN Ministers thanked the Royal Government of Cambodia for hosting the 24th Ministerial Meeting on Tourism and related meetings via video during this difficult time.
