(Central): According to the Ministry of Social Affairs, juvenile offenders currently incarcerated in prisons together with adults will be relocated to receive separate vocational training at the Youth Rehabilitation Center soon after. Completed in March.
Meanwhile, on the morning of February 5, 2021, Mr. Vong Soth, Minister of Social Affairs, together with many officials, inspected the construction process of the Youth Rehabilitation Center to prepare for the opening of the illegal juveniles who are staying in prisons to live separately. At this center. The Youth Rehabilitation Center currently under construction is located in Bakou Commune, Kandal Steung District, Kandal Province.
According to Minister Vong Soth, at the groundbreaking ceremony for the construction of the Youth Rehabilitation Center on February 20, 2020, the Youth Rehabilitation Center has an important role to play in managing minors, providing education, vocational training, and psychological education. Treat, care, protect and help minors become honest and useful citizens for the society.
According to Chapter 13, Article 76 of the Law on Juvenile Justice, it is pointed out that the Ministry in charge of Social Affairs must establish youth rehabilitation centers in the capital-province for the management of minors.
Mr. Din Borey, Director of the Department of Youth Rehabilitation of the Ministry of Social Affairs, stated that the Youth Rehabilitation Center has so far achieved about 80% and can be completed in March and can start operating soon.
He added that this is the first time that Cambodia has built this center in accordance with the juvenile justice law for the transfer of juvenile offenders from prison, and in the first year, it is planned to put 500 juvenile offenders and possibly Total storage capacity of 2,000 people.
The director of the Department of Youth Rehabilitation also stated that for this center, there will be many skills training that is in line with the current market needs, including skills such as repairing mobile phones, electricity and air conditioning to turn them into good resources. Ability to earn a living after the end of the sentence.
The director of the department added that according to the juvenile justice law, juvenile offenders are allowed to live in this center until they are 24 years old, in case of remaining punishment, they will be transferred back to prison.
It should be noted that Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the Prime Minister of Cambodia, agreed in principle with the request to establish a Youth Rehabilitation Center by Mr. Vong Soth, Minister of Social Affairs, Veterans and Youth Rehabilitation. The Youth Rehabilitation Center has a total of 17 buildings, 12 of which need to be renovated and 5 of which need to be rebuilt.
