Samdech Techo Hun Sen Recommends 12 Points for the Preparation of the National Cultural Day on March 3 in the Kovid-19 Epidemic Crisis
First, the Ministry of Culture and Fine Arts must cooperate with ministries, institutions, local authorities, national and international organizations, associations, development partners and the private sector, which are operating in the field of culture, to jointly disseminate national culture through the media in order to celebrate the Day. National culture, March 3, 2021.
Second, the Ministry of Culture and Fine Arts shall act as the Secretariat for the preparation of propaganda documents and dissemination of the content of the National Cultural Day and shall guide all Departments of Culture and Fine Arts in the capital and provinces in disseminating the content of the National Cultural Day widely by placing banners in Public during the beginning of March 2021, especially to indigenous communities living in their geographical territory.
Fourth, the Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports and the Ministry of Culture and Fine Arts must work together to find ways to disseminate the content of the National Cultural Day on March 3 to students in the current situation of Kovid-19 disease by following the prevention and guidance measures of the Ministry of Health.
Fifth, the Ministry of Tourism must disseminate the content of the National Cultural Day on March 3 as much as possible, especially among national and international tourists through travel agencies and tour operators of all kinds.
Sixth, the Ministry of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation shall instruct all ambassadors, consuls and honorary consuls of the Kingdom of Cambodia abroad to disseminate the contents of the National Cultural Day on March 3, including: Slogans and illustrations.
Seventh, the Ministry of Cults and Religions must inspire the movement of monks and all believers to organize the dissemination of the content of the National Cultural Day on March 3 in temples, religious centers, Vipassana centers and other shrines as much as possible.
Eighth, the Ministry of Interior and the Ministry of National Defense must have a plan to guide the grassroots to maintain security and public order on the occasion of the National Cultural Day on March 3 to be effective and highly responsible.
9th: Apsara National Authority, Preah Vihear National Authority and Sambor Prei Kuk National Authority must disseminate and highlight the results of work that contributes to the preservation, protection, preservation and promotion of the value of the national cultural heritage to be stable, vibrant and have a universal value to Celebrate National Cultural Day on March 3.
10th: Capital-Provincial Administration must support the Department of Culture and Fine Arts in organizing, disseminating and posting the contents of the National Cultural Day on March 3 in their territory, focusing on education to the public, especially in Young people to have a stronger spirit to participate in preserving, protecting and promoting national cultural values.
Eleventh: All houses, all ministries, institutions, local authorities, schools, public and private enterprises must raise national flags, banners, banners, slogans and post Ahos on public streets in their units and houses from the 1st to the 1st. March 9, 2021.
And 12th: Participating in promotional activities related to the National Cultural Day on March 3 must dress in the national tradition.
