Read the full press release of the Ministry of Agriculture: The wedding ceremony becomes the groom's funeral on the day of the reception
(Kampong Chhnang): The wedding ceremony turned into the groom's funeral and the guests, both men and women, who came to eat dinner in the evening at one of the weddings, were very shocked after Received information that the merciless death snatched the bridegroom on the wedding day, depriving him of the bride forever, never to return, does not seem to sympathize with the newlyweds.
The above horrific incident happened at around 15:30 on February 4, 2021 in Kandal village, Phsar Chhnang commune, Kampong Chhnang city, Kampong Chhnang province.
According to local residents at the scene, the groom, Krong Puth, 40, a widower with two children, was abandoned by his wife in Samrong village, Phsar Chhnang commune, Kampong Chhnang city. The bride, Ros Thavy, is over 30 years old and lives in Kandal village, Phsar Chhnang commune, Kampong Chhnang city.
Prior to the incident, the victim, the groom, was getting ready to receive guests for dinner in the evening, suddenly felt unwell, so the family was taken to Kampong Chhnang Provincial Referral Hospital. . He then died in hospital from a stroke due to high blood pressure.
After the incident, the family also brought the groom's body to be kept at the groom's house in Samrong village, Phsar Chhnang commune. In particular, at the wedding at the bride's house on the evening of February 4, in front of the wedding, the bride and groom were not present to receive the guests, the bride and groom helped to receive guests instead of the children. The maiden went to attend her husband's funeral at her husband's house.
The names and photos of the bride and groom at the wedding have been removed, much to the surprise of the guests, who will be sympathetic to everyone. Meanwhile, some guests who came to eat also disappeared because they knew about this incident, while some guests came to eat and found out about this, so they went to attend the funeral at the groom's house.
