(Siem Reap): The Norodom Sihanouk-Angkor Museum is located along Samdech Vibol Panha Sok An Street (60 meters) in Boeng Don Pa Village, Sangkat Slor Kram, Siem Reap City, Siem Reap Province, a rich archeological site.
The museum was built in collaboration with the APSARA Authority and Sofia University with financial support from Japan's AEON.
The main purpose of building this museum is to preserve and present to the national and international public the artifacts excavated during the study at Banteay Kdei in 2000 and 2001.
Since opening in 2008, the museum has expanded its collection of collections, with the museum currently hosting major exhibitions such as the Koh Ta Meas and Prey Kmeng Cemetery Exhibition, the Banteay Kdei Temple Exhibition, the Kork Patri Exhibition, and the Achievement Exhibition. Cooperation between APSARA Authority and international institutions in the protection and restoration of temples in the Angkor area.
The Norodom Sihanouk-Angkor Museum is open to the public from Tuesday to Sunday from 8 am to 4 pm, especially free of charge for the armed forces, monks, nuns and children under 12 years of age.
