Australian Ambassador to Cambodia Visits Anlong Veng Historic Site Anlong Veng Peace Center
(Oddar Meanchey): Mr. Bablo Kang, Australian Ambassador to Cambodia, on February 4, 2021, visited Anlong Veng Historical Site, Anlong Veng Peace Center and met with Mr. Hor Chinvirayuth, Governor of Anlong Veng District. Anlong Veng district was the last stronghold of the Khmer Rouge movement, which was integrated back into the Royal Government in 1998.
Mr. Bablo Kang and a delegation, including Duke Sear or Tith, visited the Anlong Veng Peace Center of the Documentation Center of Cambodia. Dr. Ly Sok Kheang, Director of Anlong Veng Peace Center, welcomed and guided the visit.
The Anlong Veng Peace Center holds nearly 70,000 pages of documents, including telegrams, reports, confessions and biographies of former Khmer Rouge members in the Siem Reap-Oddar Meanchey area left over from the Khmer Rouge era (1975-1979), as well as More interviews.
The Pol Pot Cemetery and the Anlong Veng Peace Center on the ridge of Dangrek Mountain have become other important destinations. The ambassador and the delegation visited a photo exhibition in the former meeting house of the former top leader of the Khmer Rouge movement. Today, the Anlong Veng Peace Center has turned this location into a classroom for the history of the Khmer Rouge and the history of the Anlong Veng community.
