Real estate experts expect foreign investors to return to Cambodia in mid-2021
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Chrek Soknim, President of the Cambodian Association of Real Estate Appraisers, said that the spread of Kovid 19 vaccine will attract the return of foreign investors in Cambodia.
"Foreign investors will be able to return to Cambodia when the Kovid 19 vaccine spreads around the world during July and August, while some countries have already received the Kovid 19 vaccine," he said.
He added that for foreign investors, they think of two important points: before preparing to invest, they get the vaccine and the area that will come to invest with the vaccine to ensure that there is no risk of infection. Illness even if they already have the vaccine.
He said that 2021 is the year that investors began to be busy gradually, in January, some investors began to look at the real estate sector and began to trade with partners.
Mr. Chrek Soknim also confirmed that the land sector in 2020, despite the crisis 19 Kovid, but the real estate sector has not decreased or fallen in price.
Mr. Chrek Soknim said, "The flow of land sales in 2020 has decreased somewhat, but the sale price has not decreased. "It has not slowed down because the domestic trade has not slowed down, but the trade from foreign investors who can not come to invest in Cambodia due to the spread of Kovid 19."
He added, however, that the real estate sector in Cambodia remained strong, with only a portion of the investment from foreign investors missing.
Keam Seaklong, Real Estate Advisor of the Cambodian Association of Real Estate Appraisers, said that there are two main channels for buying and selling condominiums: locals and foreigners. Condo sales and rentals are down.
7 model families who built Khmer houses according to the architectural design received a certificate of appreciation from APSARA Authority
(Siem Reap): The APSARA Authority on February 4, 2021 handed over certificates of appreciation to 7 model families in the Angkor resort area who built Khmer houses correctly in accordance with the architectural plan of APSARA Authority.
The award ceremony was held at the home of the people in Preah Dak village, Preah Dak commune, Banteay Srei district, in the presence of Mr. Yit Chanda, Deputy Director General of APSARA Authority and with the participation of Banteay Srei district administration officials. .
Mr. Yit Chandarath stated that according to the policy of the Royal Government, the APSARA Authority is striving to raise the value of Khmer style houses as a tangible heritage property and to participate in showing the cultural values to national and international tourists and the next generation to know about the heritage of Khmer ancestors.
He added that Angkor is a cultural site of Khmer identity, so Cambodians living in this area must take part in preserving the cultural values of their ancestors, the cultural heritage of mankind.
The people who own the house expressed their unexpected happiness that their house was considered as a model house by the APSARA Authority and the Banteay Srei District Administration and received a certificate of appreciation.
However, they also thanked the APSARA Authority and the Banteay Srei District Administration for handing over their certificates of appreciation and appealed to other residents living in Angkor Park if they were planning to build a house. Apply to build and build a house according to the Khmer house model in accordance with the instructions of APSARA Authority.
It should be noted that in the near future, APSARA Authority plans to hand over the same certificate to more people in Angkor Park in Angkor Thom and Prasat Bakong districts who have built Khmer houses in accordance with the architectural plan of Apsara National Authority.
Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng urges the mainstreaming of road traffic law education from kindergarten (Video inside) (Phnom Penh): Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of Interior and Chairman of the National Road Safety Committee on the afternoon of the 4th This February 2021 urges the relevant ministries and institutions, especially the Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports, to integrate education on the law on road traffic in the curriculum from kindergarten.
In a meeting to review the results of road safety work in 2020 and the direction for 2021 at the Ministry of Interior, Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng said that the need to teach road traffic law from kindergarten to the younger generation. After learning more about the law and having a deep-rooted idea of obeying traffic laws.
According to Sar Kheng, in the future, Cambodia will have more labyrinths, whether in urban or rural areas, so it is important to understand traffic laws. Samdech added that when teaching from a young age, this does not lead to wasting time teaching at a higher level.
As the Chairman of the National Committee for Road Safety, Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng emphasized that the current teaching of traffic law is from primary school to higher education, but Samdech said that if teaching from kindergarten, it must be taught once. No more in higher education.
