(Kampot): Phnom Toek and Phnom Toch, located near the Cambodia-Vietnam border in Boeung Sala Khang Tbong commune and Russey commune, East district, Kampong Trach district, Kampot province, is an attractive natural tourist area, but this area is not very You go on vacation. With a total area of more than 600 hectares, this beautiful area is more than 30 kilometers east of the provincial town of Kampot.
Sitting on a red chair in front of the house, the two district owners said that from the beginning, Phnom Tuek had a lot of interesting things, both superstitious and social reality. The old man described what can be summed up as the superstition that from the beginning of the mountain there were guardians and guardians of the land near the border and no one could settle there.
As for the social reality, the sediment under the mountain is full of fertilizer to be used in rice fields. Dressed as farmers, the two claim that if the soil under the mountain is just one cart, the rice yield is very high. The sediment there is planted once, making the rice harvest for three years.
Another great thing is that the mountain of water, they can not say anything foolish, and for peace, some people always pray when they go there. The two former farmers recalled that when he was about 15 years old, many people died when he went to get the sediment under the mountain because the rocks fell from above.
Surrounding the mountain of water and small mountains, surrounded by lakes with aquatic plants, especially with palm trees and chambers that bloom, show beautiful colors, enjoy the beautiful scenery. In addition, water plants and other aquatic plants provide food for the local buffalo.
Features for camping enthusiasts, they can visit there due to the wide hills near both mountains. The entrance is not a problem, that is, even luxury cars can get there.
Not only that, this area provides a place for birds, including cranes, to fly from the canyon to the lakes around the lakes and small mountains. Some cranes in the Anlong Pring landscape protected area fly to forage in the mountains and small mountainous areas with large lakes up to more than 600 hectares.
