Ministry of Economy through Cambodian Entrepreneurs is ready to release the third aid package to small and medium enterprises and start-ups
(Phnom Penh): In 2020, Cambodian entrepreneurs handed out two grant packages. Through the Ministry of Economy and Finance, the first and second grants of Cambodian entrepreneurs provided about $ 400,000 to 27 small and medium enterprises and start-ups out of 278 applications from 19 provinces and the capital.
Small and medium enterprises and start-ups selected from various sectors such as agriculture / agro-industry, handicrafts, services, information and communication technology.
The Cambodian Entrepreneur Assistance Package is a mechanism by the Royal Government of Cambodia to implement strategies to support small and medium enterprises and start-ups to address business and operational challenges and future uncertainties caused by the epidemic. Of the Kovid-19 crisis. This particular support will be allocated to the necessary parts of the business in the sectors most severely affected by the epidemic.
Mr. Vongsey Visoth, Deputy Prime Minister and Permanent Secretary of the Ministry of Economy and Finance, noted that the grant package will help small and medium enterprises and start-ups to sustain and revitalize their businesses during the period. In times of crisis, these businesses are the driving force behind the economy by creating jobs and adding value, as well as supporting Cambodia's economic growth.
He added, "The Royal Government of Cambodia, through the Entrepreneurship Development Fund, as well as Cambodian entrepreneurs, aims to build leadership or, in other words, a leader in the private sector to fight in the economic, trade and technology battles through increasing competitiveness." "Micro-business efficiency and overall economic efficiency in the new global environment or new normalization in order to create added value and attract new economic forces in Cambodia."
In 2021, Cambodian entrepreneurs are preparing a third grant package as a response strategy to provide support to businesses to strengthen them. The aid package also acts as a mechanism to inject cash directly into the economy through business to support the work of the Cambodian people.
Dr. Chheang Vann Monin, Executive Director of Cambodian Entrepreneurs, said, “Cambodian Entrepreneurs believe that this grant package is a timely and effective response from the Royal Government of Cambodia through the Ministry of Economy and Finance, implemented by Cambodian Entrepreneurs. "Small and medium enterprises and start-ups are being affected by the Kovid-19 crisis and are preparing their businesses for the new normal context."
