Samdech Techo Hun Sen Congratulates Mr. Nguyen Fu Chong on his re-election as Secretary General of the Central Committee of the Communist Party of Vietnam (Video inside) (Phnom Penh): On February 3, 2021, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, President of the People's Party Cambodians called on Nguyen Fu Chong, expressing his warm congratulations on his re-election as Secretary-General of the 13th Central Committee of the Communist Party of Vietnam.
In this telephone meeting, Samdech Techo Hun Sen also congratulated all members of the Communist Party of Vietnam on the occasion of the 91st anniversary of the founding of the Communist Party of Vietnam and the successful organization of the 13th Party Congress.
The President of the Cambodian People's Party stressed that under the right perspective of the Communist Party of Vietnam has achieved many great achievements in successful socio-economic development and the maintenance of peace, stability and prosperity. He praised Vietnam for its active role as chair of ASEAN in 2020 and as a non-permanent member of the UN Security Council for the 2020-2021 term.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen expressed his firm belief that under the patriarchy and wise leadership of Nguyen Phu Trong, the Communist Party of Vietnam will implement all the political guidelines and decisions adopted at the General Assembly. The 13th Communist Party of Vietnam successfully transformed Vietnam into a strong nation with equity, democracy and civilization.
Mr. Nguyen Fu Chong thanked Samdech Techo Hun Sen for calling to congratulate the 91st anniversary of the founding of the Communist Party of Vietnam and the successful conclusion of the 13th Party Congress. Re-elected General Secretary of the 13th Mandate Central Committee of the Communist Party of Vietnam.
Mr. Nguyen Fu Chong also thanked the Central Committee of the Cambodian People's Party (CPP), relevant institutions and units of Cambodia for sending warm congratulations to their Vietnamese counterparts, which is a reflection of the traditional close friendship. Good neighbors as well as sustainable and long-term cooperation between Cambodia and Vietnam.
Mr. Nguyen Fu Chong also wished the Cambodian people to overcome all the challenges caused by the spread of Kovid-19 disease and achieve sustainable national development and long-term prosperity, which actively contributes. In maintaining peace, stability and development in the region and the world.
The two leaders reaffirmed their strong commitment to continue to work closely to enhance bilateral relations and enhance multifaceted cooperation through the implementation of all agreements. Effective and timely in order to further enhance bilateral relations for the mutual benefit of both countries, as well as the region and the world.
