It should be noted that President Nguyen Phu Trong was re-elected by the Communist Party of Vietnam on Sunday, January 31, 2021. Nguyen Fu Chung was elected General Secretary of the Communist Party of Vietnam for three consecutive terms (one term lasts five years).
The election took place during the Congress of the Communist Party of Vietnam, which took place from January 25 to February 1 in Hanoi, where 1,600 party delegates from across the country voted to elect a new party and government leader. And set out economic plans and policies.
The election of 76-year-old Nguyen Fu Chong to the post of party secretary general took place under a special waiver stipulating that those over the age of 65 must retire. Nguyen Fu Chong has already been elected party secretary-general twice, in 2011 and 2016.
