Teachers take student money and transfer it from Santhor Mok School to Sen Sok School, if they do not resign, they will face delisting from the framework
(Phnom Penh): After conducting a research, the Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports found that a teacher at Santhor Mok Primary School actually took 60,000 riel a month from students, according to the parents. As a disciplinary measure, the teacher was transferred from Santhor Mok Primary School in Toul Kork district to teach at Sen Sok Primary School in Sen Sok district.
The disciplinary action against the teacher came after some parents of students at Santhor Mok Primary School recently posted on Facebook that teachers at the school were forcing students to work overtime and expel them. Classes for students who do not study and demanded 60,000 riel from each student as a thank you teacher.
Ros Sovacha, spokesman for the Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports, told Fresh News on February 3, 2021 that under the cooperation between the school and the Department of Education, Youth and Sports of Phnom Penh, found the mistakes of teachers. This picture is exactly what the parents of the students mentioned.
"Under the cooperation between the Department of Education, Youth and Sports of Phnom Penh and the management of Santhor Mok Primary School to solve the above irregularities, primary school teachers working at Santhor Mok Primary School in Toul Kork district have been relocated," the spokesman said. To work at Sen Sok Primary School, Khan Sen Sok.
He added, "In general, when there are irregularities in educational institutions throughout Cambodia, the management of educational institutions has administrative measures to deal with the situation and may cooperate with the Department of Education, Youth and Sports, which is the staff of the Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports. "Local solutions, education, youth and sports."
Mr. Ros Sovacha said that in general, any teacher who violates the guidelines of the Ministry will be subject to administrative penalties, such as written reprimand, may be contracted after the misconduct or The change of place of work may lead to the removal of the name from the civil service under the auspices of the Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports.
According to Ros Sovacha, the teacher who kidnapped the student has committed similar mistakes in the past, and the school and the education department have been reprimanded and contracted.
Mr. Ros Sovacha said that the change of school is another serious disciplinary measure for this teacher. If he continues to make such mistakes, he may face delisting from the Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports.
The spokesman of the Ministry of Education also emphasized that the Royal Government of Cambodia is highly committed to strengthening the quality of teachers by improving the qualifications and salaries of teachers every year.
Mr. Ros Sovacha said that the Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports has continued to work with stakeholders, especially the Ministry of Economy and Finance to increase teachers' salaries.
