Mr. Vongsy Visoth Chairs a Meeting to Review the Draft Cambodian Digital Economy and Social Policy Framework
The fourth phase of the Rectangular Strategy points to the need to prepare for the digital economy and respond to the Fourth Industrial Revolution, to maximize the benefits of rapid technological and digitalization in the country, the region and the world.
The Cambodian Digital Economy and Social Policy Framework is a strategic document that reflects the Royal Government's long-term vision of building a digital society and economy into a new economic growth platform, as well as contributing to competitiveness and promoting diversification. Economy and Promoting the Welfare of the People of Cambodia's Digital Society.
The policy framework will also capture the opportunities and potentials of the digital technology sector, aiming to use digital technology to pave the way and accelerate the country's development, and to address existing challenges as well as challenges. And the negative effects that may eventually occur due to the effects of using digital technology.
In addition, in the context of the Kovid-19 crisis, this policy document will also be an important tool in Cambodia's post-Kovid-19 economic recovery plan, providing both direct and indirect support for growth. Economy through building rich digital infrastructure, logistics, attracting investment, creating productivity and enhancing competitiveness.
The draft policy framework is scheduled to be submitted to a meeting chaired by Dr. Aun Porn Moniroth, Deputy Prime Minister, Minister of Economy and Finance and Chairman of the Supreme National Economic Council for further review and approval in the near future. This policy document from the Royal Government. Samdech Picheay Sena Tea Banh Meets a Group of Doctors Vaccinated against Kovid-19
