(Phnom Penh): In January this year, Cambodia exported nearly 30,000 tons of fresh mangoes, including 11,638 tons of fresh mangoes with phytosanitary certificates and 18,000 tons of fresh mangoes without phytosanitary certificates. This was confirmed by Mr. Veng Sakhon, Minister of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries.
Currently, there are 124,319 hectares of mango plantations nationwide, with a total harvested area of 91,398 hectares, yielding an average of 16 tons per hectare for one season with a total yield of 1,448,677 tons.
Cambodia has signed an agreement on fresh mango exports to China and Korea.
China has not yet exported, and the ministry is currently evaluating companies that have applied to meet their phytosanitary requirements for the export of fresh mangoes from Cambodia to the country. China, too.
The General Department of Agriculture has also received applications from 55 companies / plantation owners / farming communities for registration of mango plantations and packaging locations for the export of Cambodian fresh mangoes to China.
It should be noted that in 2020, Cambodia exported 957,680 tons of fresh mangoes to foreign markets, of which 107,680 tons were exported with phytosanitary certificates and 850,000 tons were exported without phytosanitary certificates. .
