Wildlife Alliance cooperates with the Royal Government to conserve forests and wildlife in Stung Hav and Prey Nob districts, Preah Sihanouk province.
The meeting was attended by Mr. Ung Sam Ath, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries, Deputy Governor of Preah Sihanouk Province in charge of Forestry, Prey Nup District Governor, Steung Hav District Governor, Deputy Director of Prey Nup Forestry Administration and leaders of the Council for Rehabilitation and Development. Agriculture and rural areas.
She said climate change has affected forests and is now facing deforestation by illegal squatters.
She added that on the tops of mountains in Stung Hav and Prey Nup districts, the Deputy Prime Minister had built temples and resorts with many statues carved out of the existing stone slabs there, which made the people more in love with nature. And the forests there are growing, as part of promoting people's participation in forest conservation and conservation.
On behalf of the Wildlife Alliance, she would like to express her deep gratitude to the Royal Government of Cambodia, especially the Deputy Prime Minister and relevant government agencies for supporting the Wildlife Alliance's operations in Cambodia to protect and conserve forests and wildlife.
She also urged local authorities, relevant ministries and forestry administrations to continue to work more closely with the Wildlife Alliance to prevent deforestation in order to preserve the forest as a habitat for wildlife of all kinds. Both provide a source of water and a green environment for humankind, as well as cultural and Buddhist values for future generations.
At the same time, the Deputy Governor of Preah Sihanouk Province promised to guide the people to participate in the maintenance of the forest and continue to regularly inspect the forest protection area and asked Wild Aid to continue planting trees elsewhere.
Meanwhile, the Prey Nup district governor agreed to continue cooperation with Wild Aid and requested the Ministry of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries to continue legal measures to support forest protection activities.
He said that the participation of the Wildlife Alliance is a valuable contribution with the Royal Government in preventing environmental impacts and the conservation of wildlife and forests, especially the preservation of natural resources for the Royal Government to develop the economy and Improve people's livelihoods and preserve forests, wildlife and other natural resources for future generations.
On behalf of the Royal Government, the Deputy Prime Minister would like to support the projects of the Wildlife Friends in the Cardamom Mountains by cooperating with the Ministry of Environment, relevant institutions and local authorities to continue to preserve the forests in Cambodia.
The Deputy Prime Minister stressed that the Royal Government will not provide land in the forest protection and conservation area to any investment company. Not only that, take care of this area, including mountains and slopes, water sources to protect forests and build pagodas. We also have good cooperation with the above two district administrations and the forest administration to protect the forests in these two districts.
