Ministry of Environment Celebrates World Wetlands Day 2021 in Borey Ou Svay Sen Chey District, Stung Treng Province
Stung Treng is a province in the northeast of Cambodia, rich in natural resources, forests, wildlife, minerals, as well as important river systems, has established a major freshwater ecosystem for fish and provides a beautiful landscape. Luxury for attracting national and international tourists.
Stung Treng Province has one Ramsar site, the Ramsar site of Stung Treng Province, which is an internationally important wetland, located 5 km from the provincial town, stretching along the Mekong River from south to north to the border. Laos is rich in flooded forests, an important habitat and a rich food source for mammals, birds, aquatic animals, fish and many other biodiversity.
Mr. Eng Phirong, Director of Stung Treng Provincial Department of Environment, said that the organization of this day is aimed at disseminating awareness related to wetlands and biodiversity to the public.
"The wetland day on February 2 will make spiritual progress by understanding the economic value and benefits of the wetland, as well as loving and protecting the wetland, loving the flooded forest, fish, birds, all kinds of animals," he said. "In this wetland."
On that occasion, leaders, government officials and people also invited to plant trees around Borey O'Svay Sen Chey district hall to protect the environment.
