The fruitful conclusion of the FTA is seen by the Minister of Commerce as positive for the two countries to get together. He said that after the FTA, the trade volume between the two countries will gradually increase.
Mr. Pan Sosak said, "I can not make a specific assessment, but hope that after the Cambodia-Korea Free Trade Agreement will increase the trade volume between the two countries will increase more than now because "In the absence of an FTA, trade volume between the two countries will increase by between 15 percent, except in 2020, in the context of 19 cases of Kovid."
"As Cambodia has more processing, more exports will grow faster, with more than $ 1 billion expected to hit the trade balance soon," he added.
Mr. Pan Sosak said that the potential crops that will be exported include: cashew, pepper, rubber, etc., including the export of rice, cassava. This effort is to make Cambodia an industrial country, not just to sell raw materials.
The agreement will further boost Cambodia's exports to the Republic of Korea on goods previously exported, such as garments and textiles, footwear, bags, spare parts, electronics, rubber and agricultural products. The Republic of Korea can also help boost its exports to Cambodia, including vehicles, electronics, electronics, beverages, pharmaceuticals and plastic products.
Mr. Song Saran, President of the Cambodian Rice Federation, said that after the Cambodia-Korea FTA, the Cambodian Rice Federation will try to contact Korean partners in the rice sector to discuss trade possibilities with each other, study the quality requirements and Korean standard.
He added that in 2020, Cambodia exported only 20 tons of rice to Korea, which is a very small amount. However, the Cambodian Rice Federation will try to learn more about how Cambodia should expand its rice export potential and establish a market with Korea.
He stated that the export of rice is not in the zero tax (0), but the Rice Federation of Cambodia will find ways to get a tax discount. Generally, rice exports to Korea are subject to a 400 percent tax.
Please be informed that the negotiation of the Cambodia-Korea Free Trade Agreement aims to strengthen the economic partnership and expand the liberalization of bilateral trade, mutually beneficial, aimed at enhancing the economic interests and well-being of the people. And the business of the two countries to be even better.
Following the announcement of the formal conclusion of negotiations on the free trade agreement, the two countries will implement domestic procedures for the signing of the bilateral agreement, which is scheduled to take place in mid-2021. UPDATE: Leaders who donate salaries to the Ministry of Health to fight Kovid 19 Phase 2 can reach 803 people
