Ms. Men Sam An recommends 8 points to the officials to carry out the inspection work more effectively
(Phnom Penh): Ms. Kittisangkhab Dr. Men Sam An, Deputy Prime Minister, Minister of National Assembly-Senate Relations and Inspection Closing Ceremony This February 2021, we have made eight recommendations to fulfill our work more effectively.
These eight recommendations include:
* First: Strengthen work discipline and ethics by being present and continuing to work normally by using useful time, such as monitoring information and researching documents to strengthen capacity.
* Second, because the dissemination of the law is necessary, the working group of the Ministry must continue to educate and disseminate the law widely in all 25 capitals and provinces.
* Third: To continue to push for the draft inspection law prepared by the Ministry by continuing to coordinate with the relevant ministries and institutions for this law to be approved.
* Fourth: To continue to implement the online complaint application program and electronic library (e-library), through which those citizens can file complaints and can easily view legal documents and legal documents on computers and mobile phones. The implementation of the program is to facilitate the provision of public services to the people.
* Fifth, to strengthen the effectiveness of the mission to inspect, investigate, investigate complaints and monitor the implementation of the law by finding information in a balanced, clear, evidence and sufficient evidence, both factual and legal. All complaints sent to the relevant authorities for review and investigation must follow up and investigate the information about the progress of the settlement clearly and in a timely manner and then return the information to the plaintiff.
* Sixth: All civil servants in ministries and departments must understand the laws and regulations related to the core work of the Ministry in order to increase the capacity and ability to interpret, explain, discuss and debate in the performance of duties, especially in the work of inspection, complaint handling. Enforce the law and disseminate the law.
* 7th: The National Inspection Institute must strengthen the quality of training, especially to strengthen the capacity of teachers.
