(Phnom Penh): On the evening of February 2, 2021, Lt. Gen. E Sok Khi, Deputy Commissioner General of the National Police, urged all security agencies to continue to participate in disseminating the Royal Government's policy on safe villages, communes and sangkats. Updated 7 points to maintain security and order in society.
On the occasion of the closing ceremony of the 31st Private Security Agency Training, a representative of General Dr. Neth Savoeun, National Police Commissioner, Lt. Gen. Ey Sok Khi added that in addition to promoting the policy of safe villages, communes, private security agencies. You also need to get involved, because private security agencies are also role models in society.
According to Lt. Gen. E Sok Khi, all private security agencies not only work for companies or enterprises, but also play an important role in maintaining security, safety, public order, especially the protection of property and lives of the people. Also.
The Deputy Commissioner of the National Police emphasized that after going through a two-day training course, private security agencies must use the knowledge they have acquired to target for the benefit of society. He said that when performing duties, think that even if you work for a different company or institution, but must be considered as a model citizen by using words, gestures, responses to customers as appropriate. Original.
In addition, General Er Sok Khi considered the role of private security agencies as an important support force to the competent authorities. If they see or suspect any illegal activity, whether in their standing position or where, they must immediately report it to the nearest competent authority or to their area chief or supervisor.
Meanwhile, Lt. Gen. Lim Sokharasmey, Director of the Department of Private Security Management, said that so far, 31 training courses have been conducted by private security agencies, including the Deputy Chief of National Police of the Department of Private Security Management and the Phnom Penh Municipal Police. A total of 113 participants and 5,620 participants.
Lt. Gen. Lim Sokharasmey emphasized that the private security agency training course aims to meet the needs of capacity building to become qualified and qualified private security agents for participation in maintenance and protection activities. Stability, security, safety, order and life of the people, as well as promoting the policy of safe villages, communes and sangkats.
He added that the refresher course consisted of nine instructors from four departments, including the Department of Private Security Management, the Central Department of Judicial Police, the Technical and Scientific Police Department, and the Fire Prevention and Rescue Department.
