(Phnom Penh): Mr. Sok Chenda Sophea, Minister Delegate to the Prime Minister and Secretary General of the Council for Rural Development (CDC), said that Cambodia faces a decline in investment in 2021 and may spread to the next year.
The decline in investment in recent years due to the crisis of Kovid 19 No investors come to study investment, which usually means that before deciding to invest in something, investors always come to study for 2-3 years Years in advance.
Mr. Sok Chenda Sophea said, "According to the United Nations Conference on Trade and Investment, Development has released a report on global investment activities in all regions and countries. Down 42 percent, while the ASEAN region fell 31 percent. Investment in Cambodia decreased by only 12 percent.
He added that, however, for 2020, no investors will come to study and evaluate to invest in 2021 due to the Kovid 19 crisis, which means that if there are investors to invest in Cambodia before coming:
* Must have a medical examination from your home country first. * Arriving in Cambodia, you must do the work for 14 days before leaving to do your work. * After finishing work in Cambodia, you must return to your home country and do the same 14 days. These factors prevent investors from investing.
He added: "For me, investment in 2020 is not a drop in investment because it is something that has been decided before, but investment in 2021-2023 is the result of the study of investors who studied in 2020. "There may be investment in 2021, but if no investors come to study investment in 2020, then in 2021 there will be a decline in investment."
He said that because of this, the CDC is working harder to attract investors. In fact, the CDC has contacted a number of ambassadors from China, Korea, India, Singapore and Japan to discuss investments and plans to meet with ambassadors from other countries.
Please be informed that in 2020, Cambodia received a total of 238 investment projects with a total investment of more than 8,250 million US dollars, down 12 percent compared to the same period in 2019, which had 315 investment projects of 9,397 million US dollars.
