Senior Minister Osman Hassan: Countries in many regions praise Samdech Techo for leading Cambodia to maintain good racial and religious harmony
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Osman Hassan, Senior Minister in Charge of Special Missions and Chairman of the Cambodian Muslim Development Foundation, said that Samdech Techo Hun Sen is a leader of the country, which is considered by many countries as a good role model who has opened his heart. Widely loves the people, regardless of race, religion or political affiliation.
In the distribution ceremony to about 400 families from 3 communes in Russey Keo district at Vihear Thom Kilometer 9 on the evening of February 1, 2021, Senior Minister Osman Hassan emphasized that Samdech Techo always considered people as The same Cambodian blood in all difficulties under all circumstances, the prince never left the people.
On the contrary, the prince has always been careful, especially in the period of the Kovid-19 crisis, as well as in the circumstances where the country was affected by the recent floods, the prince has managed to solve the problem directly by placing Issue effective measures to prevent the spread of Kovid-19 and to rescue people affected by the floods so that no one dies due to ignorance, hearing or no rescue.
The Senior Minister also expressed his pride that Cambodia has good leaders who have managed to lead the country to peace, development in all fields, especially to maintain good harmony between race and religion, make the people live. Unite in peace, there has never been a racial or religious conflict.
He expressed his deep gratitude to Samdech Techo Hun Sen for taking care to support all religions in opening up the right to freedom of religion in accordance with the love and satisfaction of the people in order to preserve and protect the traditions. The tradition that they love to enjoy.
Regarding the current epidemic of Kovid-19, the Senior Minister emphasized that in the world at present, Kovid-19 has not decreased, both in the region and in Cambodia. There is also a risk of Kovid-19, which we still have a series of importers of this disease from outside.
To fight this disease, Senior Minister Osman Hassan took this opportunity to ask people to pay attention to continue to implement three preventive measures on a regular basis: first, wear a mask, second: wash your hands with alcohol or gel. And third, the safety gap must be maintained in accordance with the guidelines of the Ministry of Health.
The gifts distributed to the above 400 families are 20 kg of rice, 1 box of mask and 1 bottle of gel.
