General Him Yan Chairs a Meeting to Disseminate the Social Campaign "Order and Reduce Traffic Accidents"
(Phnom Penh): General Him Yan, Deputy General Commissioner of the National Police, on behalf of General Dr. Neth Savoeun, National Police Commissioner, led a meeting to promote the social campaign "Work, order and reduce traffic accidents" to the 32nd SEA GAME. 2023.
In the dissemination meeting on February 1, 2021 at the General Commission of the National Police, General Him Yan made four recommendations to the leadership of the Traffic Police and Public Order Department and the traffic and order management of the Capital-Provincial Police Commission, including :
* First: The meaning and significance of the 32nd SEA Games 2023
* Second: Events and venues
* Third: The purpose of promoting the social education campaign on "Maintaining order and reducing traffic accidents" towards the 32nd SEA Games 2023
* Fourth: Measures to participate in the dissemination of social education campaigns on "maintaining order and reducing traffic accidents" from now until 2023, including:
Participating in educational campaigns and public order as well as at home in an orderly, aesthetic, safe and hygienic manner, further promoting the enforcement of laws and education on road traffic laws and safety standards. Increase road traffic with transparency and efficiency in order to increase participation in law enforcement and reduce road traffic accidents to a maximum.
Strive to improve road traffic order and participate in resolving traffic congestion, increase the capacity and efficiency of officials, as well as improve professional ethics, increase the technical equipment to operate (security cameras, speed monitors, national monitoring equipment. Drunk and vehicle sound meter).
