Samdech Sar Kheng: If we do not agree, one day drugs will control Cambodia
(Phnom Penh): Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of Interior, expressed concern over the current drug trafficking in Cambodia, which is spreading to rural areas. Samdech Krala Hom said that if they do not agree, one day drugs will control Cambodia.
In commemoration of the 15th International Day of Remembrance for Road Traffic Victims in Kandal Province on Tuesday morning, February 2, 2021, Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng stated that 6 to 10 provinces a day Detect one to two drug offenses.
Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng emphasized, "Concerns, my predictions are not so wrong, there are concerns about drugs spreading to rural areas. Now it is that in one day at least 6 to 10 provinces have one or two cases. "If we do not agree to do this, drugs will control us one day."
The report shows that the drug trafficking situation in Cambodia remains acute and widespread from year to year, with no signs of abating. By 2020, reports show that police forces cracked down on 10,193 drug cases nationwide.
Police seized 3,251 kilograms of drugs, including methamphetamine, amphetamines, cocaine, ketamine and 289 kilograms of marijuana and 287,735 opium, the report said.
The report added that the number of arrests increased by 20 percent compared to the previous year, while drug seizures increased by 17 percent.
