According to the report of the Department of Fire Prevention and Rescue of the Ministry of Interior, there were about 937 fires in 2020, killing 24 people and injuring 36 others.
According to the report, the number of fires in 2020 will increase by 220 cases compared to 2019. 707 houses and 594 stalls and other property were damaged by fire.
Most of these fires were found to be caused by electrical explosions (37.88%) and the use of fire (incense burners) by 32.33%. The other 29.77 percent is under investigation by professional police officers.
Ministry of Environment Supports Ben for Sacrifice to Protect Natural Resources in Phnom Tnaot-Phnom Pok, Preah Vihear Province
(Preah Vihear): Mr. Neth Pheaktra, Secretary of State and Spokesman of the Ministry of Environment, confirmed that the Ministry of Environment and its partner organizations have supported, and the Ministry has provided $ 20,000 per year for five years to Mr. Ben Davis who is living with The family will dedicate their physical and mental strength to the protection and conservation of forest and wildlife resources in the Phnom Tnaot-Phnom Pok wildlife sanctuary in Preah Vihear province.
A spokesman for the Ministry of Environment emphasized that the Ministry of Environment, in particular Mr. Say Sam Al, Minister of the Environment, acknowledged the efforts and encouragement of Mr. Ben Davis and his family to join the Royal Government of Cambodia in conserving natural resources in the area. Phnom Tnaot-Phnom Pok Wildlife Sanctuary.
At the same time, Mr. Neth Pheaktra called on community groups, people to cooperate and agree on the sustainable use of natural resources, because natural resources are our lifeblood. He considers forests as well as wildlife to be very important for human and animal life. At the same time, it is also an attractive tourist destination for boosting the country's economy.
During a visit to Phnom Tnaot-Phnom Pok Wildlife Sanctuary, Ben Davis confirmed that he had volunteered to protect the forest and wildlife at Phnom Tnaot-Phnom Pok Wildlife Sanctuary after seeing This area is already rich in many species of animals.
"Wildlife and forests are very important to all of us, for the people of Cambodia, as well as for tourism," he said. "So I need to come and defend this area."
Faced with countless obstacles and past hardships, the foreigner, who volunteered to protect Cambodia's forests and wildlife, stated: "In the past, I had difficulties, but now "There is the Royal Government of Cambodia, the Ministry of Environment and local authorities to continue to help, and so far it is no longer difficult."
Mr. Ben Davis expressed confidence after the presence of the Ministry of Environment rangers, a coalition of police and gendarmes and community defenders involved in the protection and conservation of natural resources that make up the protection of forests and animals. The forest is in good condition and in the last three to four years, deforestation and hunting and trapping activities have decreased significantly compared to previous years.
Related to tourism in the Phnom Tnaot Phnom Pok Wildlife Sanctuary, the famous foreign wildlife conservationist said that this wildlife sanctuary is rich in many species and the rarest animals in the world. These include raccoons, deer, wild boars, monkeys, peacocks, wild chickens and many more are here.
Meanwhile, Ms. Sarin, the wife of Mr. Ben Davis, said that this place serves food, natural guesthouse for tourists to visit. In the past, many tourists, especially Cambodians, have visited the forest and wildlife in this place.
Ms. Sarin added, "If you come here, please tell me first by phone or Facebook because there is a limited reception. Here can not get too much. I have prepared vegetarian food for them. She also described that in addition to looking at the forest and wildlife, this place also offers a rope ride from the brown mountain down to see the beautiful forest and waterfalls.
Separately, Mr. Chhun Chheng, Deputy Director of the Department of Environment of Preah Vihear Province, stated that education and dissemination of the importance of forests and wildlife to the people is something that can not be overlooked.
He said that the park rangers and in cooperation with the community authorities have jointly protected the forest and wildlife, making the area now rich in wildlife and forests, which in the future will also be an important tourist attraction in Preah Vihear province.
It should be noted that in January 2019, Samdech Kittipritthbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen, President of the Cambodian Red Cross, handed over a car and two motorcycles to Mr. Ben Davis for patrol.
(Phnom Penh): On the morning of February 2, 2021, the Royal Government Spokesperson Unit held a press conference on "Local Progress of Communes, Sangkats and Continuing Work Directions of Kep Province" on the ground floor of the Freedom Hall of the Office of the Council of Ministers. Speakers from Kep Province, led by Mr. Sam Sarin, Chairman of the Provincial Council.
