Announcing the transfer of appointments and equipments to a total of 215 Phnom Penh Police
(Phnom Penh): On the morning of February 2, 2021, the Phnom Penh Municipal Police Commission held a ceremony to announce the transfer of duties, appointments and ranks to National Police officers of the Phnom Penh Municipal Police under the chairmanship of Lt. Gen. Thet, Deputy Commissioner and Phnom Penh Municipal Police Commissioner and Lt. Gen. Hok Thavann, Deputy Director of the Personnel Department, representing General Pen Vibol.
The ceremony was also attended by the Deputy Commissioner of the 14 District Police Inspectorate, as well as many other relevant officials. 85 officers transferred and appointed and 130 ranks, a total of 215 people.
To begin with, Lt. Gen. Hun Sothy, Deputy Commissioner for Human Resource Planning, read out the Prakas of the Ministry of Interior, the decision of the General Commission of the National Police on the transfer of duties, appointments and ranks, and read the order of the Phnom Penh Municipal Police. To the ceremony.
Lt. Gen. Thet and Lt. Gen. Hok Thavann were honored to present the appointment letter to the Deputy Commissioner and to equip many other officials as well.
On that occasion, Major General Horm Vantha, the newly appointed Deputy Commissioner, represented the Deputy Commissioner and all the newly appointed officials in front of the presidency, committing to serve the people. Best.
In conclusion, Lt. Gen. Thet congratulated the Deputy Commissioner and many other officials who have just received the transfer of duties, appointments and promotions, must strive to serve the unit and the people to the best, especially must be received High responsibility to perform duties effectively.
In addition, the General Commissioner advised the fire prevention skills to pay attention to have a clear plan to provide education and training on prevention and prevention of fires to occur eventually.
On the other hand, the Commissioner also instructed the Deputy Commissioners, especially the 14 District Police Inspectors, to cooperate and implement the 7 qualifications of safe villages, communes and sangkats to get the best results. Society, people live in high security.
In addition, the commissioner emphasized that all officers must wear proper uniforms, be clean, respect the discipline of the force, use appropriate words and gestures with the people, and have people on duty to deal with and receive people's complaints on a regular basis. .
