In 2020, the United States ranked Cambodia second in the fight against human trafficking and considered it an injustice for Cambodia, which is working hard to combat human trafficking.
Ranked No. 2 as a country under US surveillance of Cambodia, this means that Cambodia has made little effort to combat human trafficking.
Steve Stuehser made the remarks during a working meeting with National Police Commissioner General Neth Savoeun on the afternoon of February 1, 2021, in order to further strengthen the cooperation between US law enforcement officers and the police. Cambodian nation in the fight against all kinds of transnational crime.
During the meeting, General Dr. Neth Savoeun clarified the legal aspects, experiences and realities, making the US representatives better understand the real situation of Cambodia's efforts to combat human trafficking, especially women. And children.
Through the interpretation of General Dr. Neth Savoeun, the US side has a clear understanding of the real situation of the fight against human trafficking in Cambodia. The US delegation promised to send a clear report to Washington on the real situation of anti-trafficking efforts in Cambodia.
The two sides expressed a common vision to further enhance cooperation by promoting clear information exchanges, including the provision of crime data and the results of the suppression of human trafficking. Co-sponsoring the promotion of human resources, the US side has developed a budget for training programs on investigative skills and the fight against human trafficking through modern technology.
