(Stung Treng): Brigadier General Ieng Vandy, Commander of the Stung Treng Provincial Gendarmerie, on behalf of General Sao Sokha, Deputy Commander of the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces and Commander of the National Gendarmerie, this morning, February 2, 2021. Groundbreaking ceremony for the administrative building of Sesan District Gendarmerie Base.
Currently, the Sesan District Gendarmerie Base is led by Lieutenant Colonel Kim Makara, Acting Commander. Lt. Kim Makara took office less than two months ago, but is eager to contribute to the initiative to build the Sesan District Gendarmerie Base to make it suitable for the Armed Forces. .
The high will of Lieutenant Colonel Kim Makara is to follow the recommendations and instructions of General Sao Sokha, Deputy Commander of the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces and Commander of the National Gendarmerie. Build infrastructure, build buildings, camps, shelters, forts from the national level to the capital-province-city-city-district-khan.
The Sesan District Gendarmerie Base Building, which has just been laid, is 9 meters by 24 meters in size, made of stone, tile, with a demonstration plan, built on an area of 40 meters by 100 meters, and has 4 study rooms. And a meeting hall. The administration building cost more than $ 80,000 to build.
In that, with the support of Mr. Sovann Pisen, the governor of Sesan district, he helped to pour the soil and plan all the windows and doors. Separately, Mr. Chhun Ratha and his wife, a businessman from Stung Treng province, helped build bricks and fences.
