Man Arrested in Banteay Meanchey Province's Malai District, Murderer Arrested
(Banteay Meanchey): The killer who killed an elderly man wearing a military uniform has been arrested by the police, saying that he is a drug addict and the intention to kill the victim is to sell a motorcycle to buy tobacco.
It should be noted that on the morning of February 1, 2021, in Banteay Ty village, O'Tompot commune, Malai district, Banteay Meanchey province, a murder occurred when an elderly man wearing a military uniform was beaten with a stick by a stranger, causing serious injuries. He died at the hospital.
According to the local police, the victim was named Rong Roeung, 61 years old, living in Banteay Ty village, O'Tom page commune, Malai district. Local authorities said that in the morning, residents found the victim was beaten up, lying unconscious on the spot, while residents also helped to transport to the hospital to save lives due to the beating. The victim died of his injuries.
After the murder, Banteay Meanchey Provincial Police Commissioner Major General Sithi Loh issued an order for the competent authorities to arrest the killer. This evening, Malai police arrested the killer in Malai district.
After the confession, the suspect was sent to the provincial police commission to prepare a case to be sent to court for legal action. Embassy of India - Ministry of Women's Affairs builds two school buildings at Kambol Primary School
(Phnom Penh): Ms. Ing Kantha Phavi, Minister of Women's Affairs, and Ms. Tevy Nyi Cobragade, Ambassador of India to Cambodia, on February 1, 2021, signed a Memorandum of Understanding (MoU) for the construction of a three-room school building for Grade 1 students. 1 to 3 and 4 to 6 students at Kambol Primary School in Sangkat Kambol, Khan Kambol under the QIP of the two governments.
Ms. Ing Kantha Phavi reminded the cooperation between the Ministry of Women's Affairs and the Embassy of India in Phnom Penh in the implementation of various QIP projects by the Ministry of Women's Affairs, including the project to promote the empowerment of women through information and communication technology (ICT). To students, especially girls, and improve their learning conditions through the construction of new toilets and classrooms.
The Minister said that the purpose of this cooperation is in line with the common goal of the national strategy and national plan to provide universal education to ensure the participation and equality of all children in Cambodia.
Project types under QIP include the construction of physical infrastructure, such as roads, community centers, local water resources management, and social infrastructure (including capacity building) such as education, health, hygiene, welfare, rural children, gender equality development, or targeted community development. Sustainable Development (SDGs).
Cambodian-Chinese Officials Jointly Distribute Book "His Excellency Xi Jinping: Governance of China" Part 3 to Banteay Meanchey Province
On April 10, 2017, the first part of the book "His Excellency Xi Jinping, Governance of China" in Khmer was officially released at the Peace Palace under the presidency of Samdech Techo Hun Sen. The Prime Minister of Cambodia presented the contents of this book not only for the benefit of the scholars, but also for the practical experience of the leaders of the country.
The book China Governance, which is published continuously, especially in the third volume, is presented to the public to share China's knowledge and experience of various developments to the world to better understand China's development. This book will also be useful and be a beacon to participate in promoting exchanges, learning from each other for common prosperity as a community of common destiny.
Consul General Liu Jiecha supported the National University of Meanchey, the Chinese Cultural Center of Cambodia and the Cambodian Association of Progress Researchers, which organized today's event in the spirit of increasing the provision and sharing of Buddhist knowledge from China to officials. Government officials, researchers and students in Banteay Meanchey province have been able to absorb and learn more about China's progress over the past 72 years, especially poverty reduction.
Since 2013, Cambodia under the leadership of Samdech Techo Hun Sen has been active in joining China in implementing the Belt and Road Strategy in order to achieve a common community of common destiny for greater benefits. To the nations of our two countries.
In addition, she encouraged the ceremony to take the book "His Excellency Xi Jinping on Chinese Governance" Part 3 and strive to refine good ideas as an element to strengthen good governance in line with the situation and Cambodian Socio-Economic Development Equipment.
International Analysis: Promoting the Establishment of a Unified Community of Humans on the basis of Multilateralism
Moon Jae-in, the three presidents of South Korea, said that now is the time to re-adhere to multilateralism and the spirit of the whole global environment, the need to strengthen solidarity and cooperation.
Mr. Chea Monirith, Director of the Planning and Project Department of the Cambodian Civil Society Forum, said that China has actively initiated and implemented the principles of multilateralism and called for the facilitation of relations between countries through regimes and rules. This shows respect and protection for the common values of all mankind: peace, development, truth, justice, democracy and freedom.
Promoting the creation of a common destiny of mankind on the basis of multilateralism requires that countries should respect each other's sovereignty and core interests, manage differences through dialogue, and resolve issues through dialogue.
Countries should adhere to the principles of mutual benefit and win-win, engage in positive competition on the basis of truth and justice, and reject narrow, self-serving policies and protectionist practices. Give countries equal rights to develop and promote the international community to develop and prosper together.
In particular, developed countries should respectfully adhere to all multilateral conventions and agreements on environmental protection, while developing countries also have to fulfill their responsibilities without harming the environment for economic gain. Short-term.
It should be noted that whether to counter the current crisis, such as the spread of COVID-19, or to address the long-term challenges facing the international community, such as peace and development, the promotion of a common destiny One of humanity on the basis of multilateralism is the only way out.
