(Phnom Penh): Australia has expressed its support for Cambodia in hosting the 13th Asia-Europe Meeting (ASEM) in mid-2021 and its chairmanship of ASEAN in 2022. This is according to the press release of the Ministry of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation on the results of the second Cambodia-Australia Senior Ministerial Consultation on January 28, 2021 via video.
The second Cambodia-Australia Senior Ministerial Consultation was chaired by Ms. Soeung Rathavi, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Foreign Affairs of Cambodia, and Mr. Justin Hayhurst, Undersecretary of State of the Ministry of Foreign Affairs and Trade of Australia.
The two sides exchanged views on the progress of Cambodia-Australia cooperation in bilateral, regional and international frameworks, as well as global common concerns in the fight against the epidemic and its devastating effects. 19.
The Australian side expressed its joint desire with Cambodia to strengthen and expand cooperation and mutual support in the regional and international framework, including ASEAN, the Asia-Europe Meeting, the United Nations and the Mekong Sub-Region Cooperation to participate. Maintain peace, security and sustainable development.
In addition, "Australia reaffirms its support for Cambodia in hosting the 13th Asia-Europe Summit in 2021 and Cambodia's ASEAN Chairmanship in 2022." This is according to the announcement of the Ministry of Foreign Affairs of Cambodia.
It should be noted that Cambodia originally planned to hold the 13th Asia-Europe Summit on 16-17 November 2020, but due to the outbreak of Kovid 19, the Royal Government of Cambodia also proposed to postpone the big meeting. This is back in the middle of 2021. The Senior Officials in charge of Asia-Europe Affairs expressed their unanimous understanding and unanimous support for Cambodia's request to postpone the 13th Asia-Europe Summit.
