The Prime Minister of Cambodia, Samdech Techo, stated that the lack of water supply capacity of the Phnom Penh Water Supply Authority has caused about 40,000 families in Phnom Penh, equivalent to 12 percent, to face water shortages in the dry season of 2020 and 2021. .
During the groundbreaking ceremony for the construction of the Bak Kheng Water Treatment Plant and the inauguration of the Chamkar Mon Water Treatment Plant on February 1, 2021, Samdech Techo Hun Sen reminded that the policy of water, road, electricity and human resources is a policy. Which Samdech set out when he went on a trip to negotiate peace in France in 1987.
In this sense, Samdech Techo wants to show the Cambodian people that water policy is a priority policy that Samdech has considered since the country was just liberated from the genocidal regime. From the forum to inaugurate achievements and create achievements for clean water in Phnom Penh, Samdech Techo also reminded about the water situation in Phnom Penh after the liberation on January 7, 1979.
Samdech Techo reminded that Phnom Penh at that time did not have water like today. Even Samdech, like other leaders, had to bring water from the river to use. Samdech's house at the Independence Monument did not have clean water until 1994.
Regarding the history of clean water in Phnom Penh, Samdech Techo reminded that Samdech's wife, Samdech Kittipritthbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen, broke an unborn child because he took water up to his house when Samdech went to work as a minister. Foreign affairs at that time.
However, Samdech Techo Prime Minister wants to see the water supply network in Phnom Penh continue to expand to meet the needs of the people in Phnom Penh, which is growing rapidly. In this regard, Samdech Techo asked the French Vinci team to speed up the construction of the Bak Kheng water treatment plant as soon as planned in 2022.
In this spirit, the Water Supply Authority has expanded the construction of the Chamkar Mon Water Treatment Plant with a capacity of 52,000 cubic meters per day, including the establishment of a water distribution network. The plant was built by French company Vinci for 24 months, completed in October 2019. The factory has a total investment of 47.1 million US dollars.
Of that, the budget for the construction of the water treatment plant was $ 25.2 million and for the distribution network was $ 21.9 million. The water plant can supply water to an additional 280,000 people.
The second phase has a production capacity of 195,000 cubic meters, equivalent to the first phase and is scheduled to start in the third quarter of 2021. Implement the 30-month project, scheduled to be completed by the end of 2023. At a cost of approximately $ 134.4 million.
Senior Minister Cham Prasidh claimed that after the completion of the two-stage construction of the Bak Kheng water treatment plant, it will have the capacity to produce up to 390,000 cubic meters of water per day by the end of 2023. After the completion of this project, Phnom Penh Water Supply Authority will be able to supply water to an additional 1.4 million people and have the capacity to produce a total of 1 million cubic meters of clean water per day.
The Senior Minister also said that in response to the expansion of water production capacity 2018-2025, the Royal Government has allowed the Phnom Penh Water Supply Authority to receive about 30 million from Japan to build a water treatment plant in Takhmao City to produce 30,000 water. Cubic meters per day and the budget from the Czech Republic 1.3 million Europe to build a water treatment plant in Sangkat Boeung Thom, Khan Kambol, with a capacity of 5,000 cubic meters per day.
In addition, the Royal Government has prepared 2 hectares of land in the Koh Nora development area for the purpose of establishing a water treatment plant on the island and expanding the water supply to other areas. Not only that, in June 2017, Samdech Techo provided the principle of having another 25 hectares of reserved land in Boeung Ta Mok area to serve the water supply sector.
Mr. Cham Prasidh said that according to the forecast by 2030, the number of people using water in Phnom Penh could reach 4 million.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen urged the Ministry of Industry, Science, Technology and Innovation as well as the Phnom Penh Water Supply Authority to continue to pay attention to the production and connection of clean water in Phnom Penh. Samdech Techo Hun Sen affirmed that the priority policies of water, roads, electricity and human resources that he set out for the next 50 years will still have an effect on social development.
For ministries, state institutions and embassies do not limit the amount used, but the price is 2,500 riel per cubic meter. Spokesman of the General Commission: On February 1, 2021, another 749 vehicles were inspected and fined
Please note that for February 1, 2021, traffic accidents throughout Cambodia also occurred 5 times, in which 3 people died and 4 people were injured (3 people were seriously injured).
(Preah Vihear): Mr. Net Pheaktra, Secretary of State and spokesman for the Ministry of Environment, confirmed that a group of experts led by the Ministry of Environment has decided to select the Phnom Tbeng Natural Heritage Site to be included in the UNESCO World Heritage List.
Phnom Tbeng Natural Heritage Site is one of four natural sites: Prek Kampi, Prek Prasop Wildlife Sanctuary, Thmei Bei Thoeun Krasang Nature Reserve, which was previously approved by the Ministry of Environment. The inter-ministerial study was conducted to compile a list of documents to be prepared for submission to the UNESCO World Heritage List.
"I would like to point out that out of the four sites that the Ministry of Environment, including the inter-ministerial organization, has submitted to the UNESCO for a list of World Heritage Sites," said Neth Pheaktra. He, an expert, agreed to select Phnom Tbeng Natural Heritage Site as a UNESCO World Heritage Site.
At the same time, Mr. Neth Pheaktra stated that there are three main reasons why experts select Phnom Tbeng to be included in the World Heritage List, including:
* First: It is a place of worship from the beginning until now, it is a sacred place with beliefs, culture, traditions and customs * Second: It has the potential of natural resources, biodiversity, rare species such as triggers, deer, bears and wood Many attractions and potential tourist destinations, etc. * Third: It is an important potential tourist destination for the three communities around Phnom Tbeng.
Mr. Neth Pheaktra emphasized: "So far, the technicians have compiled some documents and are continuing to study in the Phnom Tbeng Natural Heritage Area to prepare all the documents. And complete to apply for inclusion in the UNESCO World Heritage List.
Mr. Net Pheaktra said that Phnom Tbeng Natural Heritage Site is a natural tourist destination with beautiful waterfalls and also a safe haven for rare animals, while today Phnom Tbeng Natural Heritage Area is becoming A popular and famous resort for Vihear province and popular with national and international tourists.
It should be noted that Phnom Tbeng Natural Heritage Area was established on September 13, 2016 by the Royal Government of Cambodia at the request of the Minister of Environment. The four districts are Sangkum Thmey, Kulen, Rovieng and Preah Vihear.
This heritage site is unique in its natural beauty, the waterfall has three stages from the top to the foot of the mountain and the view of the banana plantations of the people along the road to Phnom Tbeng, which is about 400 meters high, which travelers must Cross the 1,380 steps. Not only that, Phnom Tbeng is a historical site where Cambodians worship those shrines, including three stones.
Nowadays, Phnom Tbeng Heritage Site has become a tourist attraction, especially for young people to enjoy weekends or holidays with group and family tents. Vong Soth Belly and cash support for poor families perform well for 2020
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Vong Soth, Minister of Social Affairs, Veterans and Youth Rehabilitation, assessed that the social protection program, including the cash support program for pregnant women and children under 2 years old and the cash support program for poor families, performed well for the year. 2020 ago.
The Minister confirmed that the meat subsidy program for pregnant women and children under 2 years old started in June 2019, as of January 19, 2021, only recently, there are pregnant women and children. More than 170,000 people have benefited from this program, with a total budget of about $ 10 million from the government.
Three rounds of cash support programs for poor families have already been implemented, with the Royal Government spending more than $ 200 million in the past three rounds. Currently, the Royal Government is also continuing to provide cash support in the fourth round, which will last for three months from January to March 2021. This was further confirmed by Mr. Vong Soth, Ministry of Social Affairs, Veterans and Youth Rehabilitation.
For cash support to poor families in January 2021, there are more than 710,000 poor families with more than 2.8 million members and plan to spend more than 32 million dollars.
