Crack down on illegal wood processing handicrafts in Kulen district, confiscate luxury wood and some materials
(Preah Vihear): An illegal wood processing handicraft site in Phsar Thmei village, Srayong commune, Kulen district, Preah Vihear province was cracked down and confiscated under the direct command of Mr. Vuth Savy, Deputy Prosecutor of Preah Vihear Provincial Prosecutor's Office. A large number of exhibits are sent to be handled according to the law.
Mr. Vuth Savy stated on February 1, 2021 that under the coordination and guidance of Mr. Ty Sovinthal, Prosecutor of the Preah Vihear Provincial Prosecutor's Office, this afternoon, he led the force of the judiciary. The Forestry Administration raided an illegal wood processing handicraft site at the above location.
As a result, the police confiscated several cubic meters of bulldozers, drill motors, bulldozers and all kinds of Beng Thnong rosewood and sent them to be stored at the Forestry Administration for legal action.
Mr. Vuth Savy stated that one of the illegal wood processing handicrafts that was cracked down on had a lot of wood. All. As he led the force down, no merchants claimed to belong to him, so the exhibits and various types of wood were confiscated in accordance with the law.
Mr. Vuth Savy stressed that any wood processing site without a proper permit must be cracked down on, as well as other illegal gambling sites, regardless of their background. He also called on people to do business in accordance with the law, in general, all business locations must have a law.
