On the 35th floor can be found a beautiful courtyard on the roof of the Sky Villa. This open space creates an attractive atmosphere for harmonious city life. This place is the best choice for those who want to have a private courtyard in the air with a view of the growing city.
Sky Villa has 256 units and 8 types, all of which are luxury units that are ideal for the aristocracy and the modern family. The apartments range in size from 272 square meters to 509 square meters, a unique luxury development project in the city. All the units are modern and stylish, and the size of the house is as big as a villa, which allows enough light to make the living comfortable.
If you want to live in a busy city but still be able to enjoy the quiet, a well-thought-out room design is essential. Sky Villa uses double-layer sound insulation glass that can block 90% of the noise to the living room and living room.
The apartment type of Sky Villa project is designed with more than 2 rooms. Both the master bedroom and the second bedroom have ample space that allows for safe use of the space. The bedroom can easily accommodate a large bed that is more than 2 meters long and does not make the room cramped. There is also a locker room and closet for all residents of Sky Villa.
When it comes to the kitchen, there are two rows of layouts for the most convenient refrigerator location. The luggage compartment is clean and there is enough space for a table that can seat 4-6 people. No matter what the occasion, Sky Villa's kitchen area allows you to enjoy a meal together.
Sky Villa has a four-storey underground car park, a secure passageway for entry and 24-hour surveillance to protect the home. Secure each home with three popular and modern unlocking methods: PIN + Swipe card + key and is equipped with full video internet as an additional security measure. Australia unveils plans to vaccinate Kovid-19 nationwide no later than October 2021
