(Banteay Meanchey): 25 live pigs transported by truck from Thailand without proper documents were arrested by the Director General of the General Department of Animal Health and Animal Production on January 31, 2021 at Te Haing Road, Kork Roka Village, Tapen Commune, Svay Chek District. Banteay Meanchey Province.
The crackdown was ordered by Mr. Tan Phannara, Royal Government of Cambodia Delegate in charge of the Director General of the General Department of Animal Health and Animal Production, and coordinated by Mr. Meas Chanpiseth, Prosecutor of the Banteay Meanchey Provincial Prosecutor's Office.
After receiving the order of the Intervention Team to Suppress Animal Movement Crimes of the General Department of Animal Health and Animal Production, in cooperation with the Production and Veterinary Office of the Banteay Meanchey Provincial Department of Agriculture and the Svay Chek District Inspectorate, intercepted a white Ssangyong vehicle. 15-seater passenger car with license plate Phnom Penh 2AH-1047.
According to the answer of the owner of the truck transporting pigs and according to the explanation from the professional officer of the Production and Veterinary Office of Banteay Meanchey Province, the truck was transporting live pigs from Thailand through Area 1 in Chak Puok Village, Slor Kram Commune, Svay Chek District, Banteay Meanchey Province. Delivered to distribute in some provinces without any permit.
Currently, the team has brought all the exhibits to be stored at the animal sanctuary of the General Department of Animal Health and Animal Production for processing.
