The five oil wells in the Apsara region are expected to be operational in 2021 and are estimated to receive more than 7,000 barrels per day, which is still small. Although this amount is small, Samdech Techo said it was a good start to the oil and gas industry in Cambodia.
Samdech Techo made this statement on the occasion of opening the construction site of Bak Kheng Water Treatment Plant and the inauguration ceremony of Chamkar Mon Water Treatment Plant on the morning of February 1, 2021.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that the first well has been operating for 33 days, producing 1,236 barrels per day, for a total of 33 days, producing 40,788 barrels. The second well, which started operating on January 30, 2021, is in the phase of separating oil and gas.
Samdech Techo stated that so far, Cambodia has only received 4,156 barrels of crude oil, the remaining 3, 4 and 5 wells will continue to drill and pump oil in 2021, according to estimates. Cambodia will receive only 7,000 to 7,500 barrels of oil per day, which is still small and has no economic impact.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen said, "Although Cambodia's oil pumping is small and has not yet had an economic impact, it is a good start to the process of the oil and gas industry in Cambodia. We will continue with the investment team. Others.
