The Ministry of Public Works provides more modern services, Mr. Sun Chanthol asked people to come to the service directly, do not rely on others to lose money
(Phnom Penh): Senior Minister Sun Chanthol, Minister of Public Works and Transport, requested all people to seek services under the authority of the Ministry of Public Works and Transport directly, do not rely on others (brokers), which leads to financial loss.
Senior Minister Sun Chanthol's call came as he led several journalists to visit and present the Ministry of Public Works and the Techo Sen Institute of Public Works and Transport last week.
In addition to presenting Cambodia's first road and bridge building training institute and training institute building, the US Harvard Minister also took reporters to visit his public service center.
This service includes: Vehicle Registration Service, Vehicle Technical Inspection, Driver's License Application, Inland Waterway and Port Transport License Application and Country Freight Business License Application. Original.
Just entering the Ministry's public service center surprised the media with the modernization of the ministry's services, which is not inferior to the services provided in the private sector business. Upon entering this center, visitors to the service can click on the number according to the service they go to. Then they have to sit and wait for their numbers. When your number reaches a service, the number will be displayed on a screen and there will be a voice call.
On the shirt of each service officer is affixed a name. At this point, the Senior Minister said that people who go to the service, if any service providers use awkward gestures or charge excessive fees, etc. can call to report this abnormal case immediately.
In this center, a slogan that reads "Officials are slaves of the people, not the masters of the people" is displayed prominently in front of service officials.
Senior Minister Sun Chanthol said that this arrangement is to help provide services to the people faster and faster and eliminate inactivity.
Reform of the provision of public services is a policy that the Royal Government of Cambodia under the leadership of Samdech Techo Hun Sen has focused on and is working on very carefully.
Despite the Royal Government's efforts, the provision of public services has not improved. The Ministry of Public Works and Transport (MPWT) has noted a number of reforms in the provision of public services under its jurisdiction.
Senior Minister Sun Chanthol, after joining the Ministry of Public Works and Transport in 2016, has led many reforms in the provision of this service. In addition to building an automated system that allows people to access services online, Mr. Sun Chanthol has set up three shopping malls in Phnom Penh, including: Aeon Mall 1, Aeon Mall Second and Chip Mong's Noromol Mall.
Senior Minister Sun Chanthol said that providing fast and transparent services to the people is a big goal of Samdech Techo Hun Sen. Therefore, what he strives to reform this service is to comply with the recommendations of the Prime Minister and to give confidence as well as the trust of the people on the Royal Government of Cambodia.
