"Solar" saves the new building of the Ministry of Public Works more than 30,000 dollars per month
(Phnom Penh): The new office building of the Ministry of Public Works and Transport as well as the "Techo Sen Public Works and Transport" institute building were built by Senior Minister Sun Chanthol with "solar" power to generate electricity for use in the building. .
On the occasion of inviting journalists to inspect the achievements of the Ministry's new building on Street 598 in Sangkat Chrang Chamres 2, Khan Russey Keo last weekend, Senior Minister Sun Chanthol, Minister of Public Works and Transport, said that the installation of "solar" power. This makes the Ministry earn more than $ 1,000 per day in electricity bills.
The presence of the Ministry of Public Works and Transport building also received some criticism when it was first completed by a group of architects. Lovers of architecture have criticized the ministry for building a lack of emphasis on Khmer-style designs.
The "solar" system not only saves energy, but also saves the planet and depletes the ozone layer. Environmentalists have encouraged the use of clean energy, such as the "solar" system, to reduce global warming.
The Ministry of Public Works and Transport is the first ministry in Cambodia to use the "solar" system for energy extraction. This is seen in line with the Royal Government of Cambodia's policy of saving and reducing national budget expenditures.
Journalists invited to visit the ministry were shocked and shocked to hear that the "solar" system was saving the ministry more than $ 30,000 a month.
It should be noted that the new office building of the Ministry of Public Works and Transport and the Institute of "Techo Sen Public Works and Transport" at the same location was officially inaugurated under the presidency of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia on January 22. 2021 ago.
The new office building of the Ministry of Public Works and Transport is built on an area of nearly 4 hectares. This building includes: 9-storey administrative building, 2 administrative buildings (double wing building), 8-storey high, a meeting hall building and a 3-storey library. The building is equipped with office equipment, furniture and elevator and connected with modern technology to serve work and meetings.
The building also has a library for research officers, a room for various programs and a place for officials to relax. In the new ministry location, there is a collection of various services under the authority of the Ministry that is modern and fast.
During the inauguration of the Ministry building, Samdech Techo Hun Sen praised the achievements of the Ministry. Samdech Techo also expressed his pleasure that the Ministry established the first training institute on road and bridge construction skills.
Officials: Institute of Science and Technology of Cambodia helps border students get higher education and knowledge
(Oddar Meanchey): The Institute of Science and Technology of Cambodia, Oddar Meanchey branch is assessed as contributing significantly to providing knowledge and skills to the children of the people on the Cambodian-Thai border.
At the opening ceremony of the new school year of the Institute of Science and Technology of Cambodia on the morning of January 31, 2021, Ms. Heng Socheat, Deputy Governor of Samrong City, said that Oddar Meanchey is a province far from Phnom Penh. Therefore, it is an obstacle for the education of the children of the people in this province after they graduate from general education.
According to Ms. Heng Socheat, despite the efforts to promote and promote education, some students still decide to drop out of higher education due to lack of ability to continue their studies in Phnom Penh.
For the Deputy Mayor, the presence of the Institute of Science and Technology of Cambodia in Oddar Meanchey has contributed greatly to the education of the people in Oddar Meanchey to get a higher education.
"Science and Technology of Cambodia, Oddar Meanchey Branch is promoting students to get real quality knowledge and skills from teachers who are professors," she said. In particular, also helped reduce the cost of students in the province.
The Deputy Director of the Institute said that the Institute provides real professional skills and clear research with quality, sufficient capacity to contribute to the promotion of education, economy, living, national prestige through education and cooperation on the national and international stage. Based on the principles of peace, good governance and basic non-violence.
Please note that the Institute of Science and Technology of Cambodia, Oddar Meanchey Branch is located in Chhouk Village, Sangkat Samrong, Samrong City, Oddar Meanchey Province. There are 4 training institutes: Master's Degree, Bachelor's Degree, Associate's Degree and Technical and Vocational Degree with 6 majors: Public Administration, Business Administration, Information Technology, Public Administration, Marketing, Banking and Finance.
Currently, the institute has a total of more than 1,000 students.
