One person was killed and five others were missing Sunday as a tropical cyclone hit Fiji for the second time in a month. This is according to the release by CNA on Sunday, January 31, 2021.
Cyclone Ana hit Fiji with winds of 140 km per hour, bringing heavy rains and flooding. A 49-year-old man drowned, four fishermen and a 3-year-old boy are missing, and more than 7,600 people have been evacuated from their villages, according to Fiji Disaster Management Authority. They flooded the temporary accommodation provided by the state.
In December 2020, four people were killed and 23,000 were displaced after Cyclone Yasa hit Fiji at speeds of up to 345 kilometers per hour.
Pailin Governor Sends Worker to Return Home After Coverage 19
(Pailin): The Governor of Pailin Province, Ms. Ban Srey Mom, paid a personal visit to 19 Kovid patients when they were cured of Kovid 19 disease. This gesture was highly appreciated and enjoyed by the patients because it shows the attention of the provincial leaders to the people.
While sending patients home on the morning of January 31, 2021, Ms. Ban Srey Mom brought the congratulations of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia to the patients from the hospital. On behalf of her, she also expressed her happiness and instructed the patient to continue to have sedation for another 14 days at home, and if there are any changes, contact a doctor immediately.
She also advised 19 newly treated Kovid patients not to forget to take their medication regularly as prescribed by their doctor. The provincial governor also praised and thanked the team of doctors who worked hard day and night to take care of patients until they recover.
Ms. Ban Srey Mom further confirmed to the newly treated patients that during the treatment and accommodation phase, it is the attention of Samdech Techo Hun Sen and Samdech Kittipritthbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen, without leaving any Cambodian workers. Suffering from the Kovid 19 virus unknowingly and unresolved.
She added that the two princes had assigned the Ministry of Health and a team of medical experts to do this work as a front line, then forces and local authorities to fight and prevent the spread of this vicious virus into the local.
She also asked the patient, if there are any relatives who have to return to their hometown, to provide true information to the security forces and medical teams and to volunteer for 14 days.
Kampong Speu Provincial Governor: White Shirt Army Frontline Fighters Against Kovid 19
(Kampong Speu): The Governor of Kampong Speu Province, Mr. Vy Samnang, evaluated and admired the team of doctors who fight against Kovid 19 disease. The governor called 19 Kovid fighters on the front lines to help protect people from the deadly disease.
Mr. Vy Samnang said this during the groundbreaking ceremony for Damnak Damrey Health Center in Treng Trayeung commune, Phnom Sruoch district in front of about 300 government officials and people on January 30, 2021.
On that occasion, Mr. Vy Samnang said that the health sector has been accused of being weak in treating people. On the contrary, when the 19-disease Kovid disease occurred, it highlighted the important role of the medical team, demonstrating the vital involvement of the medical team in the fight against the disease.
The provincial governor said, "Our doctors are nicknamed the White Shirts because in the battle with Kovid 19, the shadowless enemy, they are the bravest front-line fighters." For the health of our people, they have sacrificed their happiness away from their families without hesitation.
On that occasion, the provincial governor also highlighted Cambodia's success in combating and preventing Kovid 19 under the skillful leadership of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia. He said that Samdech Techo has set out a plan for the Ministry of Health and relevant authorities in all areas to try to take samples from people who are suspicious and to treat and treat patients to prevent the spread and spread to the community.
The Governor emphasized that on behalf of the Provincial Council, the Board of Governors and on behalf of the Royal Government of Cambodia, he would like to commend all Cambodians who have listened to the instructions of the Ministry of Health and the appeal of the Royal Government of Cambodia. There were no deaths or new infections in the community.
