Myanmar military claims to 'respect and defend 2008 constitution' amid coup concerns
Rangoon: The Myanmar military on Saturday announced that it supports and respects the constitution and will do everything in accordance with the law. The remarks are seen as easing concerns over rumors that the military could stage a coup to overthrow the newly elected government following allegations of voter fraud. This is according to the release by CNA on Saturday afternoon, January 30, 2021.
Myanmar's military statement came just one day after UN Secretary-General Antonio Guterres and Western embassies in the Union of Myanmar issued statements. It expressed concern over the post-election tense situation in Myanmar and, in particular, the possibility of a military coup.
Aung San Suu Kyi's National League for Democracy (NLD) party called the Myanmar military statement "a reasonable explanation". The NLD has in the past called for the Myanmar military to remain an institution that recognizes the aspirations of the people through the election results.
