Lt. Gen. Hun Manet: When there is peace, the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces plays an important role in saving the people and participating in the development of the country
During the inspection of the two road construction sites at the above location, Mr. HUN Manet stated that while the country is completely peaceful, the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces has played an important role in rescuing the people and participating in the development of the country. Progress.
Lt. Gen. Hun Manet also praised and appreciated the leadership of officers, deputies and soldiers in the Army Engineering Command for their efforts to rebuild the roads damaged by the floods for the people to travel. Easy.
Lt. Gen. Hun Manet urged the Army Engineering Force to continue its efforts to build the road technically correct, ensuring both quantity, quality and aesthetics.
According to the report of Lt. Gen. Ouch Vantha, Deputy Commander of the Army and Commander of the Engineering Command, the construction of the 9,300-meter-long red paved road in Kut Sot commune, Ochrov district, was completed by the Army Engineering Force. The Army led the force and machinery to complete the task on December 22, 2020 and is scheduled to end on March 15, 2021.
The Army Engineering Corps used a total of 17 vehicles. As a result, the work to date has been clearing and transporting gravel for a total length of 3,601 meters on a total distance of 9,300 meters. In addition, the engineering force has been grinding red stones for a total length of 1,800 meters.
After inspecting the construction site in Kut Sot commune, Ochrov district, Banteay Meanchey province, in the evening of the same day, Mr. HUN Manet and his accompanying delegation continued to inspect the road construction site which was damaged by the flood. In Slor Kram commune, Svay Chek district, Banteay Chey province.
As a result, the Army Engineering Corps achieved the construction of a road in Slor Kram commune, Svay Chek district, and the overall evaluation achieved 60%.
It should be noted that on January 29, 2021, Lt. Gen. Hun Manet, accompanied by the Deputy Commander of the Army and many other senior officers of the Army, inspected the road construction site of the Army Engineering Corps. The mainland, which is constructing a 9,300-meter-long red paved road, is located in Kut Sot commune, O'Chrov district, Banteay Meanchey province.
