Mr. Moeng Ponlok announces the appointment and inauguration of the Cambodian Youth Movement Association (Group 157), Kampong Chhnang Branch
The ceremony was held in the presence of Mr. Moeng Ponlok, President of the Cambodian Youth Movement Association (Group 157), Mr. Lux Sovannara, Member of Kampong Chhnang Provincial Council and represented by Mr. Long Chhun Lay, Chairman of Kampong Chhnang Provincial Council and Mr. Sun Sovannarith, Representative of Mr. Chhour Chandoeun, Governor of Kampong Chhnang Province. The program also distributes gifts to the elderly and many poor families.
Speaking on the occasion, Mr. Moeung Ponlok stated that the establishment of the Cambodian Youth Movement Association 157 is for the purpose of youth movement in all areas to help people affected by disasters, help the disabled, help the elderly, regardless of political affiliation, race and color. In order to join the Royal Government in maintaining peace, the nation must develop.
He said that there is peace, there is everything today, if there is no peace, not even all kinds of rights and freedoms. Therefore, on behalf of the Cambodian youth, we must join the youth movement to protect the peace together.
He added that as of today, the Cambodian Youth Movement Association 157 has been established in 14 provinces, including branches in Kampong Chhnang today. In the past, our association has helped people affected by floods in some provinces, and last year in Siem Reap, our association also organized a youth movement in Siem Reap to ride a bicycle together to raise more than 8 Ten thousand dollars to support Kantha Bopha Hospital as well.
At the same time, 12 years ago, when the country was at war on the Cambodian-Thai border, our Cambodian Youth Movement Association also mobilized young people across the country and other institutions to jointly support the fighters on the front lines to make the defense of the motherland. Our fighters succeeded against the enemies who tried to occupy the territory of the temple of Preah Vihear, which is the heritage of the Khmer ancestors.
Separately, Mr. Sun Sovannarith, Deputy Governor of Kampong Chhnang, who presided over the ceremony, said that in Kampong Chhnang, there are more than 100 associations with a total of more than 30,000 families, and in the future, all associations in the province and expand members. To raise 200,000 families to improve his livelihood at the grassroots level.
He called on all local authorities in the province to cooperate with the Cambodian Youth Movement Association 157 and all communities in the province to jointly develop our base to be successful and to keep the peace together, because if there is peace There is development in all areas.
