Ministry of Foreign Affairs: European Strategy for Development Cooperation with Cambodia 2021-2027 focuses on three areas
(Phnom Penh): The European Strategy for Development Cooperation with Cambodia 2021-2027 focuses on three areas: economic growth and job creation, agriculture and natural resource management, with a focus on fisheries and governance, and the rule of law.
This is according to the press release of the Ministry of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation on the meeting between Deputy Prime Minister Prak Sokhon, Minister of Foreign Affairs and Mrs. Carmen Moreno, Ambassador of the European Union to Cambodia, which took place on Thursday morning, January 28, 2021. At the Ministry of Foreign Affairs.
The Deputy Prime Minister thanked the European Union for its development assistance to Cambodia, which has been implemented both under the bilateral framework and jointly with European countries and has made a significant contribution to Cambodia's socio-economic development over the past two years. A decade and a half ago. He welcomed the initial consultation, which aims to improve EU development activities.
The Deputy Prime Minister also expressed his anticipation for the completion of the EU Strategy for Development Cooperation for Cambodia 2021-2027.
