Gifts of Samdech Techo Hun Sen and Samdech Kittipritthbandit were handed over by Mr. Seng Teang to the 372 twins in Por Sen Snay village, Kampong Thom province.
(Kampong Thom): Mr. Seng Teang, Personal Assistant to Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, and Mrs. They were the grandchildren of Samdech Techo and Samdech Kittipritthbandit to the residence of the family of three twins in Po Sen Snay village, Srayov commune, Sen Chey city, Kampong Thom province.
Those generous donations include 5 million riels, 50 kilograms of rice, 2 large boxes of milk, 5 kilograms of sugar, 2 sarongs and 2 scarves.
The three twin grandchildren are the second children of a 32-year-old father, Run Bunthoeun, a military officer, and a 28-year-old mother, Tuy Philen, a deputy technical officer. The three twins were born on January 16, 2021 at Kantha Bopha Hospital in Siem Reap.
In front of his family, Mr. Seng Teang brought a message of deepest greetings from Samdech Techo and Samdech Kittipritthbandit, who always send their condolences to the people everywhere in the country. Cambodia.
According to the personal assistant, from 1999 to the present, for the past 22 years, 372 families have given birth to triplets or four twins and have already received generous donations from Samdech Techo. And Samdech Kittipritthbandit to support the hardships in daily life, especially to raise three twin children, who are the grandchildren of Samdech Samdech after giving birth.
He said that the number of families of three twins is even more that Samdech Techo and Samdech Kittipritthbandit supported through MPs and working groups to help people in villages, communes, districts, capital, province before 1999.
He added that all these donations are not gifts from the Royal Government, donations from the Cambodian Red Cross or donations from parties that serve political activities, instead, these gifts are gifts from pure sincerity. The high thinking of Samdech Techo and Samdech Kittipritthbandit, who have realized the real difficulties for people who have actually given birth to three or four twins.
The personal assistant reminded all citizens to take care of hygiene, live clean, wash their hands with algae soap or hand wash to prevent the spread of the deadly Kovid disease that has been spreading around the world.
Representatives of the twin families expressed their deepest gratitude to Samdech Techo and Samdech Kittipritthbandit for always helping the people in all situations, especially for the people in need, Samdech was always present to intervene Time.
