The promotion ceremony for the above 10 officers and deputies of the Royal Gendarmerie, including 6 colonels, 2 lieutenants and 2 lieutenants. The ceremony was held at the Kampong Thom Provincial Gendarmerie Hall with the participation of Deputy Commander, Deputy Chief of Staff, Director of Departments, Sub-Departments, Offices, Local Commanders, and Heads of Security Headquarters on the afternoon of January 29, 2021.
Cambodian Ambassador Receives EU Ambassador to Cambodia to Discuss EU Strategy for Development Cooperation with Cambodia 2021-2027
(Phnom Penh): Deputy Prime Minister Prak Sokhon, Minister of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation, received EU Ambassador to Cambodia Carmen Moreno to discuss a focus on EU strategy on development cooperation. Cambodia, 2021-2027. The meeting between the two sides took place on the morning of Thursday, January 28, 2021 at the Ministry of Foreign Affairs.
The Ambassador briefed the Deputy Prime Minister on the three priority areas of the European Strategy for Development Cooperation with Cambodia 2021-2027, including: 1. Economic growth and job creation; 2. Agriculture and natural resource management. Important in fisheries and 3: Governance and the rule of law.
She also reminded of some achievements under the development cooperation between Cambodia and the EU. Among those achievements is the Bak Kheng water treatment plant project, which is supported by a grant from the European Union and the French Development Agency (AFD), plus a loan from the European Investment Bank, which will create about 16 jobs. 000 places and have the ability to supply clean water to the people who are in dire need of clean water.
The Deputy Prime Minister also thanked the European Union for its development assistance to Cambodia, which has been implemented both under the bilateral framework and jointly with European countries and has made a significant contribution to Cambodia's socio-economic development over the years. Two and a half decades ago. The Deputy Prime Minister welcomed the preliminary consultations aimed at improving EU development activities.
The Deputy Prime Minister also expressed his anticipation for the completion of the EU Strategy for Development Cooperation for Cambodia 2021-2027.
Minister of Tourism urges the virgin island ecotourism community to become an attractive community for tourists
(Kratie): Dr. Thong Khon, Minister of Tourism, on January 29, 2021, met with more than 200 people from the virgin island ecotourism community in Chroy Banteay commune, Prek Prosop district, Kratie province.
During the meeting, the Minister further stated that this virgin island ecotourism community is a tourist destination that is rich in natural resources and biodiversity, living in our country, which can show and attract more tourists. In the northeastern part of Cambodia, in particular, this site is also home to a rare species of dolphin.
He added that Cambodia has the potential for tourism to compete with other countries in the region, which is because the country is peaceful under the leadership of the Royal Government, and Kratie province in this community has white sand beach, waterfalls, rifles, dolphins. Rare nature and biodiversity live along rivers in flooded forest areas.
Moreover, the Minister stated that in this area, it can help to earn more income for the community if the community knows how to maintain and jointly take advantage of all those forests through the organization. To become a tourist destination, provide tourism services, good hospitality, especially tourism safety rules, hygiene, clean environment in the context of the Covid-19 phase.
(Preah Vihear): Mr. Net Pheaktra, Secretary of State and spokesman for the Ministry of Environment, said that the provision of ecotourism services in protected areas has been bringing millions of dollars into the local economy and promote The ecotourism potential that Cambodia has for its people and foreign tourists, as well as contributing to the cultivation of love and protection of the environment and natural resources to the public.
Mr. Neth Pheaktra made this remark on the occasion that he led a group of journalists on a three-day visit from January 29 to 31, 2021 at Phnom Tbeng Natural Heritage Park. Phnom Tnaot - Phnom Pok and Kulen Prom Tep Wildlife Sanctuary in Preah Vihear Province, organized by WCS and USAID Prey Lang Baitong Project.
Mr. Neth Pheaktra said: "In the first nine months of 2020, revenue from the provision of ecotourism services in 22 community areas in 12 protected areas in eight provinces is estimated to be injected. Enter the local economy of more than $ 25.21 million, with 536,545 domestic and international tourists (529,160 national tourists and 7,385 international tourists).
According to the spokesman, "The number of tourists visiting eco-tourism sites in the conservation and protection areas by the Ministry of Environment in 2020 will increase compared to 2018 and 2019." In 2018, there were a total of 343,852 tourists and revenue of 16.16 million dollars, and in 2019, 402,293 tourists received revenue of about 18.90 million dollars poured into the economy. .
Mr. Neth Pheaktra said that the development of ecotourism is the right strategy to improve the livelihood of local people, create new options, new occupations for the community to cut off the traditional occupation of people into the forest, logging and forest hunting and defeat tricks. Incited by some crooks to illegally occupy forest land.
According to the Secretary of State of the Ministry of Environment, there are currently 22 ecotourism communities covering an area of 35,003 hectares in 12 protected areas in eight provinces: Ratanakkiri, Kampong Speu, Kampong Speu. Koh Kong, Pursat, Preah Vihear, Kampong Thom, Kampot and Kampong Chhnang.
Mr. Neth Pheaktra said, "The Royal Government of Cambodia has a policy to turn some locations in some protected areas with tourism potential into eco-tourism areas to increase the economy for local communities to participate in the development and growth of the national economy and contribute to strengthening efficiency." Conserve natural resources and biodiversity.
At the same time, Mr. Neth Pheaktra also asked the people who visit the eco-tourism sites to participate in maintaining environmental hygiene, packing and storing garbage properly to avoid throwing litter in the open, which spoils the beauty and scenery. The beauty of those natural tourist sites.
