(Siem Reap): Bakong Village Tourism Community, I have created a wide range of tourism products to meet all the needs of tourists, as well as improve the lives of the community and the people around it. Local, provincial and even local authorities are fully recognized, appreciated and supported.
Later, Sot Sour recalled the desire of his youth to turn his base into a better place, so he devised various ways to achieve this desire.
Until September 2020, the dream tourism community was officially established in Thnal Trang village, Bakong commune, Prasat Bakong district. Out of love for the villagers, he used to have fond memories of nature in his village and wanted to highlight the name "Bakong" in order to be better known. Mr. Sot Sour and the community agreed to name their community "Bakong tourism community, my village."
Seeing the activities of the community, the people who live there always bring items from previous generations to hand over to the community to display to national tourists from Phnom Penh and other provinces, as well as foreign tourists to see Get acquainted (gain, obtain) with present-day techniques that came from Angkor. Every day, people bring vegetables, fruits, fish, meat, handicrafts to sell to tourists.
While the Royal Government of Cambodia organized the second National Ecotourism Forum for 2 days from 27-28 January 2021 in Siem Reap, also mentioned the Bakong tourism community in my village. The forum also organized a visit to this community out of six communities to get participants to learn about the community's successful experience, especially in the context of the Kovid 19 crisis.
During the reception of the above participants, Mr. Sot Sour, the community leader, presented the participants in detail and arranged for the participants to be entertained with various tourism products, such as watching traditional Khmer art performances, martial arts. Cow carts walk around the community, take a boat ride, play in the lake, eat community food, visit art objects and handicrafts made by the community.
The delegates expressed their gratitude for the hospitality of the Bakong Phum Khnom community and promised to help spread the word to other tourists, because in the community, there is a really satisfactory service to tourists.
