(Kampong Cham): The Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports, in collaboration with the Documentation Center of Cambodia, organized the inauguration ceremony of the "Khmer Rouge Research Office and Library" at the Kampong Cham Provincial Teacher Training Camp on January 29, 2021.
The "Office of the Khmer Rouge Research and Library" in Kampong Cham is a place to disseminate and receive information on the history of the Khmer Rouge, including teaching Khmer Rouge history in schools and in the community, and promoting research and compilation of The experiences of post-Khmer Rouge survivors in Kampong Cham to serve as additional lessons for teachers' teaching and student learning.
To serve the above-mentioned purposes, the "Khmer Rouge Research and Library Office" will be used as a history class, beginning with history related to Democratic Kampuchea, the history of Democratic Kampuchea, and historical events after Democratic Kampuchea.
Students, teachers and teachers will be invited to participate in a number of activities in this history class, including:
1: Classroom forum program on the importance of studying the history of the Khmer Rouge and measures to prevent genocide. 2: Public education forum program with victims of the Khmer Rouge regime. 3: Family history forum program with teachers and victims. Of the Khmer Rouge regime to discuss family experiences through the Khmer Rouge regime and education on Khmer Rouge history. 4: Teacher training program on teaching Khmer Rouge history.
