(Kratie): Mr. Thong Khon, Minister of Tourism, strongly urges the Virgin Islands, Chroy Banteay, WWF and stakeholders to continue to work together to preserve dolphins in the Mekong River to increase the attractiveness of national tourists. - International, he stated that for Kratie and Stung Treng provinces, dolphins are like the second Angkor temple.
Minister Thong Khon made this statement during a meeting with about 200 virgin communities in Chroy Banteay on the morning of January 29, 2021.
Koh Prohm Charey community is a new ecotourism community along the Mekong River in Chroy Banteay commune, Prek Prosop district, Kratie province, about 17 kilometers from the provincial town. The community was established in late 2020 with the support of the Kratie Provincial Department of Tourism and WWF.
During the meeting with the community, Minister Thong Khon said that Kratie is an important tourist destination among other provinces in the Northeast, especially with rich ecotourism potential, especially dolphins, which are rare animals. In the world.
He said that most international visitors want to visit the Mekong River dolphins in Cambodia. For Kratie province as well as Stung Treng province, dolphins are like the second Angkor Wat temple, so in the world this species is almost extinct, but has great potential, attractiveness and great value. For national tourism.
Due to the ongoing disruption of dolphins, the Minister urged the fishing community, as well as WWF and other stakeholders to continue to work together to conserve dolphins as well as other wildlife. Deer) to survive to increase the attractiveness of tourists.
He asked people not to go fishing where dolphins live because this species is very dangerous and slow to develop and can not disturb their lives.
When people take care of dolphins and they can return to serving tourists, people will get more income from tourism and participation in the conservation of dolphins and other wildlife, especially Make more money from fishing than from deforestation or hunting.
The Minister requested the Kratie Provincial Administration to facilitate negotiations with the Kampi Anlong Phsot resort so that some guests would like to visit the community by connecting the Kampi Anlong Phsot Anlong tour line and requesting communication with the Chroy Banteay virgin community so that the community can receive Fees from tourist services.
At the same time, the Minister also asked Ms. Chhay Sivlin, Director of the Cambodian Travel Agency (CATA) on behalf of the private sector to help promote the Virgin Islands community in Chroy Banteay and organize more tour packages to this area.
