(Phnom Penh): Mr. Vongsey Visoth, Minister Delegate to the Prime Minister and Permanent Secretary of the Ministry of Economy and Finance, said that although Cambodia has lost the United States Generalized System of Preferences (GSP), there are no problems affecting the Cambodian economy.
Not affected, because not only Cambodia loses GSP, other competing countries also lose, so our exporting countries pay taxes, our exporters also pay the same taxes.
Speaking at a public forum on "Macroeconomic Management and the National Budget Law 2021", the senior official confirmed that "GSP is not only offered to Cambodia, more than 90 countries around the world. "If Cambodia loses, other countries will lose as well, which means that Cambodia exports goods and pays taxes. Competitive countries also have to export taxes."
He added that concerns about the impact, unless Cambodia's exports are taxed, but other countries do not have to pay taxes, but exports have to pay the same tax, so there is no problem for Cambodia.
Mr. Vongsy Visoth said that in 2021, the United States is having problems with the transfer of power, so GSP has not yet been approved by the US legislature. The question is whether the GSP is approved or not? If not, Cambodia has to pay tax, but if it does, the amount to be taxed will be transferred back.
He added that for this GSP, Cambodia receives for the export of bags, but for the export of bicycles, clothing, furniture, Cambodia pays through MFN. Therefore, Cambodia's exports to the United States do not decline, only increase because the United States spends a lot of money to stimulate the economy, large consumption, Cambodia's export market is also fast.
"In just one year, the United States has become Cambodia's largest market," he said. "Apart from the United States, Cambodia's exports to China are also growing."
Figures from the Ministry of Commerce show that the trade volume between Cambodia and the United States in 2020 reached a total of more than 5,509 million US dollars, an increase of 16.89 percent compared to 2019 of more than 4,713 million US dollars.
Cambodia exported more than $ 5.258 million to the United States, while imports from the United States amounted to more than $ 250 million.
The main products that Cambodia exports to the United States are clothing, travel accessories (suitcases, bags), bicycles and some other items. Cambodia imports from the United States such as cars, machinery, jewelry, cosmetics, electrical appliances and some other appliances. Chbar Ampov District Governor Takes Attention to Organize Environmental Order and Sanitation
