(Phnom Penh): The construction and real estate sectors are considered Cambodia's strongholds in supporting the economy during the recession due to the Kovid 19 crisis. According to Mr. Vongsey Visoth, Minister Delegate to the Prime Minister and Permanent Secretary of the Ministry of Economy and Finance.
Mr. Vongsey Visoth said, "I think so far the real estate and construction sectors are a relatively strong economic entity that has slowed down the Cambodian economy, which is projected to be slower than the Cambodian economy. Down to -3.1 percent. "The construction sector fell from -13 percent to -2.45 percent and real estate rebounded from -5 percent to -4 percent."
"Politically, we need to take care of this sector because both sectors are an economic crisis in times of crisis," he said. "The state also has a tax-free policy for properties below $ 70,000, so sales of properties below $ 70,000 increase, while condominiums and housing prices fall."
Chrek Soknim, president of the Cambodian Association of Real Estate Appraisers, once told Fresh News that the real estate sector is still functioning, with only domestic investment and foreign investment declining. In 2020, the flow of land sales in Cambodia slowed slightly, but prices did not fall.
