(Phnom Penh): A rented room of a couple in Trapeang Koul village, Sangkat Kantouk, Khan Kampoul, Phnom Penh, caught fire, causing a great surprise. This incident happened at 9:00 AM on January 29, 2021, suspected to be caused by an electric cooker.
The room is made of galvanized iron and has two occupants: her husband Sorn Channy, 29, a lamp factory worker in the Phnom Penh Special Economic Zone and his hometown in Kirivong district, Takeo province, and his wife Koul Channy, 28, occupation Damboul Krahorm factory worker was born in Thlok commune, Traing district, Takeo province. The property in the room that caught fire included jewelry and appliances totaling $ 1,000.
According to sources, before the incident, the occupants of the room upstairs were cooking rice, then they did not remove the plug from the outlet, locked the door and left to work in the factory. Missing. When the time came, the neighbors suddenly saw smoke coming out of the house, so they were shocked and the neighbors and the village guards and the people of Kantouk commune put out the fire.
Meanwhile, Mr. Seng Kun, Deputy Governor of Kambol District, also led the force to intervene and called 3 fire trucks to go there.
The source said that after helping to put out the fire together with the fire truck to spray water to extinguish two vehicles, the fire was completely extinguished and did not spread to other rooms.
