Cambodia is committed to supporting the development of ecotourism and tourism community as the key to sustainable national tourism development
(Siem Reap): While the Kovid 19 crisis is not yet over, the Royal Government of Cambodia has urged the Ministry of Tourism, the Ministry of Environment and the Ministry of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries, national and sub-national administrations, and other relevant institutions to work together to support To the development of ecotourism and tourism community because it is an important key to promote national tourism and promote local development.
The entire forum, which includes the Ministry of Tourism, the Ministry of Environment and the Ministry of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries, national and sub-national administrations, as well as relevant institutions and the private sector, is committed to jointly supporting the development of ecotourism and tourism communities. Improved.
For the first session:
* The forum noted the effects of the Kovid-19 crisis, which severely affected tourism, land, water and air transport, accommodation, tour services and food.
* The forum mentioned the continued promotion of internal tourism as an important mechanism to generate additional income for the people.
* The forum highlighted the need to improve the quality of services in the community to promote better package planning.
* The forum promotes the use of rich potential to maximize the benefits for the entire Cambodian tourism sector.
* The forum discussed the possibility of including some protected areas and forest areas in the UNESCO list and in the existing list of preparations made by the Ministry of Tourism.
The forum promotes the study of local financial management and entrepreneurship mechanisms.
* Forum promotes the development of infrastructure to the tourism community, especially the road network.
* The forum noted that community-based tourism and ecotourism is a special sub-sector that focuses on quality rather than quantity and requires visitors to the area to be responsible, long-term and cost-effective.
* The forum calls for a joint institutional mechanism to package community visits and make greater use of community services.
* The forum recommends that a Stakeholder Platform be considered that all stakeholders can share, such as public institutions, the private sector, independent journalists and organizations, to seek funding for community development and ideas. Other.
For the second session:
* The forum suggested that the relevant ministries should formulate a joint vision focusing on the development and quality assurance of tourism products and strategies for the development and promotion of tourism products.
* Forum promotes the development of climate change resilient and high quality agriculture and market demand, as well as the promotion of community aquaculture.
* Forum to promote the development of one community, one product to promote the quality of products and market demand, as well as to promote the cultivation and harvest of natural and technical, such as beekeeping and the collection of by-products from planting trees.
* The forum proposes the identification of community areas with the inclusion of tourism activities and a clear management plan to improve the livelihoods of local people on strengthening ecotourism services and production value chains.
For the third session:
* The forum promotes closer cooperation between relevant ministries and institutions, especially the Ministry of Tourism and the Ministry of Posts and Telecommunications of Cambodia and other relevant ministries.
* The forum encourages the consideration of setting up micro-funds for the community to promote activities such as capacity building of community committees, networking, policy participation in the reform process, and participation in amendments and conservation. Especially in the context of Kovid-19 disease.
* The forum called for increased cooperation and communication between the tourism community, institutions and relevant authorities.
* The forum encourages the tourism and ecotourism community to make full use of natural resources, which are organized into small hydropower networks for community use. Like the communities that live in that area as well.
The forum encourages the participation of all communities in natural resource management.
The forum also agreed to the request of the Royal Government to organize "Ecotourism Festival" at major ecotourism destinations every year.
At the same time, Minister Thong Khon also presented a scholarship to Mr. Tit Ly, President of Stung Areng Tourism Community to encourage and encourage more participation in the development of tourism and ecotourism communities. WHO: Vaccine manufacturers are working tirelessly to fill supply shortages and urge tolerance
