(Phnom Penh): Finally, 65 families with long-standing land disputes in the Boeung Kak Lake area in Srah Chak commune, Daun Penh district, have received legal land titles after waiting for nearly 20 years.
The Certificate Awarding Ceremony was held on the morning of January 29, 2021 by Mr. Sarin Vanna, Assistant to Samdech Techo Hun Sen and Director of the Department of Land Management, Urban Planning, Construction and Cadastral Affairs of Phnom Penh, representing Mr. Khuong Sreng, Governor of Phnom Penh and Mr. Sok Penh Vuth, Daun Penh district governor.
Mr. Sok Penh Vun said that with the attention of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister and Governor of Phnom Penh, as well as the Director of the Department of Land Management, Urban Planning, Construction and Cadastral Affairs of Phnom Penh just today. He said that it is a history that 65 families living in the Boeung Kak Lake area have received a certificate of ownership of real estate for people to use legally as needed.
Mr. Sarin Vanna, Director of the Department of Land Management, Urban Planning, Construction and Cadastral Affairs, said that this property is worth the price of each house or plot, so please keep the title as safe and secure as possible. In particular, please do not iron it, because it can damage the card when we take this card to register. He asked the people to consider carefully in the case of taking the title to the bank to use the money or solve any problem.
Mr. Sarin Vanna stated that this is a rectangular strategy of the Royal Government in the field of land, is to ensure that all people get land titles and also a strategy to reduce poverty. The distribution of title deeds to the people has been delayed because the Phnom Penh Capital Hall administration is waiting for the approval of Samdech Techo Hun Sen to make concessions to all the people.
He added that systematic land registration is one of the ways we can do land registration clearly, efficiently, transparently and ensure the warmth of the people in holding the land and ensure the safety of the land. Good land management is the basis for the state to consider collecting revenue into the national budget and facilitate investment promotion to boost the national economy.
On the other hand, it is a real contribution to the implementation of the Royal Government's policy to reduce poverty, and the land survey and the issuance of land titles now people pay only 500 Riels is a land grant from Samdech Techo Hun Sen provides the people he has been waiting for for more than 20 years.
Mr. Sarin Vanna, Director of the Department of Land Management, Urban Planning, Construction and Cadastral Affairs of Phnom Penh Capital City, said, "After receiving the official title, you have been waiting for a long time."
