Monks and Buddhists: Cleansing the Mind and Determining Calmness to Listen to the Dharma Brings Happiness
(Phnom Penh): On Thursday, the 15th day of the month of Meak, in the year of Chuot Tosak, Buddhist era 2564, which is on the 28th day of January, 2021 AD, this is a special day for Buddhism, which is Meak Bochea Day. On the afternoon of Meak Bochea, Cambodian Buddhists flocked to the pagodas near their homes to offer flowers to the Buddha, give alms to the monks, and listen to the monks give sermons and advice. Distribute the Dharma as well.
Monks and Buddhists alike claim that purifying the mind and calming the mind to listen to the Dharma brings happiness. That happiness is both physical and mental.
Venerable Kat Chenda, a monk at Wat Sansom Kosal, issued a decree that, of course, the Dharma had contributed greatly to the security of the society, more or less. He said that those who are virtuous in themselves always do small things without guilt, and this leads them to true mental happiness.
"Most of the people who do not have Dharma in their body are always angry, angry and feel bad, and especially when they are a little upset, they use guilt as a trinity. This also leads to other people's stories, causing various conflicts that cause physical suffering. Venerable Card Chenda has additional orders.
The monk continued to make gestures to explain the Dharma, the Venerable continued that the Cambodian Buddhists, who are male, should be venerated once in a lifetime to purify the mind, which is the way to happiness in the future. He warned that if something is done, one should think carefully first so that the action does not cause harm to others, which leads to living in a peaceful society.
At the same time, Mr. Kim Heang, Legal Assistant, stated that he observed that the law of society was similar to the five precepts stated by the Buddha. He understands that if everyone has the five virtues in them, they may not be persecuted by social law, because having the five virtues in the body does not lead to crime.
During the interview at Wat Sansom Kosal, he added that he always came to the pagoda to listen to the monks share the Dharma regularly, especially on Shabbat, because he understood that when he listened to the Dharma, he never thought of anything wrong. Strive to cleanse the mind and forget all sorrows. As for the fact that he came to the pagoda on the day of Meak Bochea, because he was a follower of Buddhism and the worship of the Buddha always made him happy.
After offering flowers to the Buddha image and giving alms to the monk, Mr. Kim Heang said, "Dharma helps a lot! I always listen to the Dharma to train the mind not to be guilty and to find happiness in myself.
At the same time, Ms. Dalin, an intern lawyer, expressed her desire to see people obey Buddhism and understand the Dharma well, which she claims that the content of the Dharma is aimed at educating people. Do good deeds.
Ms. Dalin is also a fan of the Dharma, and also supports the presence of Venerable Card Chenda. She added that normally women always want to meet men who know right from wrong, black and white, good and bad, etc., because meeting men like this is like celebrating many pagodas.
