BEIJING (Reuters) - China on Thursday issued a renewed warning to Taiwan that "independence is tantamount to war" The past near Taiwan is a response to the current security situation in the region and to maintain China's sovereignty as well as national security. This was released by CNA on Thursday afternoon, January 28, 2021.
"Taiwan is an integral part of China," said Chinese Defense Ministry spokesman Wu Qian. "Recent actions by the Chinese military in the Taiwan Strait are necessary to respond to the current security situation in the region and to safeguard China's own sovereignty and national security."
"Past actions have been in response to outside interference and provocations by Taiwan's independence movement," Wu said. The Chinese Defense Ministry spokesman warned the Taiwan Independent Movement that they were playing with fire and facing self-immolation ... Wanting independence for Taiwan is tantamount to wanting war for Taiwan. The same.
