Dr. Sok Sokretya Meets Lt. Gen. Rath Sreang on Migrant Workers and Kovid-19
(Phnom Penh): Recently, Dr. Sok Sokretya, Personal Adviser to Samdech Techo Hun Sen and Chairman of the Board of the Khmer Migration Foundation, Samdech Techo Sen met with Lt. Gen. Rath Sreang, Deputy Commander of the National Gendarmerie and Chief Phnom Penh Gendarmerie Command.
Discussions focused on the return of Cambodian migrant workers from Thailand and to strengthen the implementation of the Ministry of Health's safety measures to prevent and prevent the spread of Kovid-19 in the community.
Lt. Gen. Rath Sreang confirmed that the return of Cambodian migrant workers was not linked to the Kovid-19 outbreak. Through his experience as a former Commander of the Banteay Meanchey Provincial Gendarmerie, every year Cambodian migrant workers return home to reunite with their families during major festivals such as Global New Year, Chinese New Year and Khmer New Year. And Pchum Ben and so on.
At the same time, Cambodian migrant workers, most of whom are farmers, often return home during the dry season and dry season rice harvest.
In particular, the most worrying thing is that the authorities have difficulty in managing data and keeping security for Cambodian migrant workers who smuggle in and out illegally in small corridors (also known as ant corridors).
After discussing the work, Lt. Gen. Rath Sreang also sent Dr. Sok Sokretya to visit the Phnom Penh Gendarmerie Command.
