Senior Minister Kun Kim, Vice President and Secretary General of the Veterans Association, on behalf of Samdech Techo, handed over the rice and noodles house. According to the report, 320 poor families received 100 kg of rice, 30 kg of rice and 1 box of noodles.
During the handover ceremony, Senior Minister Kun Kim conveyed the condolences and greetings from Samdech Techo Hun Sen to all veterans who sacrificed their lives to find peace for the country until now. Under the win-win policy of Samdech Techo Hun Sen.
General Kun Kim mentioned the care of Samdech Techo and Samdech Kittipritthbandit, both Samdech always remember the veterans and advised him to visit and solve difficult problems for veterans.
Senior Minister Kun Kim also praised the Provincial Veterans Association and its working group for focusing on building infrastructure for veterans, including roads, canals, ponds and clearing land for veterans' families there.
On that occasion, the Secretary-General also instructed the veterans to follow the instructions of the Ministry of Health to protect themselves from Kovid-19 and to take good care of their health to continue to see the development and progress of the nation.
Veterans and local people in Chongkal expressed their gratitude and unforgettable gratitude to Samdech Techo and Samdech Kittipritthbandit for their well-being.
The veterans and the people have shown their commitment to protect and support Samdech Techo's leadership forever.
