(Kampong Speu): Mrs. Kittisangkhab Dr. Men Sam An, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of National Assembly-Senate Relations and Inspection, in the morning of January 28, 2021, presided over Meak Bochea ceremony held at Preah Moha Sak Moni Chet, Phnom Preah Reach Trop (Udong) and the counting ceremony of 80 monks in Ponhea Leu district, Kandal province.
According to the documents contained in the Royal Ceremony of Tuvat Samas, there are two sources of Meak Bochea:
Source 1: Meak Bochea is a festival commemorating the day of the Rectangular Meeting of 1250 monks, which took place on the full moon day of Rami in the year of Roka, 44 years before the Buddhist era, which was one of the great days of Sakyamuni Gotama. Our teacher, who had such an assembly only once in the Buddhist era.
Source 2: Meak Bochea is a festival to commemorate the day when the Buddha declared his life in the presence of the devil on the full moon day of March, Meak, another great day before the Buddhist era, three months before the Buddhist era. Our Master met the apostles and proclaimed His age.
For Cambodian Buddhists, we also celebrate Meak Bochea like other Buddhist countries, that is, since the reign of King Sisowath Monivong, the Royal Government has designated the full moon day of March as a national holiday, abbreviated as Meak Bochea is a Buddhist festival.
