(Ratanakkiri): Mr. Ouk Kim Ratha, the owner of a Pailin (Ta Nen) plantation in Village 4, Trapeang Chres Commune, Kon Mom District, said that he has about 20 hectares of land to grow longan crops, with a continuous yield, but the market price is Dropped sharply.
Mr. Ouk Kimratha, a former graduate of the Royal University of Agriculture, Chamkar Dong, said that the planting period is between 4-5 years, with 400 seedlings per hectare, and the cost per hectare is 4,000-5,000 dollars.
