(Phnom Penh): The spokesperson of the Royal Government of Cambodia, chaired by Mr. Phay Siphan, this morning, January 28, 2021, held a press conference to review the progress and work direction of the commune / sangkat in Kampot province.
This morning's press conference was no different from previous conferences, with one provincial council and one commune councilor in the province presenting some of the achievements and efforts of the provincial councils and commune councils. / Sangkats, as well as relevant authorities in the province to improve the lives of people and development in the province, as well as in the commune / sangkat.
Mr. Nouv Saem, Member of Kampot Provincial Council, presented many achievements related to economic development projects, social work and the fight against Kovid 19 disease. According to Mr. New Saem, all these works have the active participation of provincial councilors to ensure the effectiveness of all these works.
In addition to highlighting the achievements of the provincial administration, Mr. New Saem also highlighted the achievements of the provincial council. He pointed out that in 2020, the provincial council convened 12 ordinary meetings and participated in 64 other programs.
The provincial council also approved the monthly, quarterly, semi-annual and 2020 reports of the provincial administration, the adjustment of the Kampot and Teuk Chhou district administrative boundaries, the five-year provincial development plan and the three-year rolling investment program.
In 2020, the provincial council also met with the people 21 times and organized the forum and dissemination and consultation of the provincial council in 2020 with about 1,455 people.
Mr. New Saem said that through all these forums, the provincial council has received 72 requests from the people. Of these, 10 cases have been resolved and the remaining 62 cases will be resolved in 2021.
The provincial councilor said that some of the people's problems that can not be solved because most of them are related to spending a lot of money, which is the responsibility of national institutions.
For 2021, Mr. New Saem said that the provincial council plans to raise some plans, such as:
* Participate in promoting the implementation of the three-year rolling investment program and development projects of localities, districts, communes, sangkats to achieve better results and in line with the joint development projects of the provincial and national levels.
* Participate in monitoring the implementation of the cash support program for the poor in category 1, 2 and 2 affected by the Kovid-19 epidemic crisis, making sure that the implementation of this policy has a positive impact on the people who Really affected and does not appear to be an inactive phenomenon that leads to discrimination from the people.
* Continue to visit villages, communes and back to people's homes to find out the real needs or challenges that are necessary in the face of the effects of Kovit-19.
* Continue to urge the authorities to improve the provision of administrative services, public services and request services to the people in the direction of the slogan (make it quick and transparent).
Encourage local and foreign investors or find philanthropists, development partners to help local development and create jobs for people.
* Support the rehabilitation and development of physical infrastructure, which is a necessary priority of the province, such as roads affected by the recent floods, bridges, schools, health centers, irrigation centers, dams, canals and Other public buildings.
