General knowledge: Before independence, what did East Timor face with Portugal and Indonesia?
Timor-Leste: Today, East Timor, or Timor-Leste, is an island nation in Southeast Asia that gained independence from Indonesia in 2002, but before gaining full independence, a lot has happened to the people of this country in particular. It is related to Portugal, the old colonial power, and Indonesia, which is like a giant next door.
In the 16th century, when the Portuguese army conquered Malacca, they continued to occupy Sumatra and other archipelagos, including Timor-Leste, and ruled the archipelago of Southeast Asia for centuries. 20.
When Portugal decided to leave the East Indies, Indonesia declared independence on November 28, 1975. East Timor, which had been under Portuguese rule since the 16th century, also gained independence. Less than a year later, Indonesia took the opportunity to invade Timor-Leste in 1975.
In the occupation of Timor-Leste, Indonesia claimed that all the territory in this area had previously belonged to Indonesia and that East Timor should be reunited with Indonesia.
The independence movement also emerged and was subsequently suppressed by the Indonesian army. East Timor itself reported that during Indonesian rule, more than 102,800 civilians and their militias were killed.
(Siem Reap): According to the report from the Unit for Construction of 38 Road Infrastructure in Siem Reap City, which inaugurated on November 30, 2020 under the high presidency of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia. January 25, 2021, more than 17.5% of construction has been completed.
This report was confirmed on January 28, 2021, on the occasion of Senior Minister Sun Chanthol, Minister of Public Works and Transport, Permanent Deputy Chairman of the Inter-Ministerial Commission, accompanied by Samdech Pich Sena Tea Banh, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of National Defense. And Chairman of the Inter-Ministerial Commission inspected the progress of the construction of 38 road infrastructure in Siem Reap City, Siem Reap Province.
The inspection of the road construction was done in order to check the quality of the construction, to encourage the construction unit to follow the technical specifications, the load book correctly and the acceptable standards, that is, to make the road strong and durable. Long lasting and complete as planned.
It should be noted that the project to build 38 road infrastructure in Siem Reap city, Siem Reap province, with a total length of 108.74 km, plans to use the total national budget of more than 140 million US dollars and more than 9 million US dollars for the necessary work to build the system. Drainage of rainwater and sewage outside the construction of these 38 roads, using a construction period of 13 months, is scheduled to be completed by the end of 2021.
The project covers all aspects, including: sewage system, rainwater drainage, sidewalks, sidewalks, roads for the disabled, bicycle lanes, parking lots, public street lighting, signs and diagrams, security camera systems, sewage filters. And gardening and planting trees.
In addition to the construction of 38 road infrastructure, more than 8 kilometers of the Siem Reap River will be rehabilitated and implemented by the General Department of Wastewater Treatment System of the Ministry of Public Works and Transport to further enhance the city's beauty. Tourism, culture, history and nature, as well as to help boost national economic growth.
