Mr. Vy Samnang and Ms. Seang Chanheng led a Buddhist ceremony and inspected the achievements at North Mum pagoda, a precious gift from Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of Interior, and Ms. Seang Chanheng. Built in the temple above.
Meak Bochea is celebrated to commemorate the day when the Buddha proclaimed the founding of Buddhism in the world in India in 588 BC, on the 15th day of the month of Meak, just nine months after his enlightenment.
These principles are called in Pali as "Padimok advice". Padimok is the name of Pali Buddhism, which is a set of disciplines for monks to recite in the monks' meeting every half a month: for example, learning Padimok, performing Padimok, etc., which each Buddhist must study to understand and practice.
