Please be informed that Meak Bochea is one of the major festivals in Buddhism that Buddhist countries around the world always celebrate. This ceremony is held to commemorate the two epochs of the religion of Preah Samma Samput, the teacher, which took place on the full moon day of March, the same day, the day of the quadrangle meeting and the day when he announced the age of sangkha.
Every year, Cambodian Buddhists celebrate Meak Bochea in all pagodas throughout the country, considering it the most noble fulfillment of the Buddhist tradition in accordance with the Constitution of the Kingdom of Cambodia, which states that "Buddhism is the state religion." Kampot Provincial Court President Long Kes Phirom donates 50% of his salary for 6 months to the Ministry of Health to fight Kovid-19
