Minister of Health: Peace, political stability have brought about the progress of the health sector, which is the fruit of national pride
(Phnom Penh): The National Report on the Final Results of the Census of the Kingdom of Cambodia in 2019 Reflects Good Progress on Health Indicators and was officially released on January 26, 2021, highlighting key health indicators. Some.
Mr. Mam Bunheng, Minister of Health, said that in the special report, the most important indicator is that the life expectancy of the Cambodian people in 2019 will increase to 75 years, of which the life expectancy of men has increased to 74.3 years and women increased to 76.8 years. The increase was significantly linked to a drop in infant and child mortality rates per 1,000 live births per 1,000 live births.
Through this national report, we observe that the infant mortality rate decreased from 26 in the 2008 census to 18 out of 1,000 live births in the 2019 census, and the under-five mortality rate decreased from 44 in the 2008 census, 28 out of 1,000 live births in the 2019 census. In addition, the maternal mortality rate has dropped significantly.
