(Siem Reap): Mr. Say Sam Al, Minister of Environment, on the afternoon of January 27, 2021, cut the ribbon to officially inaugurate the 32 kW solar power plant with battery storage system. 87 kWh at Sok An Phnom Kulen Research and Conservation Center in Siem Reap.
The event was attended by leaders and officials of the Ministry of Environment, representatives of relevant ministries and institutions, representatives of the Siem Reap provincial authorities, representatives of the Swedish Embassy in Cambodia, development partners and park officials and community members.
According to Mr. Ngan Phirun, Deputy Governor of Siem Reap, the new achievements for Siem Reap, a province of tourism, culture and nature, so the use of clean energy does not affect the environment is a starting point for other resorts in Siem Reap as well. Others that do not have a national grid.
The Minister also considered today's achievement as a new step for the preparation of other support infrastructure in the future, aiming to develop the center to serve as a basis for cooperation, scientific research, knowledge exchange and Technology, raising awareness of the importance of biodiversity and ecosystems, sustainable development and sustainable living in Cambodia.
Mr. Say Sam Al also mentioned that the research center and conservation of the hair "Sok An Phnom Kulen" will contribute to the diversification of the local economy, especially tourism, connecting with culture and nature, and help increase employment options, additional sources of income and improve the lives of local people. This goes one step further in line with the policy of the Royal Government of Cambodia.
It should be noted that the working group of the Department of Biodiversity of the General Secretariat of the National Council for Sustainable Development has been collecting forest species from Phnom Kulen and other areas for further recording and identification.
According to Ms. Chan Somaly, Undersecretary of State at the Ministry of Environment, the Sok An Phnom Kulen Research and Conservation Center was established to:
First: Research: Identify inventory and determine the criteria and special functions of each species in a scientific way.
Second: Conservation: Salvage, breed, refine and restore endangered and endangered species from natural forests, especially for the preservation of endemic species.
Third: Outreach: A place for education and outreach on the types and numbers of wildlife in Cambodia.
