(Phnom Penh): The Ministry of Economy and Finance this morning, January 27, 2021, organized a public forum on macroeconomic management and financial law for management in 2021 at Sofitel Phnom Penh Phokitra Hotel to disseminate more widely to the public. Learn more about macroeconomic management and the 2021 budget law.
Watch the full video of Mr. Vongsey Visoth opening the public forum on macroeconomic management and the 2021 national budget:
Mr. Vongsey Visoth made this statement during the public forum on macroeconomic management and financial law for 2021 management of the Ministry of Economy and Finance on the morning of January 27, 2021.
Mr. Vongsy Visoth said, "Cambodia should stop borrowing from outside and return to domestic borrowing as external borrowing starts to increase. In fact, the World Bank currently has an interest rate of 2.8 percent per annum. "Only 0.7 percent, so Cambodia has suspended some loans and turned to borrowing from Japan, the ADB and from Europe."
He added that Cambodia is currently negotiating with the World Bank to ease interest rates so that prices do not rise too much.
He stressed that after all, the main goal of Cambodia is not to borrow money from foreign countries, but to borrow locally through the issuance of bonds. Cambodia's debt, meanwhile, remains low, despite the 19-crisis Kovid crisis in 2020.
