Criminal police of the Ministry of Interior arrested the manager of Sidach company for $ 760,000 for running for Chinese citizenship
(Phnom Penh): Police from the Criminal Department of the Ministry of Interior on the morning of January 27, 2021 arrested and sent a company manager to the Phnom Penh Municipal Court in connection with the complaint of three Chinese nationals in the case of C. Deduct $ 760,000 guaranteed to run for Cambodian citizenship, but failed.
The suspect, 46-year-old Sin Davuth, resides at B10, Lum Road, Boeung Chhouk Village, Sangkat Kilometer 6, Khan Russey Keo, and is the General Manager of Goldwell. Sources at the Phnom Penh Municipal Court revealed that the authorities had complied with the order to bring Sin Davuth to Mr. Plang Sophal, Deputy Prosecutor of the Phnom Penh Municipal Court for questioning. The three Chinese.
According to the complaint, in August 2019, a Chinese company director relied on Sin Davuth, General Manager of Goldwell, to help run the application for Cambodian citizenship for three Chinese nationals. There were two men and a woman.
Sin Davuth then demanded that the Chinese hand over $ 760,000 to run the Cambodian citizenship application, and promised that the results would be released within 90 days. When the agreement was reached, the Chinese handed over 10 checks from the Union Commercial Bank of Cambodia, totaling $ 760,000, to Cindavuth for the job.
When the deadline came, there was no summons from the relevant institutions to swear in the previous administrative procedure. Due to this reason, the plaintiff contacted Sin Davuth, but he escaped. And did not meet to negotiate as when accepting the money, and even tried to escape.
It was not until March 27, 2020, that the Chinese discovered Sin Davuth, and then Sin Davuth said that he did not use the money to run for Cambodian citizenship, but to use his own work, but Sin Davuth could. Promised to pay back all the money, but refused to pay and escaped further. Because of this, the Chinese relied on a lawyer to sue the suspect, Sin Davuth, the company's managing director.
Until January 26, 2021, the Ministry of Criminal Police arrested the suspect and brought him for questioning, but the suspect still refused to pay the plaintiff, so the police sent the case to court. Lt. Gen. Hun Manet: The sisterhood alliance between the army and civil society institutions is an initiative of Samdech Techo, and this mechanism has contributed significantly to building and strengthening the national defense.
