(Phnom Penh): The Information and Quick Reaction Team of the Phnom Penh Municipal Police on January 27, 2021, issued a statement denying the publication of a case in Por Sen Chey district that a mother beheaded her daughter. In fact, the slip itself.
The Press and Quick Reaction Team confirmed that the case of violence caused by a mother cutting her daughter causing head injuries was not actually a case of violence, but slipping on her own in the bathroom.
Immediately after receiving the information and following the orders of Lt. Gen. Thet, Deputy Commissioner and Phnom Penh Municipal Police Commissioner to investigate the case accurately and clearly, Lt. Col. Mon Vuthy, Police Inspector of Po Sen Chey District, led the officers to investigate directly. Arrived at the victim's house.
According to the girl's statement, she confirmed to the authorities that on the evening of January 25, 2021, she had an argument with her mother because she did not know how to fish, so when she went to the bathroom, she slipped. He collapsed and called his brother and mother to be taken to the hospital immediately.
At the same time, the father also confirmed that it was a case of slipping and falling, not a case of cutting by the mother. Until January 27, 2021, the district inspector Por Sen Chey brought the victim and his parents for further questioning at the inspectorate. Mrs. Director of the Department of Social Affairs, Deputy Governor and Representative of Sangkat Kakap 1.
After researching and questioning, the police handed over the girl to the Department of Social Affairs to be treated for her injuries. At the same time, out of compassion, the inspector also donated some money to the girl victim.
Ten pagodas in Kratie city together to celebrate Meak Bochea at Wat Bacha is more solemn than last year
(Kratie): On Thursday the 15th and Friday the 1st of Roach Khemak, the year of Chuot Tosak BE 2564, which falls on January 28, 2021, tomorrow is the day to celebrate Meak Bochea, which is one of the major festivals. In Buddhism, the Buddhist countries around the world always celebrate.
Wat Ratha Balaram, also known as Wat Bacha, is a well-known pagoda located in Kratie City, Kratie Province, and often organizes religious and national festivals during the Meak Bochea Festival. Go with 10 Buddhists at the foot of the pagoda to celebrate together in this pagoda.
Venerable Theung Chantra, Honorary King of Preah Vinay Thor, Provincial Councilor and Chief Bishop of Wat Balabaram, led the monks to prepare the pagoda courtyard and decorate the pagoda to celebrate the festival in accordance with the religious reputation of Preah Samma Samput.
Venerable Theung Chantra said that the Meak Bochea ceremony was held to commemorate the three merits of the Three Noble Truths: the Buddha, the Dharma. Nirvana.
He added that the Meak Bochea ceremony also commemorates three other great things that Samma Samput did when he was still alive. The three main stories are: 1: He held a quadrangle meeting with 1,250 monks, all of whom were monks, 2: The Buddha, the Master, performed the Patimok advice, 3 He gave the age of sangkha to the devil, saying that in three months he would enter Nirvana.
The chief abbot of Wat Bacha has said that this year, to celebrate this great festival in Buddhism, the provincial hall, chaired by the provincial chief, decided to have 10 pagodas in the province hold a joint Meak Bochea ceremony in the pagoda. Balaram is called Wat Bacha.
According to Venerable Theung Chantra, the Meak Bochea ceremony on January 28 will be attended by the provincial governor, a large number of Buddhist officials in the province.
During the festival, there will be car parades and pedestrians on the streets to announce the purity of the Buddhists in Buddhism. More specifically, there were 1,500 ready-made candles and 1,800 balloons of six colors.
