(Phnom Penh): Mr. Vongsey Visoth, Minister Delegate to the Prime Minister and Permanent Secretary of the Ministry of Economy and Finance, predicted that the Cambodian economy will recover by 4% in 2021.
Mr. Vongsey Visoth pointed out that this remarkable recovery in growth was due to the strong efforts and intervention of the Cambodian government.
Mr. Vongsey Visoth's statement was made during the invitation to participate in the public forum on "Macroeconomic Management and Financial Law for Management 2021" of the Ministry of Economy and Finance to disseminate to the public to learn more about macro management Economy and budget law 2021 this morning, January 27, 2021.
He added that a large part of the Cambodian economy comes from tourism, so if tourism stagnates, it will be difficult for Cambodia to recover economically. Another factor is the demand for Cambodian exports to international markets. Cambodia fears that as the global economic recovery slows, so will Cambodia's exports.
The senior official stated that the courage to claim economic growth of around 4% this year because Cambodia has received warm intervention from the head of the Royal Government, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia to restore the Cambodian economy during The world, especially Cambodia, is facing the crisis of Kovid 19.
The Royal Government of Cambodia has intervened in many areas to prevent the economic downturn in Cambodia. In 2020, the Cambodian economy will shrink by -3.1 percent, while in the ASEAN region it will shrink by -3.3 percent.
Mr. Vongsey Visoth said that due to the intervention of the head of the Royal Government in preventing the spread of Kovid 19, lending to small and medium enterprises (SMEs), tax relief and the participation of some of the currency. The National Bank of Cambodia has made it easier for investors to do business.
He added that due to the excellent intervention of the Cambodian leadership, Cambodia's economic growth was between 3.1 percent and less than 5 percent.
Mr. Vongsey Visoth said that without the intervention of social protection, social assistance, rural employment, Cambodia's poverty will fall to 17 percent, but after the help to reduce poverty in Cambodia between 14 Percentage only. Unemployment also fell from 4.1 percent to 4.1 percent.
"The intervention of the Royal Government is really beneficial to the economic recovery and good for the stability of people's lives and the reduction of poverty," he said.
According to the senior official, Cambodia's garment industry fell from -7.7 percent to -6.4 percent, and Cambodia's garment exports fell by 10 percent, but non-garments increased by 26 percent. As a result, Cambodia's exports fell by only -1 percent.
For the agricultural sector in 2020 will contribute 0.5 percent of the Cambodian economy, while exports of agricultural products will increase by 18 percent.
