(Preah Sihanouk): Chinese gunmen and accomplices who shot and killed Chinese people in the early morning of January 21, 2021 in Sihanoukville, Preah Sihanouk Province were arrested by the police. A total of three people have already built a case to be sent to the provincial court to be punished according to the law.
Preah Sihanouk Provincial Police Commissioner Major General Chuon Narin told Fresh News this morning, January 27, 2021, that the gunman and his accomplices who shot the Chinese man were arrested about 10 hours after the incident. That is, on January 21, but the authorities have not released the information to the public because they need to continue to search for those involved.
According to the General Commissioner, in addition to the gunmen and the three accomplices, there are other accomplices who are being investigated by the specialized forces to be arrested and punished according to the law. However, the three people who were arrested have been sent to the provincial court and have already been detained by the investigating judge.
A Chinese man was shot dead by a gunman in a pool of blood while the driver was seriously injured. The incident happened at around 9 am on January 21, 2021 in front of Casino Life in Sihanoukville, Sihanoukville Province.
