(Phnom Penh): Mi Cheat Company donated two QMS machines and two TV sets to the National Blood Transfusion Center in order to contribute to supporting the daily operation of the center on the morning of January 27, 2021.
Speaking at the handover ceremony of the National Blood Transfusion Center, Ms. Chheng Sokuntheavy, General Director of the National Blood Transfusion Service, said that the two new items that the National Blood Transfusion Center donated to the National Blood Transfusion Center were 40-inch flat screen TVs. Two machines and a QMS machine, which is a modern technology and highly capable of managing data on the number of customers at the National Blood Transfusion Center accurately and easily.
She added that the provision of both materials is in line with the daily needs of the National Blood Transfusion Center to serve the people more efficiently and quickly.
Dr. Sok Po, President of the National Blood Transfusion Center, said that the operation of the National Blood Transfusion Center today is very busy, even in the situation of 19 Kovid, where the center receives hundreds of donors and uses blood per person. Day by day, the provision of QMS sensors and televisions has really facilitated the day-to-day operations of the National Blood Transfusion Center.
On this auspicious occasion, Mr. Sok Po would like to express his sincere gratitude to Ms. Chheng Sokuntheavy, Director of the three companies and the management, as well as the staff of the company who always help organize the blood donation program and support the blood donation process. Of the National Blood Transfusion Center.
