"I have brought Prime Minister Hun Sen's request for Indian vaccine assistance to Cambodia to my leadership," she said. The 19 Kovid vaccines made in India are shipped to neighboring India such as Myanmar, Bhutan, Sri Lanka, Nepal, Bangladesh and so on. "To strengthen ties with Cambodia, I believe we will be able to provide some vaccines to Cambodia."
"However, the arrival of 2021 has brought hope for all of us to get the vaccine against Kovid 19," she added. India produces more than 60% of the world's vaccines. India has truly acted as the pharmacy of the world, and this shows India's importance to the world in the context of the spread of Kovid 19.
Cambodia and India have shared close historical ties for the past 2,000 years, dating back thousands of years of cultural, civilized, commercial, marital, and blood ties. The Indian language, art, architecture, textiles, clothing, food are modified and synthesized in Cambodian society, and this Indian transformation can be seen in all aspects of daily life.
