For one year, Cambodia has not had 19 deaths from Kovid. Cambodia is also rated as one of the top 19 countries in the world for controlling the spread of Kovid.
Under the guidance and implementation of the strict measures of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the Prime Minister of Cambodia, as well as the strict implementation of doctors, health workers, relevant authorities, the armed forces and the people throughout the country to control the situation of Cambodia. Spread. In particular, Cambodia was able to successfully eradicate 19 cases of Kovid in the "November 28 Community" event.
Although Cambodia has done well in the management of Kovid 19 for a year, the risks for Cambodia have not been eliminated as Kovid 19 continues to spread around the world. In this regard, Ms. O Vandin, Secretary of State and spokesperson of the Ministry of Health, reminded the people not to forget and continue to participate in the implementation of measures to prevent the spread of Kovid 19.
She also called on the people to continue to strictly implement the three measures of protection (wear masks, wash hands, keep a distance) and 3 do not (do not go to closed places, do not go to crowded places and do not touch each other) to be consistent. Appeal and guidance of Samdech Techo as well as the Ministry of Health.
She also called on travelers to the country, both by air and by land, to take part in the cataclysm and not to run away from the cataclysm, which could lead to infection in the community.
The spokesperson of the Ministry of Health also called on the owners of ceremonies or weddings to strictly follow the instructions of the Ministry of Health on January 26, 2021 by spraying heat, spraying alcohol and wearing masks to the participants. In particular, the principle of maintaining a safe distance by requiring only five people to sit at a table.
It should be noted that during the one year of the Kovid 19 epidemic, it was observed that the Royal Government of Cambodia, headed by Samdech Techo Hun Sen, had introduced a number of measures to prevent the spread of Kovid 19 and solve economic problems.
The Royal Government of Cambodia has released a number of budget packages to help solve the problems of the people and help maintain economic stability, as well as ensure the operation of factories in Cambodia.
