(Phnom Penh): The Minister of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries, Mr. Veng Sakhon, urged all farm fish farmers to further expand their potential while the Ministry has suspended the import of fish from abroad in order to increase domestic production.
Mr. Veng Sakhon praised the proper organization of the farm in terms of water quality, drainage system and environmental farming, which is suitable for the life of fish and can be considered as a model farm throughout the province.
Regarding the inspection of this fish farm, Mr. Veng Sakhon advised that he should make efforts to expand the breeding potential, including breeding and expansion of breeding partners to ensure the current supply to the market, while the Ministry has been suspending the import of fish. From neighboring countries to increase domestic production.
He added that farms should use the potential of farms with land, water and environment in collaboration with the Fisheries Administration to establish breeding and hatching facilities for fish that are scarce and popular in the market to supply to farmers in and outside the area or as a place to research the quality of feed. Fish and student work internships.
Mr. Veng Sakhon also encouraged the farm owners that the Ministry as well as the Fisheries Administration will wait for co-operation to facilitate the investment process of fish farming in the farm and the establishment of a fish hatchery in Kampong Thom province to be successful.
Japan to provide $ 238 million in concessional loans to Cambodia in 2020 to respond to the effects of Kovid-19
(Phnom Penh): Throughout 2020, the Government of Japan will provide concessional loans (low interest loans) in the amount of approximately 238 million US dollars to contribute with development partners to support the implementation of policy implementation of The Royal Government of Cambodia in response to the effects of Kovid-19 disease.
During the meeting, the Deputy Prime Minister also congratulated Ms. KAMEI Haruko on her appointment as the new Chief Representative of the Japan International Cooperation Agency (JICA) in Cambodia and thanked her. The Government of Japan and the people of Japan have always supported the rehabilitation and economic and social development of Cambodia.
He said Japan is a strategic partner and one of the largest bilateral cooperation partners financing Cambodia. Japanese government funding is targeted at all areas, including health, education, agriculture, infrastructure, highways, bridges, international autonomous ports, irrigation, power grids, and water supply.
Ms. KAMEI Haruko also expressed her pleasure to be on duty in Cambodia and expressed her appreciation for the efforts of the Royal Government of Cambodia, which has achieved many fruitful achievements, especially in taking strict and serious measures. Prevent and control the spread of Kovid-19 today.
During her tenure in Cambodia, she pledged to continue to strengthen and expand cooperation in all priority areas of the Royal Government of Cambodia, as well as to continue to support further financing within the framework of Official Development Cooperation (ODA). Within the framework of grant financing, concessional loans and technical assistance.
