This confirmation was made by Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of the Ministry of Interior, during the launching ceremony of the National Report on the Final Results of the 2019 Cambodian General Census on January 26, 2021 at the Sofitel Phnom Penh.
Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng said that the Royal Government of Cambodia, led by Samdech Techo Hun Sen, has reformed all sectors in order to reduce poverty, which is the core of all policies and development strategies of the Royal Government. In fact, statistical data is an important basis for the formulation of strategic policies of the Royal Government and also a tool for evaluating the progress of those tasks.
In addition, Samdech Krala Hom said that according to the statistical data collected from the census and surveys, it provides an important basis for preparing and monitoring the National Strategic Development Plan, assessing the poverty situation in Cambodia and achieving the goals of sustainable development in Cambodia, as well as helping Researchers at the national level, including the wider national and international community.
Developing countries and partners are facing the achievement of the universally agreed sustainable development goals through the 2016 Declaration. However, the measure of the progress of the Sustainable Development Goals is based on available information and census data. Preliminary data sources on population and housing characteristics and characteristics are essential for achieving sustainable development goals and for various development plans.
"Census information is a solid foundation for providing live indicators for monitoring education, gender, mortality and environmental goals, in addition to economic, social and demographic and health surveys, which provide direct indicators for "Monitor poverty and some other indicators."
Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng added that the mid-term report of Cambodia's National Strategic Development Plan 2019-2023 will be regularly evaluated and reviewed. This census report will help to make necessary improvements and refinements in goals, objectives and plans in line with the latest data and facts.
