This circle is shaped like an outer circle, a central circle, and an inner circle. The outer circle is 30.5 meters in diameter with 30 stones, each more than 3 meters high, while the central circle is 23 meters in diameter with 40 stones, but only two are standing. Straight and 6.7 meters high, while the stone in the inner circle is 15 meters in diameter, with 42 stones, height between 2.1 and 4 meters and an average weight of 25 tons.
Archaeologists have speculated that these stone structures may have been built between 3000-2000 BC and more than 5,000 years ago.
In this modern age, Stonehenge is a popular tourist destination in the United Kingdom and also a cultural symbol of this great power. In 1882, the British Parliament successfully implemented the conservation of Stonehenge, designating the area as a National Heritage Site. Until 1986, the entire Stonehenge area was inscribed on the UNESCO World Heritage List.
The World Heritage Site is currently under the control of the Royal Family of the United Kingdom in collaboration with the British National Heritage Authority to better preserve and manage the nation's heritage.
