Hunan Chinese Chamber of Commerce in Cambodia Provides Kovid-19 Medical Equipment to Ministry of Health
(Phnom Penh): The Chinese Chamber of Commerce of Hunan Province in Cambodia has provided medical equipment for the fight against Kovid-19 to the Ministry of Health on January 26, 2021.
The handover ceremony was held at the Ministry of Health under the chairmanship of Ms. Youk Sambath, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Health and Chair of the Technical and Supply Working Group of the Inter-Ministerial Commission on Combating Kovid 19 and other leaders.
On that occasion, Ms. Youk Sambath expressed her deep gratitude to the Chinese government and people, including the Hunan Provincial Chamber of Commerce in Cambodia, which has always supported the Cambodian health sector.
She said the aid underscores the high concern of the Hunan Chinese Chamber of Commerce in Cambodia for the Royal Government and the people of Cambodia, especially in the current context where we are working together to promote safeguards. Prevent and respond to the spread of Kovid-19 as soon as possible.
