Murderer arrested for trying to kill widow
(Koh Kong): Pursuant to the order of the Ministry of Interior and the directives of Major General Kong Mono, Koh Kong Provincial Police Commissioner, on 24 January 2021, the Serious Crimes Unit of the Koh Kong Provincial Police Commission cooperated with the Koh Kong District Police Inspectorate. Search for the perpetrator of the case of rape and murder at Dey Khmao point, Dey Tumnup village, Trapeang Rong commune, Koh Kong district, Koh Kong province.
Lieutenant Colonel Lay Tyro, Director of the Bureau of Serious Crimes, said that the premeditated murder occurred at 6:30 pm on January 23, 2021 at Dey Khmao point, Dey Tumnup village, Trapeang Rong commune. Koh Kong District, Koh Kong Province.
Suspect's name is Him Saat, alias Ou Arifin, male, 18 years old, Khmer Muslim, Occupation: Worker of KK1 factory, Temporary residence in Village 4, Sangkat Dang Tong, Khemarak Phoumin City.
According to the suspect's confession, he and the victim lived together in Sovan Baitong village, Kandol commune, Botum Sakor district, Koh Kong province. The suspect said that he knew that the victim wanted to visit the house, missed his child, and promised to take him on a motorcycle with him to the scene. The suspect stopped the motorcycle and grabbed the victim. Prey raped her, but she was very upset for fear of breaking the news, so she kept her mouth shut.
Lt. Col. Lay Tiro confirmed that the bodies of the victims, after an autopsy, were handed over to relatives for traditional rites. For the suspects, the authorities have prepared a case to be sent to the provincial court for legal action. The Minister of Posts and Telecommunications announced a six-month salary cut to the Ministry of Health to fight Kovid 19
