Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng Announces the Release of the National Report on the Final Results of the 2019 Cambodian Census
(Phnom Penh): Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of Interior, and Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, this morning, presided over the launching ceremony of the National Report on the Final Results of the National Census. Cambodia 2019.
The ceremony was held at Sofitel Phnom Penh with the participation of Mr. Kittisetha Dr. Chhay Thorn, Senior Minister, Minister of Planning and Vice Chairman of the National Census Committee of Cambodia 2019, Representative of the United Nations for the People. Cambodians (UNFPA), representatives of the embassies of friendly countries in Cambodia, as well as leaders of many relevant ministries and institutions.
According to Ms. Hang Lina, the Royal Government delegate in charge of the Director General of the Institute of Statistics of the Ministry of Planning, the results of the 2019 census were 97.5% transparent and accurate, which allows the relevant institutions to use as needed. Especially for planning purposes, as this figure has also been sent to the United Nations.
The annual population growth rate decreased from 1.5 percent between 1998 and 2008 to 1.2 percent between 2008 and 2019. Cambodia's annual growth rate in the last decade, we see, is higher than the average growth rate in Southeast Asia, which is only 1.0 percent.
The capital with the largest population is Phnom Penh at 2,129,371 and Kep with the smallest population at 41,798. The population density was 86 people per square kilometer in 2019. The sex ratio according to the provisional figures of the 2019 census was 94 males per 100 females, unchanged from 2008.
