Break the murder case! Police Arrest Man Who Killed Cousin in Batheay District, Kampong Cham Province
(Kampong Cham): A murder case that occurred on the night of January 23, 2021 at Taing Chrey village, Sandek commune, Batheay district, Kampong Cham province, was successfully separated by the Kampong Cham Provincial Police after careful research. The perpetrator was arrested at 8 pm on January 25, 2021.
After receiving the report from the Batheay District Police Inspector, Major General Em Kosal, Provincial Police Commissioner, assigned Colonel Chan Hor, Deputy Chief of Provincial Criminal Police Planning Team, to lead the Special Criminal Police Force, the Provincial Technical and Scientific Force, and the District Specialist Force. The district police inspector and the administrative police station arrived at the scene to investigate immediately.
After questioning, the suspect confessed that he had actually used a sword to stab the victim, who was his cousin, and that the reason for the confusion was that he had been angry with the groom's guests. In that, the professional force confiscated 1 sword as well.
The suspect is currently being held in custody at the Batheay District Police Inspectorate on the orders of the Deputy Prosecutor of the Provincial Prosecutor's Office and is compiling a case to be sent to the Kampong Cham Provincial Court.
