Pailin Governor Helps Build Homes for 45 Veterans in the Province
(Pailin): Seeing the hardships and lack of shelter for veterans in the province, Dr. Ban Srey Mom, Governor of Pailin Province and Honorary President of the Cambodian Veterans Association, helped build houses for 45 veterans in the province.
She added that out of sympathy for the need and in return for the merits of veterans in the cause of the motherland in the past, she volunteered her own donations to help build homes for the homeless veterans.
Senior Minister Kun Kim, Vice President and Secretary General of the Cambodian Veterans Association, stated that Dr. Ban Srey Mom has been helping disaster-stricken people and underprivileged members of Pailin Province since she was a Pailin MP. So much so that the people are very satisfied and supportive of her, especially when Pailin province suffered from floods in the past.
The Senior Minister considered her enthusiasm and gestures to the veterans and their families as a model gesture.
Senior Minister Kun Kim, Samdech Techo's Chief of Staff on Veterans Affairs, also thanked her and all the philanthropists who donated their own funds to provide a warm shelter for Cambodian veterans.
The senior minister said, "This is a very good gesture in return for our veterans, who are all grateful to our society." Because of the sacrifice in this national cause, it is possible to maintain peace and provide good opportunities for business, investment and a good life. So we have to know how to repay them. ”
