Tensions on the Sino-Indian border escalated in mid-2020 when the two countries' armies clashed with sticks and batons in the disputed border area of northwestern and northeastern India. The army also died. The two sides then blamed each other and sent additional troops to the border area.
The Chinese side has not yet responded to the allegations made by India. However, for months, the Chinese and Indian militaries have resumed negotiating efforts to ease tensions. Sri Lanka to lead nationwide elephant census in 2021
(Colombo): The Sri Lankan Ministry of Wildlife Conservation will conduct a nationwide elephant census in 2021 to determine the number of elephants in its country, local media reported on Monday. This is according to a release by Xinhua on Monday, January 25, 2021.
But Sri Lanka in 2020 recorded 407 elephant deaths, the first highest annual elephant loss. As many as 122 people have been killed, the second-highest annual death toll in the world due to elephant-human conflict.
Killing wild elephants in Sri Lanka is a criminal offense, but there are regular reports that villagers are angry that they were killed by poisoning or shooting.
