National Bank of Cambodia: By 2020, deposits in the banking and financial sector will be close to $ 34 billion, while loans will be close to $ 37 billion!
Despite being affected by 19 Kovids, people are still able to deposit their money into the banking system.
National Bank officials confirm that the growth of deposits in 2020 is slower than last year.
According to the National Bank of Cambodia, "By 2020, consumer deposits will reach 33.8 billion US dollars, an increase of 15.5 percent, of which consumer loans will reach 37.3 billion US dollars, an increase of 14.8 percent." "And the banking system's assets were $ 59.4 million, an increase of 15.7 percent."
According to the report, by 2020, there will be 285,074 credit restructuring accounts, equivalent to 4.2 billion US dollars. The reorganization of banks decreased in November and the balance of reorganization began to decline from September. Microfinance institutions, on the other hand, had their accounts and restructured loans rebounded to a record low in October but rebounded in November.
Of that, the riel accounted for 9.8 percent of the $ 3.2 billion of the general currency. Riel deposits accounted for 7.7% of total deposits and KHR loans accounted for 12.8% of total portfolio.
Regarding the increase in deposits in the banking sector, Mr. Oknha Huot Ieng Tong, President and CEO of Hatta Bank, said that Hattha Bank's savings deposits increased by 32%, higher than loans.
He added that the increase was due to the fact that in 2020 there may be 19 Kovid crisis, people do not invest money or do business, so send it to the bank to get interest, this is a surprise that Hatta Bank received because last year never received. Ministry of Tourism launches 3-day training course for tourism entrepreneurship trainers
