(Siem Reap - Banteay Meanchey): On the morning of January 25, 2021, Mr. Kao Thach, Royal Government Delegate in charge of the Director General of the Bank for Rural Development and Agriculture and his colleagues inspected the use of credit and the effectiveness of credit under the financing project. Special of the Royal Government of a fish farm in Prey Krouch village, Sangkat Krabei Ral, Siem Reap city, Siem Reap province.
Mr. Mao Panha, the farm representative, said that the farm has a total area of 8 hectares. After receiving a loan from ADB under a special government financing scheme, his farm has the opportunity and possibilities to expand, as well as sufficient capital to supply seed feed.
The farm received a loan from ADB under a special government financing scheme with an interest rate of only 0.42% per month to expand its fish farming business.
Leaving Siem Reap on the afternoon of January 25, 2021, Mr. Kao Thach and his colleagues inspected the use of credit and the effectiveness of credit under the special financing project of the Royal Government of a duck farm in Sangkat Pong. Animals Serey Sophorn, Banteay Chey Province.
According to Ms. Ya Tuong, the owner of the farm, the farm covers a total area of more than 2 hectares and has a total of more than 20,000 duck eggs, and her farm can produce about 18,000 duck eggs per day. To 19,000 eggs. As for the market, it is for sale in Banteay Meanchey and Battambang provinces.
She added that with a low interest rate loan from ADB, her farm was able to expand and her egg sales increased accordingly. She also expressed a willingness to borrow more from ADB to expand duck cages and increase duck egg production.
She also thanked ADB, especially the Royal Government of Cambodia, for taking into account the well-being of farmers by dropping special low-interest credit packages to help farmers in the 19th crisis. Apparently, her farm has also benefited greatly from ADB loans.
The farm received a loan from ADB under a special government financing scheme with an interest rate of only 0.42% per month to expand the egg-raising business.
In the afternoon of January 25, 2021, Mr. Kao Thach and his colleagues continued to visit the farmers who are members of Kangva Agricultural Community and inspected the mixed vegetable cultivation of the community in Phnom Pong Kangva Village, Sangkat Kampong Svay, Serey Sophorn City, Banteay Meanchey Province. . The Kang Va community has a total of 46 families and a total cultivated area of 57 hectares.
According to some community members, the cultivated area of the farmers is divided into two seasons: in the fifth season, the cultivated area can only be 26 hectares, while in the rainy season, the cultivated area can be up to 57 hectares. The crops there are carrots, onions, cabbage, corn, cabbage, etc., and the yield is for local supply and in Phnom Penh.
Recognizing the potential of the Kangva community and the efforts of community members, Mr. Kao Thach, the Royal Government delegate, encouraged the community to continue to strengthen and expand cultivation, taking into account the quality and asked for a clear plan. Cultivation and consideration of a stable supply in the market.
In response to this, Mr. Kao Thach advised the community to sign an agricultural contract with Khmer Safe Vegetable Company to ensure market clarity, as the company will guarantee the purchase. Vegetables at the prices stated in the agreement.
On that occasion, there was also the presence of Khmer safe vegetable company, and both sides also negotiated and achieved better results.
Please also note that some members of the Kangwa community have been using ADB loans to expand your vegetable cultivation and netting.
Cambodia, China hold panda painting exhibition to strengthen cultural and tourism ties between the two countries
