Senior Minister Kun Kim is interested in the efforts of farmers after receiving rice seeds from the Royal Government to plant and rehabilitate after the floods
(Battambang): Through the inspection of farmers' fields, Senior Minister Kun Kim, First Vice-Chairman of the National Committee for Disaster Management, was impressed by the efforts of farmers after receiving fragrant rice seeds and OM54 51 seeds. This is a non-seasonal type of rice from the Royal Government of Cambodia to be planted in rehabilitation after suffering from floods at the end of the rainy season.
At this point, Senior Minister Kun Kim said that these are the attention of the head of the Royal Government of Cambodia, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia to all people and under all circumstances, especially when the people Faced with difficulties such as the recent floods to help restore the lives of people to improve.
The Senior Minister's interest came after the handing over ceremony of the house to the veterans, accompanied by the leadership of the Ministry of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries, including relevant provincial officials on January 22, 2021. Progress of rice cultivation after the recent floods in Prey Norin and Peam Ek communes, Ek Phnom district, Battambang province, after receiving rice seeds from the Royal Government of Cambodia.
On that occasion, the farmers' representatives who received rice seeds from the Royal Government confirmed that the rice seeds received in the past were growing well and there was no pest damage, which made the farmers Delighted and immediate intervention from the head of the Royal Government after the flood, such as providing rice seeds and food, etc. to restore the planting in time will help alleviate their hardships to a large extent. Well.
The senior minister praised the condition of all the rice plants are growing well and the problem is not a problem because these rice plants are already flowering and hope that the rice yield will increase.
Mr. Sok Touch reacted to the theft of large trees in Techo Sen Russey Trip National Park
(Phnom Penh): Dr. Sok Touch, President of the Royal Academy of Cambodia, expressed his legal reaction to the continued illegal logging of trees to learn how to clear land and burn the forest in the Royal Academy of Cambodia Techo Sen Russey Trip Park in Cheb District, Preah Vihear Province. .
This is not the first time that Techo Sen Russey Treb National Park has been burglarized by nearby residents, destroying about 300 large trees and continuing to destroy them. Hundreds of felled trees were found in the homes of people living in the park.
As the President of the Royal Academy of Cambodia, a research institution, Dr. Sok Touch stated that the Royal Academy had educated him to love the forest for two years and asked him not to cut down the forest, but to rely on non-timber forest products. Such as mushrooms, vines, grapes, etc.
Dr. Sok Touch emphasized that the Royal Academy of Cambodia has done everything in vocational training for his descendants. In addition, after the end of the Kovid-19 epidemic, his descendants will become tourism service providers, guiding tourists, arranging guesthouses, preparing food for tourists, etc., which we will organize training in the future. Face.
The Royal Academy of Cambodia Techo Sen Russey Trip Park has been implementing a number of projects, including: Dairy Cattle Project, Nursery Planting and Planting Project in the Royal Academy of Cambodia Techo Sen Russey Trip Park, Goat Raising Project and Research Project for the Protection and Conservation of Natural Resources. At the Royal Academy of Cambodia Techo Sen Russey Trip Park to restore forest cover to help prevent climate change.
