Mr. Hun Many: The development of 38 roads in Siem Reap will help restore the economy of the people and be ready to receive tourists after the Kovid 19 crisis
(Siem Reap): Mr. Hun Many, President of the Union of Youth Federations of Cambodia and Chairman of the Seventh Committee of the National Assembly, expressed his belief that the development of 38 roads in Siem Reap is to help restore the economy of the people in the province and as a preparation. Receiving tourists to Siem Reap after the Kovid 19 crisis.
Mr. Hun Many made this statement on the occasion that he, together with Mr. Tea Seiha, Governor of Siem Reap and Mr. Prak Sophoan, President of the Union of Youth Federations of Cambodia in Siem Reap, visited the construction of 38 roads in Siem Reap on the afternoon of the 23rd. January 2020.
"The view of the road construction confirms that despite the fact that the world is experiencing a crisis of the Kovid 19 epidemic, it has not had a serious impact," Hun Many said on Facebook. To the development of Cambodia. "On the contrary, this development is to help restore the economy of the people in Siem Reap and to prepare to receive tourists to Siem Reap after the Kovid 19 crisis."
According to the Siem Reap Provincial Administration, the 38 roads have a total length of 108.74 km, with a total budget of 140 million US dollars and more than 9 million US dollars for the necessary work to build the drainage system. Rain and sewage outside the construction of these 38 roads.
Through the construction of these 38 roads, Siem Reap will be transformed into a modern city and a potential tourist destination, which has been designated by the Royal Government of Cambodia as a core area of the national development pole as a cultural, historical and natural tourism destination in line with the city's physics. Along with taking into account the protection and improvement of the environment, the comfort of the people and the development of smart cities (Smart City).
Once completed, the project will serve as a grid interface, connecting the city to the suburbs and connecting to major tourist areas and national road networks to reduce traffic congestion in the city, boosting transportation. Attract investors, businessmen and national and international tourists as a contribution to the national economic growth after the Kovid-19 crisis.
