The Ministry of Social Affairs considers that the minimum policies and standards on the protection of the rights of victims of human trafficking have been in place for more than 10 years, and the Ministry has been cooperating with the International Organization for Migration (IOM) and relevant partner organizations. To review and update this document so that it is consistent and responsive to the current situation.
Please be informed that the Consultative and Revision Workshop on Minimum Policies and Standards on the Protection of the Rights of Victims of Trafficking in Persons was organized for the purpose of reviewing the results of the evaluation on the implementation of Minimum Policies and Standards on Human Rights. Protection of the Victims of Trafficking in Persons by Development Partners and Gather Comments and Inputs for Editing Minimum Policies and Standards.
