Ms. O Vandin considers the release of Australian news on the effectiveness of the fight against Kovid 19 as giving justice to Cambodia (Video inside) (Phnom Penh): Ms. O Vandin, Secretary of State and spokesperson for the Ministry of Health, considered the release of the Australian press. From Cambodia's highly effective management of the fight against Kovid 19 is a justification for Cambodia's efforts.
Australia's SBC newspaper on January 22, 2021 published an article highlighting some of the measures and measures that led Cambodia to be more effective in combating Kovid 19 for more than a year and no deaths. No.
"It's amazing," SBC quoted Dr. Francis Daily as saying. "I thought we would be killed by Kovid 19 there, but after the first two or three months of the outbreak it became clear that there were not many Kovid 19 cases."
The article, published by SBC, also highlighted Cambodia's effective control measures and response to the fight against Kovid 19, which has prevented Kovid 19 from spreading.
Ms. O Vandin said that in the past, some foreigners, foreign institutions and the public have suspected that Cambodia is hiding data on 19 cases of Kovid. She considered the SBC release to be a fair trial for Cambodia on the 19 cases of Kovid.
"Justice has now really been given to Cambodia, and there is a clear recognition of Cambodia's efforts to better implement measures to prevent the spread of the Kovid 19 virus," she added.
Ms. O Vandin also said that the management and fight against the 19-virus virus does not depend on small or large countries, the president has strong or weak medical resources, but it also depends mainly on the placement. Issue measures to control, combat and implement those measures effectively.
In addition, all relevant authorities of Cambodia, as well as the people of Cambodia, have joined together to strictly implement the health rules that make Cambodia highly successful in the fight against Kovid 19.
Ms. O Vandin also stated that Samdech Techo Hun Sen is an exemplary leader in the world who has been mentioned and written in analytical and research articles published in the United Kingdom and Tuesday. The nation also said that Cambodia is one of the few countries that has limited medical resources, but has implemented measures to prevent the spread of Kovid 19 very well.
It should be noted that as of this morning, January 24, 2021, Cambodia has found a total of 458 cases of Kovid 19 infection, of which 405 have been cured and 53 patients are hospitalized.
For more than a year now, the Royal Government of Cambodia, led by Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the Ministry of Health, as well as all relevant institutions in Cambodia have worked hard to fight Kovid 19. Successfully for Cambodia, 19 Kovid patients have been rehabilitated and there are no fatalities.
