Kampong Thom Provincial Authority solves the problem of lack of water to irrigate 2,000 hectares of farmers in Stung Slap and Kaek Som Bai rice fields in Santuk district on time
(Kampong Thom): Mr. Sok Lou, Governor of Kampong Thom Province, led his colleagues and relevant departments as well as local authorities to solve the water shortage for people to grow rice in the area of Stung Slap and Kaek Som Bay area, Koh Koh commune, Santuk district, Kampong Thom province. January 23, 2021.
On that occasion, Mr. Sok Lou, Governor of Kampong Thom Province, stated that water is the most important issue for all kinds of agricultural crops, especially rice, which the head of the Royal Government of Cambodia has been paying the most attention.
He said that this problem occurs because this year, the water in the river died too quickly, causing the people who grow crops in the area to ask for food about 2,000 hectares lack of water in the lower part of the water.
The provincial governor said that in order to join the Royal Government, people must know how to share irrigation water to everyone, and those who grow crops in the upper community canals, please understand the people at the bottom to get water. The bottom is irrigated equally, based on common interests.
In that, Mr. Sok Lou allowed the disconnection of the dam so that the water flowed to the bottom and allowed the people to restore the old canal at Kaek Sabay, nearly 4 kilometers long. . He confirmed that the province already has plans to build a dam in this area.
On that occasion, the people of Stung Slap and K'aek begging for rice were very happy, saying that the shortage of water came at a time when their rice was being prepared, which needed to be fertilized and sprayed. Yield and people said that in one season, all the fields in the area for rice can be done only once, because this area is a lowland area, the water does not easily drain and return soon, if the damage can not be cultivated. Repeat that.
The people thanked the provincial authorities, especially Mr. Sok Lou, for helping them solve the water problem immediately and on time without leaving the people in trouble.
