China mobilizes unusual bombers and fighter jets to patrol Taiwan's airspace
BEIJING (Reuters) - Eight bombers and four Chinese military fighter jets landed in the southwestern corner of Taiwan's ADIZ airspace on Saturday, the Defense Ministry said. Taiwan immediately deployed a missile system to monitor the situation. This was released by CNA on Sunday, January 24, 2021.
Taiwan considers the move of a large number of Chinese military aircraft, including eight H-6K nuclear warplanes and four J-16 fighter jets, an unusual move. In response to China's actions, the Taiwan Air Force warned Chinese military aircraft and deployed air defense missile systems to monitor the situation.
The deployment of Chinese bombers and fighter jets to and near Taiwan on Saturday came just days after new US President Joe Biden was officially sworn in.
