The Ministry of Health provides 5,000 liters of water storage tank and study materials to 304 teachers and students of Plou Touk Primary School, Kampong Leng District, Kampong Chhnang Province.
The donations include: 1 5,000-liter water tank, 1,000 notebooks, 1,000 pens and some funds donated to 304 principals, teachers and students of Plouk Touk Primary School. Located in Peam Khnong Village, Plou Touk Commune, Kampong Leng District, Kampong Chhnang Province.
The team advised to take care of health in the cold climate of our country, especially to maintain hygiene, prevent as well as prevent the spread of Kovid 19 to follow the guidelines of the Ministry of Health.
It should be noted that last week, the students of Plou Touk Primary School in Peam Khnong Village, Plou Touk Commune, Kampong Leng District, Kampong Chhnang Province requested the administration to provide a plastic water tank with a capacity of 5,000 liters to store water for students to wash their hands. Face feet for cleaning before and after class and for watering flowers in the school because the water is far from the school.
The boat road primary school is currently located on a hill in a flooded area, a geographical area that is flooded every rainy season and in the dry season, the river recedes away from the school, which is a consequence for students to wash their hands. Feet are a high risk for young students and it is difficult to get water to water the school.
Plot Touk Primary School has 2 schools and 7 classrooms from 1st to 6th grade with 273 students and 1 kindergarten class with 31 students, a total of 304 students in both primary and secondary school, 150 girls There will be 7 teachers. The study map has 3 villages: Thnal Chheuteal village, Peam Khnong village and Slot village.
Dr. Sok Sokretya Asks Thailand to Reduce Fees and Procedures for Cambodian Workers During the 19 Pandemic
(Phnom Penh): Dr. Sok Sokretya, Personal Adviser to Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia and Secretary of State of the Ministry of Tourism, requested the Thai government to facilitate the fees and other paperwork for Cambodian workers working in Thailand during the Kovid disease. 19 Pandemic.
The request was made during Dr. Sok Sokretya's meeting with the Thai Ambassador to Cambodia, Mr. Panyarak Polthap, on Friday, January 22, 2021 at the Thai Embassy.
Dr. Sok Sokretya spoke about the close friendship and cooperation between Cambodia and Thailand today and in the future, the bond of unity, peace and friendship between the two countries will be even closer.
Mr. Panyarak Poultap expressed his appreciation and congratulations to the Royal Government of Cambodia for managing Kovid-19 so well that he, as well as embassy officials and all Thai people who are staying in Cambodia, are very warm.
He also praised the efforts and wise leadership of Samdech Akka Moha Sena Padei Techo Hun Sen in maintaining complete peace, rapid development of Cambodia and maintaining the friendship between the state and the people. Between the people of the two countries, Cambodia-Thailand.
On that occasion, Dr. Sok Sokretya, on behalf of the Founder and Chairman of the Board of the Khmer Migration Foundation, Samdech Techo Sen requested the Thai side to continue to facilitate the fees and procedures for Cambodians who migrate to Thailand. At a time when they are facing the Kovid-19 crisis.
The Thai Ambassador promised to bring this proposal to the Royal Government for review, and he will continue to work to strengthen the relationship between Cambodia and Thailand even closer.
