(Preah Vihear): About 200 stairs to climb Tbeng Meanchey Mountain in Preah Vihear Province, which were damaged by floods during the previous rainy season, have now started the construction and repair process, with the Krong Pali Ceremony Ask the owner of the water, the owner of the forest land to officially build this morning, January 23, 2021, and it will cost about 140,000 US dollars.
The ceremony was held in the presence of Senior Minister Meas Sophea, Chairman of the Royal Government Working Group for Preah Vihear Province, and Mr. Long Sovann, Chairman of the Provincial Council, Mr. Prak Sovann, Governor of Preah Vihear Province, and other government officials.
The director of the Preah Vihear Provincial Department of Public Works pointed out that the budget for the construction of the Tbeng Meanchey escalator came from a solidarity fundraiser under the initiative of Senior Minister Meas Sophea and Provincial Governor Prak Sovann. The construction of the stairs, however, the Governor of Preah Vihear is committed and raise additional funds to complete the construction of the stairs.
Please note that Phnom Tbeng Meanchey is located in Kraing Dong village, Preah Khleang commune, Tbeng Meanchey district, Preah Vihear province. Phnom Tbeng Meanchey is a natural tourist area on the top of the mountain, which is attractive because on the top of Tbeng Mountain there are 3 stone pagodas, Wat Dambok Khmao, Krabao Chrum, there are waterfalls, as well as many other areas related to Grandpa "Suong" »The sacred warrior of Phnom Tbeng, our sacred Khmer since ancient times.
