Progress of Samdech Mey Library for 2021
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Youk Chhang, Director of the Documentation Center of Cambodia, has received his permission to pay homage to Her Majesty Queen Norodom Monineath Sihanouk, Queen Mother of Cambodia in Freedom, Dignity and Happiness on the progress of the Samdech Mey Library for 2021.
In order to contribute to the promotion of the glorious value of Cambodian art and culture, Mr. Youk Chhang organized all kinds of art performances, including Khmer traditional dance (or royal dance), contemporary dance, painting and music every three months in the Samdech Mey Library. The Samdech Mey Library is becoming more and more active and interesting, as well as promoting national and international guests to the fame and diversity of the Samdech Mey Library.
In January 2021, an art group led by Ms. Sok Nalis visited the Samdech Mey Library and inspected the venue for traditional dance training, which will begin on January 30, 2021.
The troupe will perform classical dance to celebrate the 110th anniversary of International Women's Day on March 8, 2021 at the Samdech Mey Library. The national guest, the Ambassador and Ambassador to Cambodia, will be invited to attend the event and watch the performance at the Samdech Mey Library.
The Samdech Mey Library has played an important role in exhibiting the relics and handprints of King Norodom Sihanouk, research, dissemination and publication, including books on the relationship between Norodom Sihanouk and Prime Minister Juan Lay. China.
The Samdech Mey Library was officially established by the Documentation Center of Cambodia to pay homage to Her Majesty Queen Norodom Monineath Sihanouk, the Queen Mother of Cambodia, who worked hard for His Majesty King Norodom Sihanouk, the former King Father. Monarchs, Fathers of the Khmer Nation, the Nation of Cambodia and the People of Cambodia.
Her Majesty Queen Norodom Monineath Sihanouk inaugurates the Samdech Mey Library of the Documentation Institute of the Documentation Center of Cambodia on September 21, 2020.
The Samdech Mey Library holds a collection of more than 3,000 books and 2,800 boxes of documents on the royal family and history of Cambodia. The archives in the Samdech Mey Library also include books on the history of Cambodia and documents on the Democratic Kampuchea regime (1975-1979) of at least 1.7 million, which were researched by the staff of the Documentation Center of Cambodia for more than a year. 20 years ago.
The Samdech Mey Library also contains documents in other formats, such as photographs, movies and tens of thousands of minutes of audio recordings of victims of the Pol Pot era, which have been digitized in high quality to ensure conservation. The document is stable and easy for the public to use.
Although Cambodia is currently facing the crisis of the Kovid 19 epidemic, the educational activities of the Samdech Mey Library to educate the Cambodian people and the next generation of researchers through Cambodian art, music, film and history are still active. Face.
