(Phnom Penh): A video has been leaked showing former supporters of the Cambodia National Rescue Party (CNRP) abroad arguing violently, confirming their internal divisions.
The nine-minute video, obtained by Fresh News, confirms that the reason for the altercation was that a woman had strongly criticized the political activities of Sam Rainsy, an illegal rebel leader who often organized patriotic events. Retirement repeatedly lies its supporters. She even criticized Sam Rainsy for being politically incapable and incapable of defeating the CPP.
The woman claimed that former CNRP supporters cheated on Sam Rainsy and later regretted it. According to the same woman, she also expressed her desire to see Sam Rainsy walk away from political life to leave opportunities for the next generation.
Israel launches Kovid-19 vaccination campaign for high school students
Israel has launched a COVID-19 vaccination campaign for all high school students aged 16 and over, the Ministry of Health said on Friday. This is according to the release by the Xinhua news agency on Friday night, January 22, 2021.
According to the report, the vaccination operation will start in the next few days and will include more than 300,000 students.
On January 10, Israel also announced the vaccination of all teachers and other educators. According to the Israeli Ministry of Education, since then, more than 50 percent of the 203,000 educators have been vaccinated.
The general vaccination campaign in Israel began on December 20, 2020, with front-line medical staff and the elderly over the age of 65 and chronic patients being the first priority. Encourage supply and purchase partners for agribusiness products to strive for sustainability, quantity and quality
(Siem Reap): The signing ceremony of the Memorandum of Understanding on the Supply and Order of Agri-Vegetable Trade between the Agricultural and Food Market (FAM) and Lilyfood Industry Co., Ltd. on 22 January In 2021, Mr. Pan Sosak, Minister of Commerce, urged the two sides to work together to streamline the supply and purchase of agro-commercial vegetable products in both quantity and quality.
Both parties need to share information with each other and coordinate with relevant parties to resolve any issues that may arise in the process of supply and purchase, and to examine the possibility of further expansion. Other agro-commercial products as well as support for quality and safe products that farmers produce.
Mr. Pan Sosak expressed the hope that the cooperation in the supply and purchase of agro-commercial vegetable products will create mutual trust to increase the price of these products in the market to another level.
He said that in the past, the local vegetable market had high demand, but the supply was limited in both quantity and quality, while farmers were experiencing uncertainty in the prices of agricultural products.
He added that agro-commercial vegetable products are one of the five potential agribusiness products of the AIMS project and in accordance with the recommendations of the head of the Royal Government on the promotion of agro-commercial products to supply the domestic market. By replacing the import of agro-commercial products from abroad and increase the income of farmers.
At the same time, Cambodia also has the potential to export products to international markets, especially the European, American and Asian markets, and processed products from agro-commercial vegetables are products that Cambodia has the ability to expand to a variety of products. Many other than rice, pepper, clothes, shoes, bags and bicycles.
