Senior Interior Ministry official: US remains committed to helping Cambodia fight human trafficking
(Phnom Penh): Ms. Chou Bun Eng, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Interior and Permanent Vice Chair of the National Committee for Combating Human Trafficking, said that the United States remains committed to assisting Cambodia in the fight against human trafficking.
She said this on the occasion of the representative of Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of Interior, meeting with Mr. Patrick Murphy, US Ambassador to Cambodia on the progress of the fight against human trafficking on the afternoon of January 22. 2021 Minutes of the Ministry of Interior.
On that occasion, Ms. Chou Bun Eng said that during the 19-crisis Kovid crisis, human trafficking began to rise in any country, including Cambodia. She said that in Cambodia, human trafficking activities during the 19-Kovid crisis had two objectives: first, the illegal export of people with the purpose and exploitation, and the second: the taking of people for marriage as opposed to Will.
"The United States remains committed to spending money in support of countries (including Cambodia) that are committed to the fight against human trafficking," she said. "Just say what his help is directly to the partner organization."
