Minister Chea Van Det: Cambodia is ready to turn ASEAN into a leading digital community and economic bloc
(Phnom Penh): Cambodia's Minister of Posts and Telecommunications Chea Vandeth says Cambodia is ready to work with all member states and development partners to transform ASEAN into a leading digital community and economic bloc. That promotes economic growth using secure technology and digital systems.
Mr. Chea Van Det made the remarks while leading a delegation of the Ministry of Foreign Affairs to attend the first ASEAN Digital Ministers' Meeting via video on "ASEAN: Digital Connected Communities" and related meetings with the participation of Ministers and senior officials in charge of the telecommunications and digital technologies of ASEAN member countries, as well as development partners such as China, Japan, Korea, India, the United States and the International Telecommunication Union.
He added that Cambodia has been working to strengthen the construction of telecommunication infrastructure, both mobile and internet, to provide reliable and affordable services, as well as to promote digital literacy.
The ASEAN Digital Ministers expressed willingness to cooperate with development partners such as China, Japan, Korea, India, the United States and the International Telecommunication Union to increase digital cooperation, develop human resources and expand the scope of new technologies and strengthen technology security capabilities. And the implementation of the ASEAN Digital Master Plan 2025.
The first ASEAN Digital Ministers 'Meeting, hosted by Malaysia, was renamed the ASEAN Telecommunications and Information Ministers' Meeting (TELMIN) from 2000 to 2019 in line with global trends. Technological change.
