NEW YORK (Reuters) - The Nuclear Non-Proliferation Treaty came into force on Friday, much to the chagrin of Pope Francis and UN Secretary-General Ban Ki-moon. Of the world's major nuclear powers. This was released by CNA on Friday, January 22, 2021.
As of October 2020, 50 countries have signed and ratified the Nuclear Non-Proliferation Treaty, which was initially ratified by 122 countries at the 2017 UN General Assembly. The treaty must enter into force this Friday, or 90 days after the 50th country signs and ratifies it.
