(Phnom Penh): According to figures from the State Secretariat of Civil Aviation (SSCA), the number of passengers at Cambodia's three international airports in 2020 has dropped dramatically by 79 percent.
According to the figures, the total number of domestic, international and transit passengers will reach 2.13 million in 2020, down 79 percent from the same period in 2019.
For all three, air freight also fell 31 percent. Cambodia received 49,983 tons of goods, down 31 percent.
Ms. Chhay Sivlin, President of the Cambodian Association of Travel Agents, said that Cambodia receives about 6 million tourists a year, but now this 6 million tourists lost up to 70 percent, so the decline in freight. This is due to Kovid 19 alone, with indirect and networked side effects.
"In fact, the decline in air freight is due to Kovid 19 and also to the transportation sector," she said. "Most of the goods are supplied to tourists, but now there are no tourists, only local customers and a small number, there is not much demand, so the delivery of goods is declining."
