However, Samdech Techo Hun Sen expressed confidence that the world will reach a point where it is required to be vaccinated against Kovid-19 with a clear certificate before it can travel through other countries. The reason why the prince dared to think like this is because of his personal experience when he went to Africa, it is required to be vaccinated against yellow fever first.
He also claimed that in the future, if Cambodia vaccines more people against Kovid-19, it will require those who come to Cambodia to be vaccinated as well. It is true that this is a voluntary principle, but each country may have a need, and if Cambodia vaccines more, the flow of investment to Cambodia will be even better.
On the other hand, if Cambodia had not vaccinated its people much, investors would have seen Cambodia as a country at risk of contracting Kovid-19 and would not be investing in it. Not only does it protect people from epidemics, but vaccines are also part of attracting foreign investment. This is what Samdech Techo Prime Minister said.
