Ms. O Vandin, Secretary of State and spokesperson for the Ministry of Health, emphasized that the 194 Cofim vaccine is a vaccine with an efficiency of 79.34 percent. The vaccine is currently being submitted to the World Health Organization (WHO) and may be evaluated and approved in the near future.
She added that in order to be effective, the vaccine requires two doses and the interval from the first to the second dose is 21 days. According to O'Vandin, Sinofam's 19-dose Kovid 19 vaccine is currently used in more than 223 million doses in many countries around the world, including in Asia, the Middle East, Africa, Latin America and Europe.
