Chinese company is investing in raising ornamental fish in Cambodia for export, this year plans to export dragon and squid worth more than 2 million USD
(Phnom Penh): A Chinese company has been investing in raising ornamental fish in Cambodia for export, located on a farm in Dei Edth commune, Kien Svay district, Kandal province, and this year the company plans to export dragon and squid worth more than 2 million Dollars to China.
Mr. Veng Sakhon, Minister of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries, highly appreciated the companies that have invested in establishing ornamental fish farms, which is in line with the Royal Government's policy to support and encourage local and foreign investors to promote the sector. Aquaculture and the export of ornamental fish also contribute to the national economy.
The Minister advised that the company must prepare technical documents related to breeding in order to prepare a protocol for exporting ornamental fish to China, in collaboration with the Cambodian Fisheries Administration, to liaise with the General Administration of Customs of China to request procedures or conditions. Necessary from the Chinese side as a first step to ensure the smooth export process in the future to avoid congestion of farm produce.
