For 3 years, more than 50,000 Cambodian children received medical treatment from a team of doctors with the support of Chinese friends
(Phnom Penh): In the three years from 2018-2020, 53,210 Cambodian children received medical examinations and treatment from various Cambodian-Chinese joint medical teams, especially open heart disease, with the support of Yundi. And Fuwai Heart Hospital, Yunnan Province, in cooperation with the Cambodia-China Progress Researchers Association, with the support of the Cambodian Senate and the Chinese Embassy in Cambodia.
This statistic was presented at a ceremony to share the experience of helping Cambodian children who were successfully sent to open heart surgery and treatment in China on January 22, 2021, with the support of the Cambodian Senate and the Chinese Embassy. Yundi Cambodia and Fuwai Heart Hospital, Yunnan Province, China.
Wang Winthean, Chinese Ambassador to Cambodia, said that the project is of great significance to not only help Cambodian children and Cambodian doctors, but also to strengthen and expand the traditional ties between the two countries. Another level of strength.
The Ministry of Public Works would like to thank Samdech Techo Hun Sen and distinguished guests who attended the inauguration ceremony of the Ministry and Public Works "Techo Sen Institute of Public Works and Transport".
(Phnom Penh): The Ministry of Public Works and Transport (MPWT) thanked Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, and all the distinguished guests who participated in the historic event of the inauguration ceremony of the Ministry of Public Works and Transport and the Institute. Techo Sen Public Works and Transport on January 22, 2021.
The Ministry continued, "On the occasion of the New Year 2021, I would like to extend my best wishes and blessings to Samdech Techo, Samdech Kittipritthbandit, as well as sons, daughters, grandsons, granddaughters, Samdech, Excellencies, Lok Chumteavs, Neak Oknha, Lok Oknha, Ladies and Gentlemen and brothers and sisters." All relatives and friends, please be blessed with the Buddha and the five blessings, age, class, happiness, strength and influence, do not be lazy.
Please note that the new office building of the Ministry of Public Works and Transport and the Institute of "Techo Sen Public Works and Transport" is located along Street 598, popularly known as "Chea Sophara" in Sangkat Chrang Chamres 2, Khan Russey Keo.
The new building of the Ministry has also installed solar energy systems on the roofs of all buildings to help reduce the cost of daily electricity consumption and save the national budget with consideration for Contribute to reducing environmental impact through the use of green energy.
Senior Minister Sun Chanthol, Minister of Public Works and Transport, emphasized that the construction of this building was aimed at establishing public service facilities related to the Ministry of Public Works and Transport within the Ministry itself. In addition, to provide a comfortable location for leaders and civil servants to serve the people better.
Separately, the building of Techo Sen Institute of Public Works and Transport has 4 floors, 24 classrooms, 3 administrative offices, 1 laboratory, 1 library, and is equipped with modern study materials and technical equipment. At a cost of $ 2.5 million.
According to Senior Minister Sun Chanthol, the establishment of the "Techo Sen Public Works and Transport" Institute for the training of staff, civil servants, trainees and students to enhance the ability of Cambodian children on technical skills to build road-bridge infrastructure, which will ensure that "Cambodian children can "Has the ability to build its quality roads and bridges in the future."
