On that occasion, the head of the Royal Government of Cambodia continued to confirm the Kovid 19 vaccine, showing the reasons why Samdech decided to receive the vaccine from China now, although the World Health Organization (WHO) has not yet officially announced. Samdech stated that while Cambodia is being harassed by Kovid 19, it is no longer possible to wait, it is necessary to seek free and voluntary vaccinations for the people.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that he had sent a letter to the Chinese Prime Minister and met with the Chinese Ambassador to Cambodia to discuss and find out the mechanism for obtaining the vaccine. According to the talks, Cambodia received aid from China or borrowed Chinese money and bought both Chinese vaccines, Sinofam and Sinovak.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated: "Before that, I said that we only accept vaccines that are recognized by the World Health Organization, but looking at the other side, a large number of countries use vaccines in their countries and Sell vaccines abroad. "So in a situation like this, we can not wait any longer."
Samdech Techo Hun Sen added that China's Sinofam vaccine will arrive in Cambodia for the first time in February and he will go to the international airport to receive the vaccine. Samdech Techo continued that the Kovid 19 vaccine is a strategic commodity.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen also reaffirmed that vaccination is based on a voluntary principle, so anyone who wants to be vaccinated, if not, is not forced. Samdech wants Mr. Mam Bunheng, Minister of Health, to conduct a census to find out who wants to inject and who does not want to inject.
"There is a Chinese vaccine and we will get it through Kovak, which will be given to us in March, maybe only that much. "Kovak can buy vaccines from China, can buy vaccines from Korea, can buy from Britain, can buy from the United States, and then Kovak will give us 20% of the population, but the emergency is only 3%." This was confirmed by the head of the Royal Government of Cambodia.
According to Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the vaccination will also give investors confidence without considering Cambodia as a country endangered by Kovid 19. To find the Kovid 19 vaccine, Samdech used three channels, including: 1. Kovak, which is the World Health Organization, and 2. With friendly countries and 3rd. Negotiate directly with the company.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen has announced that the first dose of the Chinese Kovid 19 vaccine will be given first, and he hopes that other senior leaders will also be vaccinated. Samdech Techo confirmed that after the injection, Samdech will hold a press conference as well. Samdech Techo Hun Sen expressed the expectation that before Khmer New Year, Kovid 19 vaccine will be given to 500,000 people. Samdech Techo Hun Sen said that garbage collectors must also be vaccinated.
Senior Minister Kun Kim Presents 8 More Houses Donated by Samdech Techo Hun Sen to 8 Families of Poor Veterans in Battambang Province
(Battambang): Senior Minister Kun Kim, Secretary General of the Cambodian Veterans Association, on Friday morning, January 22, 2021, handed over eight houses donated by Samdech Techo Hun Sen to eight families of veterans in Samrong Ta Kok village, commune. Samrong, Ek Phnom district, Battambang province, with poor living conditions.
The handover ceremony was also attended by Mr. Ouk Khnouch, Undersecretary of State for the Ministry of National Defense, Mr. Nguon Rattanak, Governor of Battambang Province and the leadership of the Provincial Armed Forces.
Speaking on that occasion, Senior Minister Kun Kim mentioned the attention of the two Samdechs on the well-being and daily life of members of the Cambodian Veterans Association, so those who received the house of Samdech Hun Sen must work hard. Livelihood improves their livelihood because it is stable after receiving this house.
At the same time, Mr. Deng Phay, a disabled person, representing the eight families, thanked the two Samdechs for providing them with a house and vowed to respect and believe in the leadership of the Samdech against the attempt to overthrow the government if Even though they are retired.
Please note that on this occasion, in addition to handing over 8 houses, Senior Minister Kun Kim also provided some equipment and food items as a precious gift from Samdech Techo Hun Sen and Samdech Kittiprittbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen. Also.
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Vongsey Visoth, Minister Delegate to the Prime Minister and Permanent Secretary of the Ministry of Economy and Finance, on the morning of January 22, 2021, met with Mr. Asad Yaqub, President of the International Finance Corporation (IFC). Cambodia at the Ministry of Economy and Finance.
Mr. Asad Yaqub stated that he aims to learn about the progress of challenges and opportunities in Cambodia's development, as well as to discuss the vision for further cooperation of the International Finance Corporation (IFC) in Cambodia.
Mr. Vongsy Visoth praised the role and contribution of the IFC in supporting the development of the private sector in Cambodia in the past, both through funding and through consulting and technical assistance.
At the same time, Mr. Vongsey Visoth also informed Mr. Asad Yaqub about the state of the Cambodian economy, emphasizing that according to the overall estimate, Cambodia's economic growth in 2020 is better than expected, despite Decrease.
