Sun Chanthol, Prominent Minister on Public Service Reform
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Sun Chanthol is a senior official of the Royal Government of Cambodia with the status of "Senior Minister" and received the trust of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia to hold the Ministry of Commerce for two and a half years between 2013 to 2016. In April 2016, he was transferred back to the Ministry of Public Works and Transport and has continued to this day.
As a minister born of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, as Minister of the two Ministries, Mr. Sun Chanthol received a lot of support and admiration from the people for leadership and reform. Much on service delivery.
Sun Chanthol is a Cambodian who left Cambodia at a young age in 1973, when the country was in the throes of civil war and catastrophic destruction. Sun Chanthol left the country at that time with only $ 50 in his pocket.
Arriving in the United States without English skills, Sun Chanthol spent many years in Maryland, USA, learning English and earning a living by washing dishes at a restaurant at night.
In 1994, when Cambodia needed human resources to re-develop the country, Mr. Sun Chanthol was asked to return to help rebuild the country and establish the Council for the Development of Cambodia (CDC) as a one-stop shop for investment. Directly from abroad, where he served as Secretary-General from 1994 to 1997 in this institution. During this time, Mr. Sun Chanthol also served as Secretary of State at the Ministry of Economy and Finance.
Mr. Sun Chanthol returned to Cambodia again and established his own trading and investment company in 1999. From 1999 to 2003, Mr. Sun Chanthol served as Economic and Financial Advisor to the President of the National Assembly, and in 2003 he was elected a member of the Cambodian National Assembly.
Mr. Sun Chanthol was appointed by the Royal Government as Minister of Public Works and Transport from 2004 to 2008 and as Senior Minister and Chairman of the Council for the Development of Cambodia from 2008 to 2013. Mr. Sun Chanthol served as Vice Chairman of the Council for the Development of Cambodia until April 2016.
During his two-and-a-half years at the Ministry of Commerce, Sun Chanthol has made a number of important reforms to accelerate the improvement of Cambodia's business environment. Significant reforms related to the reorganization of the Ministry of Commerce have been implemented in the past, including the introduction of a transparent recruitment process in order to be able to appoint the best candidates. .
Mr. Sun Chanthol also developed automation systems for business registration and certification of goods, which enable these systems to operate online to significantly reduce informal fees and strengthen trade facilitation in the country. Cambodia.
Mr. Sun Chanthol's reform at the Ministry of Commerce was recognized as the first step towards a global relations and modernization strategy for Cambodian government institutions. Recognizing the importance of better information and education, Mr. Sun Chanthol initiated a series of workshops focusing on business, leadership and educational events.
A series of seminars by the Ministry of Commerce attracted approximately 2,000 university students to host one of the event and outstanding leaders in industry and humanitarian work, including: GE Vice President, Google Vice President President of Coca-Cola and Founder of Cambodian Children's Fund.
These workshops highlight the Common Market policy, understanding, and updates on the Ministry of Commerce's progress to reform-hungry participants. In addition, local and international experts give lectures on a wide range of topics, from e-commerce to food security.
In April 2016, Mr. Sun Chanthol was trusted by Samdech Techo Hun Sen and transferred to manage the Ministry of Public Works and Transport. The Royal Government recognizes the importance of efficient, quality and cost-effective logistics infrastructure to accelerate trade and attract foreign investment.
With the return to the Ministry of Public Works and Transport, Mr. Sun Chanthol is committed to the necessary reforms to facilitate trade in Cambodia, low cost and attractive, as well as make people's lives easier. With the issuance of a new driver's license, the process of exchanging a new driver's license, applying for a vehicle registration and inspecting a vehicle (check) is effective.
The Ministry of Public Works and Transport (MPWT) before Sun Chanthol came to power saw many problems with the provision of public services. Coming to the Ministry of Public Works, Mr. Sun Chanthol set a time limit of 100 days to reform the provision of services to the people.
Mr. Sun Chanthol always said that providing services faster and closer to the people is the great desire of Samdech Techo Hun Sen. He has begun a series of reforms in the provision of services in conjunction with modern technology.
Among them, many services such as applying for a driver's license and renewing a driver's license have been set up at Aeon Mall 1, Aeon II and Norom Mall Chip Mong. Mr. Sun Chanthol also set up a mobile vehicle search to visit vehicles in remote provinces without check.
In addition to efforts to reform the provision of services, Mr. Sun Chanthol also made some important achievements. Mr. Sun Chanthol created a QR Code on the vehicle in July 2017. This modern license plate is only made in Cambodia for the first time. The new license plate contains only relevant information related to the vehicle, such as vehicle type, engine type, vehicle identification number, year of manufacture and so on.
Senior Minister Sun Chanthol claimed that the introduction of the QR Code was intended to prevent scammers by forging license plates and facilitating buyers to avoid fraudulent information.
Mr. Sun Chanthol also established and launched the online vehicle registration automation system in 2017 to facilitate vehicle registration, vehicle technical inspection, registration of driver's license exam and driver's license through the modernization of the registration system. List. This system will reduce informal costs, provide convenient and fast service, save time, can be done anytime, anywhere.
On January 7, 2019, Senior Minister Sun Chanthol inaugurated another new product of the Ministry, its own special vehicle license plate. The sale of this special license plate to give citizens the option to choose a special license plate can be ordered as desired, as well as facilitate the tax collection procedure.
Mr. Sun Chanthol also established international driver's licenses that can be used in 99 countries. Mr. Sun Chanthol also established a driver's license for the disabled, deaf and hard of hearing and announced that people with disabilities can drive legally.
Another great achievement for Senior Minister Sun Chanthol is the establishment of an institute called "Techo Sen Institute of Public Works and Transport" to train Cambodians on road and bridge construction skills. He expressed the hope that through this institute, Cambodian children will be able to build bridges across the river.
In addition to the efforts to reform the provision of services and create the above achievements, Mr. Sun Chanthol also made efforts to strengthen the quality of road construction. Mr. Sun Chanthol said that he was fed up with the people's ridicule, "the road is stuck or thick and thick."
He advised officials and the construction company that he did not want a corrupt road, he wanted a road that was in accordance with the construction contract, and he did not sign the contract for the road that did not comply with the construction contract.
In this spirit, Mr. Sun Chanthol regularly brings officers to inspect the road that was built and found a machine to drill the foundation and set up a raid team to inspect the construction of the road.
In his capacity as Minister, Mr. Sun Chanthol always pays high attention to the well-being and comfort of his subordinates. During Pchum and New Year, Mr. Sun Chanthol always holds a budget to support the officials and visit them. Mr. Sun Chanthol also developed an annual and monthly incentive program for good employees.
In order for the staff to work better and more comfortable, Mr. Sun Chanthol, when he took office at the Ministry of Commerce in 2013 and the Ministry of Public Works and Transport in 2016, built for the Ministry officials to sit and work.
When he took office at the Ministry of Commerce, Mr. Sun Chanthol built a building and planned to build a gateway to the Ministry, which does not have many. When moving to the Ministry of Public Works and Transport, located near Wat Phnom, Mr. Sun Chanthol also built another ministry administration building to facilitate the work of officials.
Despite the construction of additional buildings, it is still not possible for officials to sit and work properly. Because of this, Mr. Sun Chanthol also decided to ask Samdech Techo Hun Sen to build a new office building on Street 598, Sangkat Chrang Chamres 2, Khan Russey Keo.
The new Ministry building, which will be officially inaugurated under the presidency of Samdech Techo Hun Sen on January 22, 2021, will be up to 9 stories high and will have an 8-storey administrative building on each side. At the new ministry location, Mr. Sun Chanthol collected all the services of the ministry and gathered them at the same ministry location to facilitate the people's access to services.
Mr. Sun Chanthol has said that he would like to see his officials have a decent place to work, which is to honor and enhance the image of civil servants.
Sun Chanthol is also seen as a minister who has developed service delivery in conjunction with technology and improved service delivery.
In fact, these fugitives only create grief for the Cambodian people, especially in the face of punishment for their ignorant supporters. They have no real intention to return or live in Cambodia, because both their brains and bodies are obsessed with foreigners.
