The association's president's concerns highlight the risk of losing tourism professionals one day if tourism continues to be strained.
Speaking to Fresh News on January 21, 2021, Ms. Chhay Sivlin said, "Cambodia may one day face a shortage of tourism professionals due to the lack of reserves of all former business owners. Past tourism experts have stopped backing up. "These factors make business people in the field divided into many other jobs, such as construction, selling plots and other jobs."
Ms. Chhay Sivlin said it was a concern because it was not known where the tourism professionals went to work. On the other hand, if they get stuck in a new job, it is clear that the tourism industry will lose those professionals, as some professionals will not be able to return to the tourism industry.
"I am worried that when the situation improves, Cambodia will not have tourism experts to operate because the tourism sector requires experts to operate. If there are no experts, what will Cambodia have to compete with ASEAN countries?" "
"On behalf of the association, we have sought the support of many NGOs in the past to provide employment to tourism professionals, despite other occupations, but there has been no positive response due to the NGO's operation," she said. "Once-a-year projects cannot be prepared immediately."
"On behalf of the private sector, I would like to ask the government to take immediate action to help the tourism professionals, because the tourism professionals have come out to work as they are now, they have received training and Study for many years. This is a challenge if you want to find professionals who have many years of experience to work.
