Foreign Ministry Releases Results of ASEAN Foreign Ministers' Meeting via Video
(Phnom Penh): On January 21, 2021, Deputy Prime Minister Prak Sokhon, Minister of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation, attended the ASEAN Foreign Ministers' Meeting, which was organized via video.
The meeting expressed support for Brunei's theme "We care, we prepare, we grow" and the three key priorities that focus on building a harmonious community, preparedness and Adapt for the future to ensure the well-being of the people of ASEAN and a peaceful, sustainable and prosperous future, as well as promote ASEAN's recovery from the global Kovid-19 pandemic.
To continue the momentum of ASEAN community building efforts, Brunei has launched a number of initiatives to develop strategic trends to link ASEAN responses to disasters and disasters in order to ensure that the community ASEAN as a whole is getting stronger and ready for the future.
These initiatives include the creation of a forum that enables the people of ASEAN to contribute to disaster mitigation efforts, promote multilateralism, and promote ASEAN identity through the ASEAN Young Officials Training Program. Such as promoting youth activities on the peace and security agenda.
