Pursat Provincial Police Rejects Allegations That Authorities Beated Offenders While Cracking Down on Tonle Sap Lake
(Pursat): The Anti-Economic Crime Police of Pursat Provincial Police have denied the allegations that the perpetrators beat and injured themselves and are being treated at Boribo Referral Hospital while cracking down on crime on the water. Tonle Sap Lake.
According to a report from the Economic Crimes Police Office of Pursat Provincial Police this afternoon, on January 19, 2021 at 4:16 pm, the Economic Crime Police Force led by Lt. Col. Meas Bunthoeun Deputy Chief of Office inspected and cracked down on fishing offenses on the surface of Tonle Sap Lake at point (a) bottle in Kampong Thkol village, Ansa Chambok commune, Krakor district, Pursat province.
During the operation, the force found illegal fishing gear (b), a new and modern fishing gear that was banned in many places without its owner. Meanwhile, the authorities have removed one of the largest and longest heads to search for all owners to make an education contract and recognize the illegal gear to stop further fishing.
According to the report, while the force was retrieving, Khim, a male resident of Kbal Damrey village, Trapeang Chan commune, Boribo district, Kampong Chhnang province, and four factions, nine people came to provoke the police.
Later, the police asked Khim to come to the office to make a report, but Khim and his party did not come and did not allow the police to remove the illegal equipment in order to cause trouble with the police. Suddenly, our forces, fearing for their lives, pulled out their guns and told us not to be careful. I fired.
After the inspection, the police received information that Khim was hospitalized at the Boribo District Referral Hospital, alleging that the police had beaten him. In that, our authorities also strongly rejected and would like to ask Mr. Khim (the perpetrator) to come and explain to the competent authorities.
