Cambodia-Hungary vows to deepen bilateral cooperation as trade volume by 2020 exceeds $ 4 million!
(Phnom Penh): The first meeting of the Joint Commission of Cambodia-Hungary Economic Cooperation was held for two days on January 20-21, 2021 via video at the Ministry of Commerce. Successfully and fruitfully with high sense of responsibility.
The meeting was co-chaired by Ms. Tek Reth, Deputy Secretary of State of the Ministry of Commerce of Cambodia, and Mr. István Joó, Deputy Minister of Foreign Affairs and Trade of Hungary, co-chaired the meeting. High from relevant ministries and institutions.
The meeting was held to monitor the progress of work and promote economic cooperation activities and other priority areas, which were signed by Minister of Commerce Pan Sosak and Hungarian Minister of Foreign Affairs and Trade Péter Szijjártó on June 13, 2019 During the official visit of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia to Budapest, Hungary.
As a result, the working group of the Cambodia-Hungary Joint Commission noted the progress of cooperation in all fields through regular exchanges of visits and consultations, and continued its commitment to further deepen and expand bilateral cooperation. More.
For the field of water resources management, the two sides agreed to promote cooperation related to river basin management in response to the effects of climate change on drought and water scarcity, and to effectively manage water resources. Effectiveness.
For education, youth and sports, the two sides agreed to enhance cooperation in providing scholarships and sharing experiences on youth activities, Vocational Training Strategy 4.0 (VET 4.0) and the exchange of visits of youth delegates. The Cambodian side also thanked the Hungarian side for increasing the number of scholarships for Cambodian students from the 2021 academic year onwards.
In addition to the above key areas, the two sides also expressed interest and commitment to support the expansion of cooperation in the fields of industry, science, technology and innovation, culture, tourism, civil aviation.
In addition, the working group of the Joint Commission will work to effectively implement the Memorandum of Understanding (MoU) signed in the past through exchange of views and visits.
The two sides discussed the feasibility of using the Tied Aid Credit Cooperation project for the Techo Village Development Project 100 and a detailed study by the Ministry of Economy and Finance on the feasibility of using the loan for cooperation in Cambodia's priority areas such as agriculture. Food safety, irrigation management systems, digital technology and innovation.
Finally, the two sides signed the joint minutes of the first meeting of the Joint Commission on Economic Cooperation between Cambodia and Hungary in a cordial atmosphere and agreed to hold a second meeting. The joint commission will be in Budapest, Hungary at an appropriate time in the future.
Ms. Tek Reth Kamrong emphasized that after the meeting, especially the visit between the leaders of the two countries will help boost the economy as well as trade volume between the two countries will increase. In addition, Cambodia has encouraged Hungary to invest in agriculture and industry.
It should be noted that from 2017 to 2020, the bilateral trade volume between Cambodia and Hungary reached a total amount of more than 16 million US dollars. As of 2020, Cambodia-Hungary trade volume totals more than 4 million US dollars.
