Cambodia to host 2nd National Ecotourism Forum in late January 2021 in Siem Reap
The forum was organized as a panel discussion with keynote speakers from public and private sectors, representatives of the tourism and ecotourism community, national and international partners, and stakeholders as a result of the discussions. This will be included in the second statement on community-based tourism and ecotourism development, which will be discussed and approved at the closing ceremony.
The technical discussion will focus on three main topics:
First, the evolution and future of ecotourism and community in the context of Kovid-19 disease
Second, a complementary partnership between development and conservation in promoting community development, tourism and ecotourism
Third, support for cross-sectoral policy frameworks and mechanisms to promote community development.
At the same time, the forum also organized a mini-exhibition on community-based tourism and ecotourism to showcase key products and achievements related to the development of tourism and ecotourism products throughout the country.
