Report: The protected area of Preah Suramarit-Kosam: Kirirom National Park in Phnom Sruoch District, Kampong Speu Province is being rediscovered without proper rules.
(Kampong Speu): According to some reports and reports accompanied by real images, Fresh News Agency in Kampong Speu province shows that the red land for sale without permission in a village in Village 6, Treng Trayeung, Phnom Penh. Sruoch, Kampong Speu province, has been going on without any restraint from the authorities and professional officers.
It should be noted that at the end of 2019, the Department of Mines and Energy of Kampong Speu Province had issued a letter stating that Ms. Por Reaksmey's application for a license to dig red soil in the area of Village 6, Treng Trayeung Commune, Srok Phnom Srach was not approved.
According to the Department of Mines, Ms. Por Reaksmey's case of applying for a license to dig red soil in the area of Village 6, Treng Trayeung Commune, Phnom Sruoch District, Kampong Speu Province, according to the actual inspection of the department's professional team:
* First, the above location, the Department can not make a technical evaluation report to the provincial administration for review / decision in accordance with legal procedures.
* Second, the location for applying for a license to dig for red clay is in the protected area of Preah Suramarit-Kosamak "Kirirom" National Park, which was determined by Royal Decree dated November 1, 1993.
* Third: The above business application location is in the area where the Kampong Speu Provincial Administration has issued the land number: 10/19 d. 2019 on the denial and confiscation of forest land under state control.
Mr. Khon Sokhon, the head of the environmental field stationed there, said that he had not yet received clear information about the case, waiting to check the actual situation. In this case, according to some sources, some officials have participated and paved the way for traders to run business without permission.
Two cases of a couple who gave a motorcycle to the killer who shot the police and escaped have been transferred to Tbong Khmum Court to continue the proceedings
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Kuch Kimlong, Deputy Prosecutor and Spokesman of the Phnom Penh Municipal Court on January 21, 2021, decided to transfer the authority to Tbong Khmum Provincial Court to continue the proceedings on the case of two suspects. A couple who were allies of the perpetrators to Anaren who shot and killed the deputy director of the Phnom Penh Municipal Police.
The two defendants, Kan Channa, 26, and Hai Thida, 32, of Sabang 1 village, Dar commune, Memot district, Tbong Khmum province, provided a motorbike to the perpetrators to escape. They were both charged with "illegal possession of a weapon" under Article 490 of the Penal Code.
Two suspects, a couple who were allies of the perpetrators to Anaren, were arrested in Tbong Khmum province on January 15, sent to the Ministry of Interior and sent to the Phnom Penh Municipal Court on January 18, 2021.
The assailant who was shot dead after a fight with the police named An Naren, who shot and killed Colonel Reth Sinath, Deputy Director of the Phnom Penh Municipal Bureau of Minor Offenses on the night of December 29, 2020, after a dispute over a traffic accident in Maha Russian Federation Street in front of Phnom Penh International Airport in Por Sen Chey district.
