The following is the Prakas of the Ministry of Justice: Mr. Them Sam An continues to bring the humanitarian donations of Samdech Kittipritthbandit to 20 poor families living in Sangkat Toul Svay Prey I
(Phnom Penh): The Cambodian Red Cross Sub-Branch in Boeung Keng Kang District organized a distribution ceremony of humanitarian donations by Samdech Kittipritthbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen, President of the Cambodian Red Cross to 20 needy families living in Sangkat Toul Svay Prey I in the presence of Mr. Them Sam An, Branch Manager and Mr. Chhun Kim Ou, Honorary President of the Sub-Branch on the morning of January 21, 2021.
On that occasion, Mr. Theam Sam An sent a message of greetings and wishes from Mr. Khuong Sreng, Chairman of the Cambodian Red Cross Branch Committee, Phnom Penh, especially Samdech Kittipritthbandit, President of the Cambodian Red Cross, who always takes care of your well-being. Poor people who are suffering, vulnerable people and victims of various disasters, regardless of caste, race, color or political affiliation.
The Sub-Branch President instructed the Sangkat-Village Authority to take care of and search for the needy people so that we can prepare a charitable gift to distribute to them in order to alleviate their hardships, especially in times of need. The economic impact on the family due to Kovit-19 disease is in accordance with the principles of the Cambodian Red Cross, where there are difficulties, there is always the Cambodian Red Cross to help.
Mr. Them Sam An said that under the right leadership of the Head of the Royal Government of Cambodia, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, who has set out a win-win policy to develop the country as it is today, obviously related to the management of Kovid disease. -19 Samdech has set out a number of important strategies to prevent serious outbreaks, and so far in Cambodia, we still have no deaths due to Kovit-19 disease.
In addition, Mr. Theam Sam An asked people to pay attention to hygiene on a regular basis to avoid other infectious diseases, especially Kovid-19, which is a deadly epidemic. The world, as well as Cambodia, is concerned, following the simple steps taken by the Ministry of Health.
In addition, Mr. Yam Yuthea, Representative of Mr. Ouk Somvithya, Royal Government Delegate in charge of the Director General of the National Social Security Fund and Chairman of the Working Group of the Local Party in Sangkat Tuol Svay Prey I, also donated a total budget of 100,000 (30, 000) with the participation of commune chiefs as well as members of the Red Cross sub-branch.
(Prey Veng): Due to gambling addiction, even Tuol Neak Ta and Tuol Kob Khmor came to play, the police force of Kanhcheak district, Prey Veng province cooperated with the authorities to crack down and remove a large number of exhibits to the district police inspectorate to build a case. Sent to Prey Veng Provincial Police.
Authorities learned that the operation to crack down on cockfighting and shooting apples took place at Tuol Neak Ta and Tuol Kob Khmoch on the border of Pana Kandal village, Kotoeung Reay commune and Pana village, Ampil commune on the afternoon of January 20, 2021.
According to the police, the only exhibits left were: 14 motorcycles, 4 chickens, 7 chicken baskets, 6 pairs of chickens, 1 chicken scale, 1 metal table, 14 plastic chairs, 1 lion, 1 apple, some chicken wings and glass. A chicken mask, a watering can, some vegetables, and some shoes.
Authorities confirmed that all exhibits were temporarily stored at the district police inspectorate to complete the case file according to legal procedures.
Minister of Culture: Although Cambodia is peaceful, security, order and essential services remain a priority.
(Svay Rieng): Dr. Pheung Sakona, Minister of Culture and Fine Arts and Chair of the National Task Force for Svay Teap District, stated that although Cambodia is peaceful, stable, strong, but security, public order, people's well-being and services. Necessities remain a priority that must be addressed on a regular basis to ensure the safety and well-being of all people and society as a whole.
This morning, January 21, 2021, on the occasion of leading the working group to open a public forum on commune development policy with the participation of the working group and local authorities. Well.
At the same time, Ms. Phoeung Sakona praised local authorities at all levels, armed forces of all kinds in Svay Teap district, who sacrificed their physical and mental strength day and night for the cause to contribute to the development, peacekeeping and The well-being of the people in accordance with the policy of villages, communes, sangkats and the policy of safe villages and communes that the Royal Government has decided to set out.
She stressed that peace, political stability, security, public order are the key factors that favor the process of economic development and other sectors to grow in line with the political program and strategy of the Royal Government of Cambodia at all stages.
Dr. Pheung Sakona urged local authorities to hold regular public forums with the people to disseminate information and to get feedback on challenges and to participate in the development of villages and communes. And to strengthen accountability, operational cooperation among commune councilors to address the challenges, concerns, requests and needs of the people.
In addition, local authorities must promote cooperation in the provision of public services, development benefits and the provision of equitable social protection to citizens within their jurisdiction. Increase attention to provide services such as birth registration, marriage registration, death list, family book, residence book and Khmer identity card to citizens, citizens easily, quickly, transparently and without discrimination.
She added that the authorities need to strengthen and enhance the ethical capacity and attitude of service officials to avoid affecting the rights and interests of the people and making it difficult for businesses to apply for public services. Not only that, we need to increase the provision of support services for the elderly, especially the poor and helpless, ensuring that there are no elderly people who do not receive protection.
Ms. Phoeung Sakona also advised the Earth Authority to establish production bases in the village, such as sculpture, weaving, production of various materials using local raw materials in accordance with the policy (one village, one product) by promoting production in accordance with the geographical characteristics. Productivity and quality.
