Cambodia's banking sector remains strong and supports economic activity in the context of Kovid 19
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Chea Chanto, Governor of the National Bank of Cambodia, spoke about the strong state of the banking sector in Cambodia, despite the epidemic of 19 Kovid.
Mr. Chea Chanto's remarks were made on the occasion of participating in the program "Meeting to review the results of work in 2020 and work direction in 2021" of the National Bank of Cambodia and held on January 20, 2021.
Mr. Chea Chanto said, "Despite the situation of the Kovid 19 crisis, the banking sector has been stable and actively involved in supporting economic activities and reducing the impact of the crisis on businesses and the poor in line with the policy. Of the Royal Government.
He said that Cambodia's economic growth in 2020 suffered the first negative decline in more than two decades, mainly due to the decline in tourism, garment exports and construction.
"However, Cambodia has been able to achieve price stability and exchange rate stability, and international reserves have been steadily accumulated, more than three times the level that developing countries should be," he added.
The modernization of payment systems and the use of new financial technologies will also contribute to supporting the Royal Government in developing the economy into a digital economy.
