Please read the Royal Decree ordering the Honor of the Duke: Cracking down on a timber storage site, confiscating 5 bulldozers, 10 cubic meters of timber in Chey Sen District, Preah Vihear Province
(Preah Vihear): With the coordination and guidance of Mr. Ty Sovinthal, Prosecutor of Preah Vihear Provincial Court, Mr. Vuth Savy, Deputy Prosecutor of Preah Vihear Provincial Court, led the Provincial Armed Forces and Forestry Administration of Chey Sen District on 20 January 2021 Cracked down on an illegal timber storage site, confiscated 5 bulldozers and 10 cubic meters of timber in O'Sniet village, Tousou commune, Chey Sen district, Preah Vihear province.
Speaking to Fresh News this morning, January 21, 2021, Mr. Vuth Savy said that as a result of this crackdown, 5 exhibits of bulldozers and 134 pieces of wooden furniture equal to 10 meters were confiscated. Cubes, too. Currently, the bulldozers, scissors and illegal timber are being stored at the Chey Sen Forestry Administration for legal action.
Mr. Vuth Savy further stated that the illegal timber storage location that he led the joint force to crack down on was a group of traders who transported timber from the forest by truck to store it to lift the truck to resell. Kampong Thom Province.
He said that in order to contribute to the conservation of the forest to survive, he set up a network to monitor at all times to completely crack down on all activities of illegal timber traders.
Ministry of Labor announces payment of remuneration for seniority pay before 2019 and seniority allowance in 2020 and 2021 for manufacturing enterprises
(Phnom Penh): The Ministry of Labor and Vocational Training has issued a notification on the payment of installments of seniority pay before 2019 and seniority allowance in 2020 and 2021 for manufacturing enterprises. This is according to the announcement received by Fresh News on January 21, 2021.
The Ministry of Labor and Vocational Training has notified all factory owners, directors, enterprises and manufacturing workers who use UDCs that the payment of seniority remuneration before 2019 And seniority allowances in 2020 and 2021 shall be re-implemented in 2021 as follows:
1: Remuneration for seniority pay before 2019
* Pre-2019 seniority remuneration (if any) to be opened in 2020, to be paid in the first quarter and in the third quarter * Pre-2019 seniority remuneration (if any) Yes) to be opened in 2021, to be paid in the second quarter and in the fourth quarter.
2: Payment of seniority pay in the year
* Seniority benefits in 2020 are to be paid in the first quarter and in the third quarter. * Seniority benefits in 2021 are to be paid in the second quarter and in the fourth quarter.
3. Workers and employers can also negotiate to determine the specific procedure and date of payment of the above seniority allowance in accordance with the situation of their factories, enterprises and businesses.
At the same time, the Ministry appealed to the owners or directors of factories, enterprises, workers in the manufacturing sector and all stakeholders to uphold the common interests by discussing solutions with a high sense of responsibility to maintain work sustainability and Harmony in professional relations.
Vehicle Owners in Kampong Thom Province Reduce Costs and Worry After the Ministry of Public Works Installed a Fixed Machine in the Province
(Kampong Thom): The Ministry of Public Works and Transport, in cooperation with CMVIC, has set up a technical vehicle inspection machine in Kampong Thom province to inspect the vehicle technology (check).
Mr. Chou Kolla, Director of the Department of Public Works and Transport of Kampong Thom Province, said that the location for the vehicle was located in Puk Yok Village, Srayov Commune, Stung Sen City, Kampong Thom Province, more than 3 kilometers from the provincial town to Phnom Penh. Launched the test on January 18, 2021.
The director of the Department of Public Works and Transport of Kampong Thom province said that the inspection of this vehicle is to facilitate the people on the inspection, which previously the owner of the vehicle had to inspect in Siem Reap, Kampong Cham or Phnom Penh. Now the Ministry of Public Works and Transport is using fixed machines in the province to conduct direct inspections to reduce people's expenses.
The director of the department called on the people to understand the shortcomings and negative points when inspecting, especially to be organized because many cars cause congestion.
He added that the owner of the old vehicle must bring a certificate of inspection of the old vehicle and a copy of the vehicle identification card (credit card), and for the new vehicle must copy a copy of the import tax and a copy of the identity card.
Residents said they were happy that it was not difficult for them to travel long distances to park their cars. Waiting for a bathroom is also convenient, especially since the staff is gentle and ethical in making it easy to help the people.
It should be noted that so far, in implementing the Road Traffic Law No. 39, many people have been made aware, especially by taking the car to check the technical characteristics and to participate in respecting the traffic law. Cambodia attends ASEAN Foreign Ministers' Meeting on Video
