Samdech Techo Hun Sen and Donors Donate 52 Homes to Pursat Veterans in Pursat Province
(Pursat): Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, and Samdech Kittipritthbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen, President of the Cambodian Red Cross, and philanthropists have provided funds to build 52 houses for Cambodian veterans in need of shelter.
In a meeting to review the work of the Cambodian Veterans Association in Pursat province on January 20, 2021, after receiving information about the lack of shelter for veterans in the province, Senior Minister Kun Kim, Vice President and Secretary General of the Veterans Association. Cambodia immediately moved to raise funds to help build houses for them.
With this movement, Senior Minister Kun Kim, representing Samdech Techo Prime Minister, announced to help build 20 houses, Mr. Try Pheap, General Director of Try Pheap Company, helped build 25 houses and Mr. Mao Thunin, Governor of Pursat Province and officials Provincial government subsidizes the construction of 7 houses.
