Former CNRP leader with political rehabilitation joins CPP
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Sun Sopheak, a former leader of the former National Rescue Party, who has just received political rehabilitation, has joined the political life with the Cambodian People's Party. This is according to the decision of the Phnom Penh Municipal Party Committee of the Cambodian People's Party, which was received by Fresh News.
According to the decision signed by Mr. Pa Socheatvong, Chairman of the Phnom Penh Municipal Party Committee of the Cambodian People's Party on January 4, 2021, Mr. Sun Sopheak is a member of the Cambodian People's Party in Phnom Penh.
Former Cambodian National Rescue Party (CNRP) leader Sun Sopheak, who was banned from politics for five years by the court, was re-appointed by the Acting Head of State on October 10, 2020. . This Royal Decree was made after the obeisance of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia.
A total of 118 former CNRP members were suspended by the Supreme Court for five years on November 16, 2017, after being convicted of dissolving the CNRP in connection with a conspiracy with foreigners to defeat them. Overthrow the legitimate Royal Government.
So far, however, 14 former CNRP leaders have been rehabilitated by the King and the Acting Head of State, some of whom have formed their own political parties. Others remain silent and some join the political life with the CPP.
So far, at least three new parties have been formed or led by former CNRP leaders.
(Phnom Penh): The Cambodian side has agreed with the Indian side to set up a direct flight connection after the end of the Kovid-19 crisis to revive tourism activities and promote closer cooperation between the two countries. .
The two leaders spoke about the historic cooperation between Cambodia and India and strengthened closer diplomatic ties under the leadership of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, and Narendra Modi, Prime Minister of Cambodia. Republic of India.
Cambodia and India have a long history of cultural and religious ties, and in the past, when the Kovid-19 crisis broke out, Cambodians also enjoyed visiting India through many religious tours, which is why Minister Thong Khon suggested To the Embassy of India as well as the Government of India to re-arrange this religious visit after the end of the Kovid-19 crisis.
Regarding cooperation in the field of tourism, Minister Thong Khon raised the request for a direct flight connection between Cambodia and India after a delay due to disruption of the Kovid-19 epidemic. Ms. Tevy Ny also claimed that this work is also a priority in her mission as an ambassador.
Mr. Thong Khon requested India to continue to organize the ASEAN-India Car Racing and Self-Drive Tourism Movement, which will be an event to strengthen ties as well as promote land tourism between India and ASEAN. The Ambassador also fully accepted and supported this initiative because it will bring a lot of benefits to the tourism sector, while now young Indians really like this kind of tourism.
The Embassy of India also supports further coastal development projects in Cambodia as well as digital tourism development, with the Indian Ambassador pledging to facilitate the training of tourism professionals through online video systems.
In addition, the Indian Embassy in Cambodia will also help improve the infrastructure system in the area of eco-tourism, cultural tourism, such as improving access roads, badges, training local people to acquire skills in welcoming tourists better.
The two sides will set up a working group composed of the Ministry of Tourism, the Ministry of Culture and Fine Arts, the Ministry of Information and other relevant ministries, as well as the working group at the Indian Embassy in Cambodia and the Indian working group in New Delhi to carry out this work. Well, under the expectation that it will take effect after the end of the Kovid-19 crisis. What will Donald Trump do after stepping down as president?
