The following is the Royal Decree: Senior Minister Kun Kim chaired a meeting to review disaster management and the Veterans Association in Kampong Chhnang Province.
(Kampong Chhnang): General Kun Kim, Senior Minister in charge of Special Mission, is the First Vice President of the National Committee for Disaster Management (NCDC) and Secretary General of the Cambodian Veterans Association this morning, January 20, 2021. He chaired a meeting to review the work results in 2020 and work directions in 2021 on disaster management and the work of the Veterans Association of Kampong Chhnang Province.
The meeting was attended by Mr. Long Chhun Lay, Chairman of the Provincial Council and Mr. Chhour Chandoeun, Governor of Kampong Chhnang Province and officials from relevant departments, the Armed Forces, local authorities throughout the province.
Mr. Chhour Chandoeun, Governor of Kampong Chhnang Province, said that in 2020, the province experienced 29 disasters. Two droughts affected 1,840 hectares of dry paddy fields, 24 strong winds and five lightning strikes killed one person.
The province also experienced floods that damaged 1,792 hectares of paddy fields, damaged 1,170 meters of national and rubber roads, paved red roads and 47,940 meters of roads, and damaged 5,370 meters of canals.
On this occasion, Senior Minister Kun Kim conveyed the greetings of Samdech Techo Hun Sen and Samdech Kittiprittbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen to the leaders, officials, authorities and the Armed Forces throughout Kampong Chhnang Province.
Regarding the work of the Veterans Association, Mr. Thun Thoeun, President of the Provincial Association, said that the Provincial Veterans Association received the budget of Samdech Techo's death fund to provide the families of 88 corps members with a total budget of 352,000. 000 Riel, built 7 new houses to provide for veterans and handed over 12 houses to members of veterans. Veterans live on a total of 2,088 hectares of social land concessions.
On this occasion, Senior Minister Kun Kim also moved through departments and institutions around the province to help build 38 houses for veterans, in which the Senior Minister himself helped build 5 houses.
For 100 homeless families, the Senior Minister asked the province and relevant officials to work hard to distribute lots to provide them to all 100 families as soon as possible and on time.
(Phnom Penh): Ms. O Vandin, Secretary of State and Spokesperson of the Ministry of Health, highly appreciated the generosity of the Chinese government and people in providing 1 million doses of 19 anti-Kovid vaccine to the Royal Government of Cambodia.
Kovid 19 has caused a serious crisis in the world. For more than a year now, this global respiratory disease has not shown signs of diminishing or disappearing from the planet. To date, all countries in the world have the only expectation of a vaccine against 19 diseases that can help solve the crisis, protect the health of the people and improve the economic situation.
Companies in many countries, including China, Russia, the United States, the United Kingdom and India, have been working to develop and launch the 19 Kovid vaccine. The Kovid 19 vaccine has become one of the most promising and most marketable products. Vaccines made by Chinese, Russian, US and British companies are all being ordered from countries suffering from severe Kovid 19 disease.
Cambodia has also been seeking to purchase the 19 Kovid vaccine using the Kovak mechanism. The Kovak mechanism is an international mechanism developed by the World Health Organization (WHO) and the Gavi Vaccine Coalition. The object of the Kovak mechanism is the distribution of 19 Kovid vaccines to the poorest countries in the world.
On January 15, 2021, the Prime Minister of Cambodia, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, announced that the Chinese government, through its Ministry of National Defense and the Ministry of National Defense of Cambodia, had announced the provision of one vaccine against the vaccine. Million doses to the Royal Government of Cambodia.
China has been selling the vaccine, which is in high demand, to many countries around the world. About 223 million doses of Chinese vaccine have been given to Chinese people and people in other countries.
Chinese embassy officials in Cambodia claim that Cambodia is the first country in the world to provide the vaccine. This assistance may not be possible if Cambodia and China do not have good relations.
For Ms. Ou Vandin, Secretary of State and spokeswoman for the Ministry of Health, see that the gift of Chinese Kovid 19 is a gift born of the spirit of good relations in all aspects. Especially as an aid in the spirit of the common destiny community between Cambodia and China.
"For Cambodia, we, the People's Republic of China, have also considered the delivery of this vaccine to our country in a spirit of friendship, as our steel friend and acquaintance," she said. Come and go. And also another humanitarian sympathy because this grant is a humanitarian one. "This humanitarian is huge because 1 million doses for 500,000 people is a lot, not a little."
"On behalf of the Ministry of Health, as well as on my own behalf, I would like to express my deepest gratitude to the People's Republic of China for providing 1 million doses of this vaccine to our country," she added.
It is noteworthy that during the period of Cambodia and China being attacked by the 19-year-old Kovid, since the end of 2019, the Cambodian and Chinese governments have shown close support and mutual support. In January 2020, when China was hit hard by the 19-year-old Kovid and was discriminated against by many countries, Samdech Techo Hun Sen became the first leader of a friendly country to visit China.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen's visit led to great admiration from the Chinese people and leaders. Cambodia, through the King and Queen, also became the first donor to Wuhan, China, the site of the 19 Kovid Outbreak.
Later, while Cambodia was fighting Kovid 19, China also sent equipment and medical teams to Cambodia to fight Kovid 19.
