(Battambang): Mr. Keo Remy, Minister Delegate to the Prime Minister and Chairman of the Cambodian Human Rights Committee, has been promoting the welfare of the elderly in Cambodia.
Mr. Keo Remy made this remark during the opening ceremony of the training course on "Human Rights and Priorities for the Elderly" in Battambang Province on January 20, 2021.
This training aims to build the capacity of older people to understand and gain knowledge about universal human rights, laws and interventions in Cambodia, as well as to discuss the needs of older people in relation to human rights.
The President of the Cambodian Human Rights Committee also mentioned the importance of establishing a mechanism for community-based senior citizens' associations, which is an important contribution to supporting the elderly who are homeless and isolated. . Mr. Keo Remy also expressed his support and praise to the Cambodian Organization for the Elderly as a model organization that cares and does a lot of work to contribute to the well-being of the elderly in Cambodia.
In addition, Mr. Keo Remy also called on the relevant ministries, provincial authorities, relevant departments to continue to cooperate and support the organizations and associations of the elderly for the benefit of the elderly and the next generation. Find old age in the future. Three more "Leng" clans were given the title of "Duke" by the King
(Phnom Penh): Three other "Leng" clans were ordered by the King of Cambodia, His Majesty King Norodom Sihamoni, to be given the title of "Duke".
In addition to the three "Leng" clans in the Royal Decree, which was conferred by the King on January 20, 2021, Men Chenda was also given the title of "Duke".
By working as laborers in South Korea, they save money and work hard to learn more skills as capital to develop life in their homeland. After capitalizing through work in South Korea, the three "Leng" brothers invested in real estate and made them highly successful in the business.
The three "Leng" clans, brothers and sisters, even though they make money with real estate business, they are individuals who are recognized as simple people in society. In addition, the peasant family has always contributed to the hardships of society and carried out many humanitarian activities.
Their generous philanthropic activities have been praised and amazed, and because of the hardships of this society, the "Leng" clan have been given the title of "Duke" by the King. Honored for helping their social work. Summary of important news events for January 20, 2021
