(Phnom Penh): Several joint authorities have protected the machinery and a group of workers to implement the land decision to replace the demolition of co-debtors who built in violation of the land of 163 families who sold to the company.
The implementation of the decision was made at 7:00 AM on January 20, 2021 on the disputed land in Factory 1 Village, Sangkat Kork Khleang, Khan Sen Sok, Phnom Penh under the direction of Mr. Sin Sovann, Deputy Prosecutor Of the Phnom Penh Municipal Court and Mr. Mov Manit, Governor of Sen Sok District, as well as the participation of the Phnom Penh Municipal Gendarmerie and the Phnom Penh Municipal Police.
According to the authorities, the use of force to dismantle the construction of this hut was done by the authority of the land, the decision was made to replace No. 16 "T" R. dated June 29, 2020 of the Phnom Penh Municipal Court.
According to the information, at around 6 am, the police besieged the land that has been in dispute for about 15 years, which Ms. Chea Sarom and Ms. Touch Kunthy refused to accept their share and mobilized and Continue to build on the common land of 163 families that have already been sold to the company.
According to the information, the case involved a creditor named Banh Uta, a 40-year-old male resident of Sangkat 3, Sihanoukville, who represented ISBU (Cambodia) Ek and co-debtors, including:
* First: Chea Sarom * Second: Touch Kunthy * Third: Sim Kora * Fourth: Prum Yoeun * Fifth: Me Pov, who built a building on the land of the company above. 9973 square meters with real estate certificate number 12080106 3338, purchased from the name of Prince Socheat, representing 163 families.
According to the authorities, before the authorities enforced the land, the Phnom Penh Municipal Court issued a letter notifying the co-debtors to dismantle the building and other structures constructed from the real estate. This was twice, but the co-debtors did not dismantle it, so the authorities came down to implement the land and decided to implement it instead.
According to the report, that morning, when the Joint Commission registered Sim Korra, the son of Chea Sarom, blocked and was evacuated from the above location. The implementation went smoothly, with the people representing 163 families who agreed to sell the land to the company to help dismantle the building, and the craftsmen built a smooth fence under the protection of the authorities.
(Phnom Penh): Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, and Samdech Kittipritthbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen donate 5 million Riels to the family of boxer Choeun Sophanna, who is recovering from a traffic accident to alleviate his difficulties.
On January 19, 2021, Mr. Techo Vichea and Ms. Hun Mana assigned the donation fund of Samdech Techo to the humanitarian team led by Mr. Chin Bunthoeun to hand over Thoeun Sophanna, who is being treated for his injuries at Khmer Friendship Hospital. - Soviet.
In addition to bringing the money, Mr. Dy Vichea and Ms. Hun Mana instructed the medical team to take care of Thoeun Sophanna's patient to recover as soon as possible.
Please note that Thoeun Sophanna studied only in the 6th grade and also started his career as a boxer. When they are allowed to compete, they can only earn some income to support themselves. In addition to his boxing career, Thoeun Sophanna also took up freight business.
Unfortunately, on Sunday, January 10, 2021, Sophanna was involved in a traffic accident while transporting goods and was sent by her family to the emergency room. The accident caused Sophanna to have severe symptoms, affecting her head, breaking her nose and blinding her right eye.
