(Banteay Meanchey): The Banteay Meanchey Provincial Health Department on January 20, 2020 issued a letter rejecting and completely rejecting the accusation that it took $ 15,000 to run into the state medical system. This is according to the rejection letter from the Banteay Meanchey Provincial Health Department, which was received by Fresh News.
In its rejection letter, the Banteay Meanchey Provincial Health Department described the news as "false information, slandering and dividing internal unity, discouraging health contracted officials who are working hard to fight Kovid-19." In particular, seriously affecting the honor and dignity of the management and units of the Banteay Meanchey Provincial Health Department.
The provincial health department has also set up a committee to receive applications and review the documents to be sent to the Ministry of Health, as well as the relevant records and documents. The decision to enter the state is not within the jurisdiction of the provincial health department, but must be reviewed and decided by the commission of the Ministry of Health. Currently, the selection results have not been officially announced by the Ministry of Health.
In addition to denying and completely rejecting the above ambiguous allegations, the Banteay Meanchey Provincial Health Department also demanded that the press that published the unfortunate article present specific evidence to investigate and follow the procedure.
