(Phnom Penh): As one of the Civil Parties in Cases 003 and 004, I have been following the proceedings before the Extraordinary Chambers in the Courts of Cambodia (Khmer Rouge Tribunal) from the beginning.
I commend and commend the Royal Government of Cambodia and the United Nations for establishing a national tribunal with international participation to try former senior leaders and those most responsible for serious crimes committed in Between April 17, 1975 and January 6, 1979, to bring justice and truth to the victims of the Khmer Rouge regime, as well as to humanity as a whole.
I would like to thank the leadership of the Royal Government of Cambodia, especially Samdech Techo Hun Sen, for overthrowing the Khmer Rouge regime, saving the nation and the people from the Khmer Rouge genocidal regime on January 7, 1979, dissolving the Khmer Rouge political and military organization. Bringing complete peace in 1998 and initiating the establishment of a special tribunal to try former Khmer Rouge leaders to bring more justice to the victims.
But for me, the victims in cases 003 and 004 are also eagerly awaiting justice like other victims. The justice that I have been waiting for, whether the remaining cases are sent to trial or decided by the legal procedure not to go to trial, is that I am ready, because no matter what the scenario, I always abide by the decision of the Extraordinary Chambers in the Courts of Cambodia.
What I, as a Civil Party, now want to know is what the National and International Judges of the Pre-Trial Chamber are really doing, as it is too late to issue a decision on Case 003 appeal against Suspect Meas Muth while the decision to announce the decision will be made at the end of 2020?
On behalf of one of the victims, I strongly urge the National and International Judges of the Pre-Trial Chamber to expedite the decision on the appeal in Case 003 and Case 004, as the deadline has passed for several months. Come on. We really want to know and see how this case develops, because we do not want to wait until there is no island, no news from the Pre-Trial Chamber.
That the suspects in cases 003 and 004 are old and some of the accused and suspects have died, we are the victims are also old and some have died gradually.
We are already suffering from the persecution of the Khmer Rouge regime, some of whom are in a state of emotional crisis and are awaiting the decision of the Pre-Trial Chamber Judge of the Khmer Rouge Tribunal in Case 003. And 004 as soon as possible, without further ado, while the victim is still alive and the suspect is still alive.
I am confident that the National and International Judges of the Pre-Trial Chamber, who have many years of experience in the field of international justice, clearly understand the phrase "delay in providing justice is a denial of justice" and believe in the judges of the Pre-Trial Chamber. All will not damage the achievements and legacy that the Khmer Rouge tribunal has been deciding for the victims.
With respect to the victims, Civil Parties in Cases 003 and 004, the Ministry of Environment awarded Certificates of Environmental Peace to 6 rangers at Sre Pok and Phnom Prech Wildlife Sanctuary
(Mondulkiri): 6 outstanding park rangers received certificates of appreciation from the Ministry of Environment, including 3 rangers working in Sre Pok Wildlife Sanctuary and 3 others actively working in Phnom Prech Wildlife Sanctuary. Of Mondulkiri Province.
The handover ceremony was held in the presence of Mr. Neth Pheaktra, Secretary of State and Spokesperson of the Ministry of Environment, on behalf of Mr. Say Sam Al, Minister of Environment. Opportunity for him to lead a group of national and international journalists to visit and explore the potential of Sre Pok Wildlife Sanctuary for 4 days, from January 15 to 18, 2021.
Speaking at the Environmental Peace Certificate Awarding Ceremony, Mr. Neth Pheaktra said that this Certificate of Peace is a testament to the strong dedication of physical and mental strength to work to protect natural resources in Cambodia.
The spokesman also encouraged other park rangers who are actively working tirelessly in their duties in the Sre Pok and Phnom Prech wildlife sanctuaries and all natural resource protection areas. Now they do not receive a certificate of appreciation, but also do not put their hands down, must strive to provide more protection to participate in the protection of natural resources and biodiversity present in Cambodia to be sustainable.
In addition to receiving commendation certificates from the Ministry of Environment, all rangers at Sre Pok Wildlife Sanctuary and Phnom Prech Wildlife Sanctuary also received commendation from WWF.
According to Mr. Min Thoeun, one of the outstanding park rangers in the Phnom Prek Wildlife Sanctuary and received a certificate of environmental friendliness, before he came to work as a ranger of the Ministry of Environment, he and some other officials have been working. Hunting and logging for his livelihood did not make his family's life easier, but instead made him live in fear of the law.
Mr. Min Thoeun continued that after thinking about his past misdeeds, he decided to give up the business of hunting wildlife, which is an invaluable asset, to work as a protector of wildlife and natural resources. Let him love wildlife too.
