The above funeral announcement is considered as an invitation to His Excellency, Lok Chumteav, Neak Oknha, Lok Oknha, Ladies and Gentlemen, Relatives and distant relatives to attend the funeral of Disciple Sok Sitha and approve . General Knowledge: What is the most important black box for plane crash investigation?
A black box is an electronic device stored in an aircraft that records important information that can facilitate investigations into accidents or incidents of air travel. The device is commonly known as a black box, but in reality it looks orange to make it easier to find after a crash.
The FDR black box records data such as speed, altitude, acceleration and fuel flow of the aircraft, and it can store this data for the last 25 hours. The CVR black box records all conversations between the pilots as well as the conversations between the pilots and the air traffic controllers. The sound of the switch and the engine are also recorded by the CVR, while its sound storage capacity is limited to the last two hours.
