Expert: In 2021, the real estate sector in Cambodia will revive as vaccines become more widely used
Mr. Kheang Puthy said that 2020 is a difficult time for economic and social development, as well as the real estate sector in Cambodia as well as the world as a result of the Kovid-19 epidemic has affected almost all sectors. Except agriculture, food, etc.
He said that at the beginning of 2021, according to many businessmen and experts expressed the expectation that Cambodia's economic growth may begin to recover, in which the real estate sector can also improve. Gradually, too.
With the above-mentioned expectations, he observed that the real estate market may or may not be good, it depends on the actual situation of the risk of disease crisis, but real estate in some areas has the potential to continue. There is a market and there is regular trading.
In addition, he said, whether it continues to work, good or bad, is to look at the decline of Kovid-19, which scientists are finding a vaccine, and many major countries are adopting the use of the vaccine. High attention and caution.
Mr. Kheang Puthy said that for the real estate sector in Cambodia at the end of 2020 and the beginning of 2021, saw the sale and increase of some production chains gradually resumed, so this picture is a sign of economic activity. Back.
Therefore, considering the market situation in 2021, Mr. Kheang Puthy hopes that from the fourth month of 2021, which is in the second quarter, we see good signs and can work again.
"From my observations and analysis, it can be said that our country in early 2021 from January will have a revival of the real estate sector, but must be based on the vaccine situation," he said.
The chairman of the board of directors of the Association of Real Estate Professionals stressed that we need two to three months, a time when we can prepare for the success of economic activities to run smoothly if there is no threat of a crisis of disease again.
By 2020, Kantha Bopha Hospital will treat more than 600,000 children, while the Kantha Bopha Foundation of Cambodia will receive more than $ 20 million in donations
(Phnom Penh): Dr. Aun Porn Moniroth, Deputy Prime Minister, Minister of Economy and Finance and Chairman of the Board of Governors of the "Kantha Bopha Foundation of Cambodia" this morning, January 19, 2021, chaired the third meeting of the Board of Governors. Of "Kantha Bopha Foundation of Cambodia" in the presence of Mr. Mam Ponheng, Minister of Health and all Board members to review and discuss some important agendas.
The main agenda is as follows:
1: Operations of Kantha Bopha Hospital and financial position of Kantha Bopha Foundation of Cambodia:
In 2020, Kantha Bopha Hospital received 639,268 cases of children being consulted and treated in the outpatient department, and 132,443 cases of pregnant women were examined and treated in the outpatient department. There were 133,026 hospitalizations, 4,488 severe dengue cases, 1,492 cases of chickenpox, and a total of 24,822 surgeries.
"Kantha Bopha Foundation of Cambodia" received a total of 61,981 million Riels (over 15 million USD) and 6,000,000 USD, including: 40 billion Riels from the Royal Government, deduction from tickets Angkor Resort 2 million US dollars, donations from the Red Cross 1 million US dollars and donations from general philanthropists approximately 7,163 million riels and 3 million US dollars.
2: Implementation of the activities of the Kantha Bopha Foundation of Cambodia:
During the first 12 months of 2020, the Kantha Bopha Foundation of Cambodia has carried out key activities, including: fundraising and receiving charitable donations, public relations, and outreach of hospitals and funds.
The Board of Governors also reviewed, discussed and approved the Action Plan for 2021 and provided guidance to continue the establishment and expansion of the support structure of the Kantha Bopha Foundation of Cambodia in the provinces and ministries-institutions.
The Deputy Prime Minister instructed the Secretariat of the "Kantha Bopha Foundation of Cambodia" to make more efforts to educate the public about the presence and importance of the establishment of the Kantha Bopha Foundation of Cambodia in order to mobilize more charitable contributions from all directions to continue to contribute. To the operation and sustainability of Kantha Bopha Hospital and promote the spirit of "Khmer help Khmer" more widely.
