Read the following letter: Indian Ambassador commends National Bank of Cambodia for maintaining good macroeconomic and financial balance
The new Ambassador of India to Cambodia paid a courtesy call on Mr. Chea Chanto, Governor of the National Bank of Cambodia on January 19, 2021.
Mr. Chea Chanto thanked the Government of India and the Central Bank of India for their contribution to human resource development at the National Bank of Cambodia through long-term study and short-term training.
Mr. Chea Chanto said that India and Cambodia have had good cooperation since ancient times, after the day of liberation on January 7, 1979, the Government of India helped Cambodia in the process of restoration and development of the country.
In addition, he informed the Ambassador about the macroeconomic situation and the banking sector that the government under the leadership of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the Prime Minister of Cambodia, has managed to control the spread of Kovid 19 and put in place measures to reduce the impact. Affect the economy effectively.
Inflation has been kept low with stable exchange rates and adequate levels of international reserves contributing to confidence in the Cambodian economy. In the banking sector, the National Bank of Cambodia has introduced measures to strengthen the well-being of banking and financial institutions, provide liquidity and re-lending, which has helped businesses and the poor affected. At the same time, the banking sector ensures better credit quality.
She intends to further deepen banking cooperation between the two countries for the benefit of both sides. She praised the recent developments in the Cambodian financial sector, especially the important role of the National Bank of Cambodia in maintaining macroeconomic and financial balance and supporting economic activities in a situation where Cambodia as well as other countries in the world are suffering. Health and economic crisis.
She welcomed the modernization of payment systems, such as the introduction of the Bakong system, a payment system that facilitates general and cross-institutional payments by reducing transaction fees and making payments more immediate.
The Governor and the Ambassador agreed to increase cooperation in the banking sector of the two countries, such as: exchanging experiences on the development of payment systems, strengthening anti-money laundering mechanisms and terrorist financing, and training.
