Mr. Keo Remy: Cambodian Organization for the Elderly is a model organization in Battambang province
(Battambang): Mr. Keo Remy, Minister Delegate to the Prime Minister and Chairman of the Cambodian Human Rights Committee, stated that the Cambodian Organization for the Elderly is a model organization in Battambang province that has been active and has a clear and orderly work order. Expanded the membership of the organization to more than 1,6,000 members working for the elderly.
Mr. Keo Remy said this on the morning of January 19, 2021, on the occasion of presiding over the ceremony and distributing gifts to the grandparents who are members of the organization for the elderly located in In Prek Trop village, Norin commune, Ek Phnom district, Battambang province.
Mr. Keo Remy said that the elderly are an important resource in contributing to both nation building and family building for the younger generation because people have gone through many life experiences, which is also a good lesson, which is an external lesson. Others in the school are not. He said that the younger generation must respect the elderly, not only our parents or grandparents, but also to respect other elderly people like our family.
The event was attended by Mr. Tum Vira, Executive Director of the Association of the Elderly, the Network of the Elderly in Cambodia and the leadership of the Cambodian Human Rights Committee, as well as many stakeholders.
Mr. Keo Remy continued that the Royal Government is very considerate on the issue of the elderly, in which the Royal Government, through the Ministry of Social Affairs, always thinks about the welfare of the elderly, including the provision of cash in During Kovid 19. The head of the Royal Government has ordered the vaccine to prevent 19 cases of Kovid, and if there is a change, the elderly will still have a high priority despite the change.
Mr. Tum Vira said that the organization for the elderly is a grassroots organization led by the elderly in order to help improve the well-being of the elderly, their families and their communities. Svay Rieng Provincial Governor Inspects Svay Rieng City Development Progress
