Cambodia identifies potential commodities for boosting exports to China as free trade takes effect
Ministry of Commerce spokesman Seang Thai, Secretary of State for the Ministry of Commerce, said: "About 50-65 potential Cambodian goods have been studied on the technical barriers, tariff barriers and preferential tariffs that China provides to Cambodia to "Maximize exports to China."
He added that the study of the 65 commodities was based on basic documents extracted from trade policy documents and from the Ministry of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries, which had a clear and export-oriented basis.
He stressed that there are thousands of goods that Cambodia has the right to import to the Chinese market, but that does not mean that we have to import all the products, look at the potential goods to export, and if the potential goods have Difficulties in exports from the Ministry of Commerce and solve.
He said that currently the team is studying what should be exported? As for the goods that are planned to be exported, the team will advertise to the farmers to produce those products.
