Ministry of Information launches "Gratitude Award" for journalists from 1970 to present
(Phnom Penh): The Ministry of Information has established a "Gratitude Award" program for journalists who have contributed to the promotion of journalism in Cambodia from the 1970s to the present. This program was organized under the initiative of Mr. Khieu Kanharith, Minister of Information, General Department of Information and Audiovisual.
According to a press release issued by the Ministry of Information on January 19, 2021, the program was organized to commemorate the sacrifices of journalists who have contributed to the promotion of journalism in Cambodia. From the 1970s to the present.
The ministry said that for the first year, the organizing committee will select journalists. In particular, veteran journalists to study the history of work and qualifications to the evaluation committee.
The awards will be divided into two categories: five winners and five honorees.
Mr. Phos Sovann, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Information, said that this is the first step that the Ministry of Information has set up this program in order to thank the journalists who have contributed to this field for many years and will continue to this day. This.
