At this point, experts in the conservation and research of natural resources consider the rainforest in the eastern highlands of Cambodia as the last expectation for the presence of endangered and endangered species in the world. .
Mr. Seng Teak said that more than 50 years ago, large species of wild animals such as wild oxen, Asian elephants and reindeer, as well as predators, including large tigers and leopards, lived in large numbers in the northern and northeastern forests. Of Cambodia, where scientists have compared this ecological region to the natural forests of East Africa. But habitat loss and poaching have drastically reduced wildlife and biodiversity resources.
Meanwhile, Seng Teak predicts that wildlife populations could recover by about 30 percent in the next 10 years if timely protection measures are put in place through strict enforcement of poachers and natural loggers.
He said that the Sre Pok Wildlife Sanctuary is an example of good forest and wildlife management, as the area is registered as state-owned land and does not allow unauthorized people to enter the core areas of the wildlife sanctuary. This. He said that the Sre Pok Wildlife Sanctuary is an important part of the eastern highland landscape of Cambodia and a mangrove forest area that is important for the ecosystem, especially wildlife.
According to the scientists' report, for Southeast Asia, the largest and most interconnected mangrove resource area is in the northeast of Cambodia and has been named. As a forest area of the eastern highlands. The area is one of eight ecosystems with high biodiversity values for WWF Mekong Priority Conservation Programs.
The report from the WWF Biodiversity Monitoring and Research shows that in the last 10 years, the number of toenails such as rattlesnakes, wild boars, reindeer, etc. has been declining in the region. The core of Sre Pok Wildlife Sanctuary and within Phnom Prech Wildlife Sanctuary. Factors leading to the decline are deforestation, trapping, poaching and trafficking, and a lack of water resources.
(Phnom Penh): China's Sino-Fever 19 vaccine is scheduled to arrive in Cambodia in February with an initial dose of about 300,000 of the 1 million doses provided by the Chinese government to Cambodia.
The Prime Minister of Cambodia, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, has announced the launch of the first vaccine. The vaccine will be given to priority citizens, including royal palace officials, parliamentary officials, senators, government officials, doctors, teachers, the armed forces, motorbike taxi drivers, tricycles and taxis.
What are the features and development of Sinofam vaccine? In an interview with Fresh News on Tuesday morning, January 19, 2021, Secretary of State O Vandin claimed that the Sinofam vaccine was 79.34 percent effective. The vaccine is currently being submitted to the World Health Organization (WHO) and may be evaluated and approved in the near future.
Currently, more than 223 million doses of Sinofam's Kovid 19 vaccine have been used in many countries around the world, including in Asia, the Middle East, Africa, Latin America and Europe.
The spokesperson for the Ministry of Health also confirmed that to date, Sinofam's Kovid 19 vaccine has not been reported to have any post-injection problems.
She added: "Currently, they are meeting the evaluation team on the vaccine, they are meeting to evaluate. Thus, we think that the World Health Organization will soon be able to confirm. "Now, even though it is not recognized, it has been accepted by the World Health Organization for evaluation and will be included in the emergency use list."
She added that the Sinofam vaccine is suitable for countries in Asia, especially Cambodia. Suitable for storage of this vaccine because it can be kept at a temperature of 2 to 8 degrees.
She added that the Sinofam vaccine requires two doses per person to be highly effective. The duration of injection from the first dose to the second dose is 21 days.
