General knowledge: Dolmen stone structure is a famous architecture of prehistoric people.
(World): Tons of rocks weighing tons, which were stacked by previous generations, are called Dolmen by the world. The name seems a bit strange to most Cambodians because this type of stone is not yet found in Cambodia, but it is known almost all over the world and is preserved as a human treasure.
The Dolmen have been described as important symbols of prehistoric times and as a symbol of tribal unity, forming the human race, or rather, as a strict tradition left by prehistoric ancestors when they Still living as a tribe. According to archaeologists, these ancient stone rocks first appeared in the early Paleolithic period, between 4,000-3000 BC.
Dolmen remains a mystery to archaeologists to this day, as it is not yet known how ancient humans used to transport tons of stones and how they were prepared to preserve them. Do not fall back to the ground, even thousands of years ago. US Ambassador to Cambodia pays courtesy call on Battambang Governor to discuss cooperation efforts
