Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng: Eliminating Violence Against Women and Children is Not Excluded from the Safe Village and Commune Policy (Video inside) (Phnom Penh): Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of Interior, on the morning of the 19th In January 2021, it was mentioned that some programs have been removed and revised in the policy of safe villages and communes to be in the current situation, while some programs are no longer a concern.
Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng asserted that the drug problem and the elimination of violence against women and children were not excluded from the policy of safe villages and communes. So far, the revision of the Village, Commune and Safety Policy is almost ready to request a decision from Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia.
The Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of Interior affirmed that the Royal Government of Cambodia has been continuing to move forward in the right and strategic direction in strengthening institutions and protecting the people, especially focusing on High on women and children at the community level to ensure equal rights between women and men.
Regarding the principle of safe villages and communes, Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng emphasized that through the implementation of the policy of safe villages and communes, we have seen that we have all made efforts to implement this policy and have made good progress. . In the 10 years from 2010-2020, the results of the implementation of the policy of safe villages and communes have been very successful.
According to Sar Kheng, despite good implementation, there are still some problems that are still a problem and can be even bigger. For example, the drug problem is part of a program of safe villages and communes in the past, the relevant institutions have made great efforts, but as the drug market has spread, the number of arrests of criminals or drug exhibits has increased. Often it is not relieved.
Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng claimed that Samdech had asked Samdech Techo Prime Minister to raise the level of safe village and commune policy, meaning that previously it was only owned by the Ministry of Interior, but now it should be raised to not Of any other ministry belongs to the Royal Government, and we have expanded its content to a greater extent and will remove some points.
