The ceremony was held at the Kilometer 7 Mosque, Sangkat Chrang Chamres, Khan Russey Keo, Phnom Penh, and was presided over by Mr. Mon Kriya, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Labor and Vocational Training, Mr. Nasiet Osman, President of the Cambodian Muslim Youth Association (CMYA), senior officials from Ministries and will be attended by Khan, Sangkat and 25 CMYA volunteer doctors.
On the occasion, Mr. Nasiet Osman, President of CMYA, thanked and appreciated all the doctors who contributed their time, knowledge and resources in this valuable work.
He added that this is the first time for Russey Keo district of the one-year project that operates once a month. He said that after receiving treatment, parents and siblings continue to be monitored regularly by doctors, and medical examinations focus on common diseases, gynecological diseases in women and children, and blood tests for liver disease. Be and C. In addition to medical check-ups, there are also health education provided by our renowned doctors.
Mr. Mon Kriya sent a message of greetings from Dr. Osman Hassan, Senior Minister in charge of special missions, in a heartfelt condolences to the parents and siblings. He also thanked the district administration officials for their excellent cooperation. At the same time, the Secretary of State also reminded of health care, especially the prevention of Kovid-19 infection, which has so far transformed itself into a new, most contagious and dangerous form.
