(Kampong Chhnang): A young farmer living in Tumnup Thmei village, Chiep commune, Teuk Phos district, Kampong Chhnang province, has started a successful business of producing mushroom yarn and growing his own mushrooms after going through 8 years of experience.
Mr. Soy Channath, 33 years old, a farmer engaged in the production of cotton mushrooms and cotton mushrooms for sale this morning, January 18, 2021, said that he has been in the above business for 8 years, which he initially Go to study this profession at Kampong Cham Provincial Agriculture School, Kampot Province and also learn practical training on the farm.
Through his study and practical experience, he has been successful in this field, earning 60,000 to 70,000 Riels per day to support his daily life.
At the same time, because of this business, he built a house to live decently and also bought land behind the house to expand other agricultural businesses to improve living standards.
In addition to selling mushrooms and selling mushrooms above, in his home, there are also vegetables and fish that he raises, which local people support and come to buy and eat every day. Because the vegetables he sells to the farmers in this village are chemical-free.
