Pursat Provincial Governor Intervenes to Help Pump Water to Save Dry Rice in Some Areas in Pursat City and Bakan District
(Pursat): Mr. Mao Thunin, Governor of Pursat Province, on January 18, 2021, led a team from the Department of Irrigation to inspect the irrigation system, crop production and water pumping intervention to rescue people who are far from the irrigation system and have problems. Lack in some areas in Sangkat Lolok Sor, Pursat City and Trapeang Chong Commune, Bakan District, Pursat Province.
Speaking on the occasion of meeting with the people in the area, Mr. Mao Thunin encouraged the people to continue to work hard to grow and maintain dry rice crops that are producing better.
It is true that after the recent floods from Veal Veng and Phnom Kravanh districts, six districts of Pursat province were affected, damaging 20,412 hectares of paddy fields. We rehabilitated and for the second time a total of 33,540 hectares, all of which came through the National Commission for Disaster Management and assistance from the Royal Government of Cambodia.
He also urged the department to continue to provide technical assistance as well as pumping interventions to help farmers until the harvest is complete and continue to promote the cultivation of various mixed crops to farmers.
