Samdech Techo and Samdech Kittipritthbandit Provide Food and Budget to a Disabled Person in Takeo Province
(Takeo): Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia and President of the Cambodian Veterans Association, and Samdech Kittipritthbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen, President of the Cambodian Red Cross, donated food and some money to disabled veterans in Takeo Province.
A veteran with a disability who received this gift was named Nuth Saveth. The precious gift of Samdech Techo and Samdech Kittipritthbandit was delivered by Senior Minister Kun Kim, Vice President and Secretary General of the Veterans Association to a house in Takeo province.
Lt. Gen. Kong Kanarith, Chairman of the Finance Committee of the Mortuary Fund, together with Brigadier General Neang Sopheara, President of the Takeo Veterans Association, visited and handed over gifts to Mr. Nuth Saveth at his house in Chi Khmer commune, Traing district, Takeo province on the 18th. This January 2021.
On the occasion of handing over the donation to Ms. Sopheara, Major General Kong Kanarith highlighted the attention of the Cambodian Veterans Association, with Samdech Techo as President and Senior Minister Kun Kim as Vice President and Secretary General.
He said that the Cambodian Veterans Association always pays attention and solves all the difficulties of Cambodian Veterans as members of the Association.
Donations of food and money are often made to support the members of the association who are in need.
The budget has been steadily increasing due to the generous donations from the public from all walks of life, including investors, government officials, the armed forces, traders and the general public.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen considers the contribution of this philanthropist as a spirit of unity, a culture of sharing in the fight with Kovid 19 among the great Cambodian people, which has become a strong protection for the health of the people. .
