(Kratie): Preah Serey Samphear Eng Phalla was appointed by the Board of Priests of the Kingdom of Cambodia as the Chief Bishop of Wat Preah Vihear 100 Pillars to lead, manage and be responsible again for all the tasks on the construction work of the Buddhist school in the pagoda. Bhikkhu Samner to be in the dharma-discipline and take care of the time of ornaments and pedagogy in the pagoda from January 2021 onwards.
The announcement of the handing over of Preah Serey Samphear Eng Phalla as the Chief Bishop of Wat Preah Vihear Thom Sorsor 100 in accordance with the spirit of the meeting of the Board of Priests dated January 9, 2021 and the announcement ceremony was held on the morning of January 18, 2021 under the presidency of Preah Khos Thom Lon Sokunthea, Deputy Chairman of the Secretariat of the Board of Priests.
Preah Khous Thom Lon Sokunthea, a priest, said that the Board of Priests had decided to appoint Preah Serey Samphear Eng Phalla to lead the pagoda at Wat Preah Vihear Thom, as stated in the priest's proclamation. The management of the Board of Priests of the Kingdom of Cambodia until normal and stable.
Samdech Preah Khous Thom Lon Sokunthea requested that the monks, the committee and the Buddhists at the foot of the pagoda, the authorities at all levels should study and understand how to put this pagoda under the control of the Board of Priests of the Kingdom of Cambodia.
Samdech stated that the reason for placing this pagoda under the control of the Board of Priests was because there had been several inspections in the past but could not be resolved, but after a coordination meeting to resolve the issue, the Board of Directors decided Entered the process of Preah Serey Samprea Eng Phalla to continue to lead as the grandson of Preah Athikar Wat.
Along with the congratulations, support and encouragement of Venerable Eng Phalla in the announcement ceremony, there were also invitations from the Buddhist Committee under the pagoda, law enforcement forces and local authorities.
Please note that before the reinstatement, Venerable Eng Phalla also had protests and dissatisfaction from the Buddhists under the pagoda, as well as the committee and the abbot of the pagoda.
In August 2020, Buddhists protested and demanded the removal of the head of the Vihear Sorsar 100 pagoda from Venerable Eng Phalla, claiming that he had used the pagoda's lack of transparency and personal resources. Original. After the eruption and protest, Samdech Sangkha Director Non Nget decided to terminate the position of Venerable Eng Phalla from the Chief Bishop of Wat Preah Vihear Thom 100 Pillars and suspended the position from Sambo District Sub-District.
