(Phnom Penh): Another 100 dairy cows have been ordered from Thailand to be raised in Techo Sen Russey Trip National Park in Cheb District, Preah Vihear Province, while currently 100 cows are being raised and harvested. Next. This is according to Dr. Sok Touch, President of the Royal Academy of Cambodia.
In the press conference on "Forest Conservation in Techo Sen Russey Trip National Park" on the morning of January 18, 2021, organized by the spokesman of the Royal Government, Dr. Sok Touch confirmed that out of 100 cows, 50 Funded by Samdech Techo Hun Sen and 50 more at the expense of the Royal Academy of Cambodia.
According to Dr. Sok Touch, in order for fresh milk and bamboo to meet the market demand, the Royal Academy of Cambodia needs to raise up to 300 cows, while currently only 100 cows. Mr. Sok Touch pointed out that milking cows are limited to 9 months and will run out of milk to supply.
Dr. Sok Touch claimed that the conservation in Techo Sen Russey Trip National Park, especially the dairy cows can work because with the help of the Royal Government, without the support of the Royal Government can not work. Not now.
The President of the Royal Academy of Cambodia emphasized that Techo Sen Russey Trep Fresh Milk, in addition to supplying the local market, has also been distributed and provided free of charge to 15,963 orphanages and students. Come on, too. Mr. Sok Touch also expressed his ambition to increase the supply of fresh milk to overseas markets in the future.
Please be reminded that Techo Sen Russey Trup Fresh Milk is 100% pure milk with no added chemicals or preservatives that can harm the health of consumers. This milk is full of protein and high in calcium, it promotes health, promotes growth, nourishes the bones, and makes you smarter.
