(Pursat): Mr. Mao Thunin, Governor of Pursat Province and Chairman of Pursat Branch of the Cambodian Red Cross, this afternoon, January 18, 2021, chaired a meeting to review the activities of the Cambodian Red Cross Branch in Pursat. 2020 and set the direction for implementation in 2021 at the provincial branch of the Red Cross.
The meeting was attended by Mr. Khoy Rida, Permanent Vice President, Branch Secretary, Secretary, Branch Committee Member, Chairman, Vice Chairman of the 7 Red Cross Sub-branches, Executive Committee and many Red Cross Youth Volunteers.
The purpose of this meeting is to report on the results of humanitarian activities of the Cambodian Red Cross Branch in Pursat Province in 2020 and the direction for further implementation in 2021, as well as to study some of the challenges that the sub-branch has faced in the past.
Addressing the meeting, Mr. Mao Thunin, Chairman of Pursat Branch of the Cambodian Red Cross, expressed his appreciation and appreciation to all of you for your hard work and dedication in the past one year. Comes with better cooperation between the Branch Committee, the Branch Executive Team and the local authorities, although some members did not attend due to core busy schedules.
Finally, Mr. Mao Thunin instructed all branch sub-branch executives to contact village, commune and district authorities in the event of a disaster to resolve and respond in a timely manner.
