(Phnom Penh): Dr. Sok Touch, President of the Royal Academy, claims that he borrowed a house plan to borrow money from the bank to pay for the work of raising dairy cows in Techo Sen Russey Trip National Park. He said this on the morning of January 18, 2021 in a press conference of the spokesperson of the Royal Government of Cambodia under the theme "Forest conservation in Techo Sen Russey Trip National Park."
According to Sok Touch, every day there are about 100 dairy cows being raised in the park. He said the number of cows could not meet the daily demand of buyers, so he needed at least 300 more cows.
As for the reason for borrowing the house plan from the bank, he claimed that the Royal Government continued to help 50 more cows to be added to the Techo Sen Russey Trip National Park, but because the money came too late, he decided to borrow from the bank. .
Please be informed that according to Mr. Sok Touch's two main ideas, he wants to raise cows for milk to be used as a milk fund to distribute to Cambodian children for free and to write a book on raising cows. The first hand-made milk by Cambodian children to be a document for the next generation of Cambodian children. He also denied allegations that he was doing business for personal gain in the Techo Sen Russey Trip National Park.
