(Kandal): Residents of Kampong Luong commune, Ponhea Leu district, expressed their happiness to the commune authorities for responding to their request for the rehabilitation of Trapeang Reang Lake and the construction of two 3,500-meter-long roads after their request in the forum. Public in the past.
Mr. Leng Toun and Mr. Ros Sothea, residents of Peam Chumnic Village, Kampong Luong Commune, expressed their happiness after the authorities restored Trapeang Reang Lake, which was previously shallow, causing a shortage of water to irrigate their crops. After the authorities have restored, the lake is wider and deeper than before, which makes it easier because the lake is the main irrigation water of the people around Kampong Luong commune.
The same people continued that this is not only a good achievement for the water chief, the rubble that came out of Trapeang Reang Lake, the authorities have also built two roads with a length of up to 3,500 meters. Make it easier for people to travel and transport their crops.
At the same time, Ms. Heng Mlop, Chief of Kampong Luong Commune, Ponhea Leu District, also stated that she will continue to accept the requests of the people to implement their wishes, because on behalf of the commune authorities. As a servant of the people, we must do our best to develop at the local level in accordance with the wishes of the people and do our best.
She also denies any misinformation, accusing her of conspiring with unscrupulous traders to exploit the lake for distribution, but this is not the case. In fact, it is only following the request of the people in restoring the lake and building the road.
Allegations that she excavated the spawning grounds were not true, but the truth was that they were privately owned, digging to create their own fishponds.
