Due to drug effects, a man attacked and seriously injured a village chief while mediating in a family dispute in Svay Chrum district
This horrific incident happened at 2 pm on January 17, 2021 in Trabek Phrong village, Ta Suos commune, Svay Chrum district. According to Mr. Pin An, Svay Chrum District Police Inspector, the suspect, 28-year-old Keo Thou, had an unspecified occupation, his wife Nuth Ratha, 32, had a daughter and was pregnant with another resident of Keut village. The above reason just came back from Phnom Penh.
As for the victim village chief, his name is Sous Sary, male, 70 years old, occupation: Trabek Phrong village chief, living in the above-mentioned village. Rescue. The source added that this case not only caused the village chief to be injured, but also caused damage to some other equipment, including a 2013 Honda Dream 125 series motorcycle, completely burned and some other equipment.
The inspector said that before the incident, the suspect was traveling from Phnom Penh to visit his hometown in the commune where the incident took place. The frightened wife also ran away from home to complain to the village chief Trabek Phong to mediate.
Later, the village chief arrived on a motorbike. Suddenly, the suspect used an ax to cut and hit the head and body of the village chief, causing serious injuries. Only once.
He added that in this case, both the police and the district military police and district soldiers surrounded the suspect with an ax and refused to surrender to the authorities to mediate while the house was on fire, but finally forces It took us more than two hours to arrest the suspect at 4:20 pm the same day and send him to the Svay Chrum District Police Inspectorate for further questioning.
The district inspector confirmed that the police later tested the suspect with a positive result of drugs in his body. Phnom Yeay Sam is a Malay wildlife sanctuary and a former battlefield during the Stone War. Grows like bamboo in rows, desirable
