(Phnom Penh): Dr. Sok Touch, President of the Royal Academy of Cambodia, said that among the people who settled in the Techo Sen Russey Trip National Park, 7 families have volunteered to move out of this area after the mediation of the Royal Academy. And Preah Vihear provincial authorities, while eight other families are still settling.
This statement was made by Dr. Sok Touch at a press conference on forest conservation at Techo Sen Russey Trip National Park, organized by the Royal Government Spokesperson Unit at the Office of the Council of Ministers on the morning of January 18, 2021.
Techo Sen Russey Trip National Park was established by Royal Decree No. SOR / Nokor / 04014/436 dated April 17, 2014 with a total area of 11,435 hectares, focusing on forest conservation, cultural preservation and Both are well developed. After the establishment of the national park in the north of Cambodia, people have settled in this area of the national park in a row, up to now there are 31 families.
Dr. Sok Touch stated that most of the people living in the above national park are engaged in deforestation to sell wood to traders and to sell resin (resin), which leads to the loss of many forests. In addition, they often cut down forests in the dry season, including burning forests to cultivate land in the rainy season, which often leads to forest fires.
Mr. Sok Touch said, "The governor of Preah Vihear province has sent the deputy governor to solve the problem for the people in that area. Now, 7 families have volunteered and 8 families are still volunteering because the place where we set up the house is The well has a plot of land 30 meters long, 50 meters long, and in the park area, there are no schools, pagodas, no water, but can not be driven out because there is wood.
He said that when the people to move out of the Techo Russey Trip National Park, the Royal Academy of Cambodia will set up a checkpoint at the entrance to the national park to prevent illegal logging while the work ahead is now. Deforestation must be prevented because people living in the area continue to cut down trees.
According to Dr. Sok Touch, the livelihood of these 31 families is to cultivate rice on land that has already been cleared from the dry season and to enter the forest to find other non-timber forest products such as picking mushrooms, picking fruits and digging vines. Original. Another occupation is cutting wood for resin, with up to 5 liters of resin per tree, but the people like to cut down the whole tree to get more resin.
Ministry of Land Management proposes 4 points to relevant ministries and institutions to resolve land disputes and cause land disputes
(Phnom Penh): Deputy Prime Minister Chea Sophara, Minister of Land Management, Urban Planning and Construction, on January 18, 2021, sent a letter to a number of relevant ministries and institutions, which are the authorities occupying state and provincial land. Implement four points to avoid land disputes and cause land disputes.
According to the letter from Deputy Prime Minister Chea Sophara, the Ministry of Land Management, Urban Planning and Construction has observed cases of land surveying and demarcation for the purpose of granting ownership and leasehold rights to state private land without inspection and Verify from the Cadastral Administration that the norms of the plot lack the accuracy of each plot and cause land disputes.
The Deputy Prime Minister further stated that in order to avoid the problems mentioned above, the Ministry of Land Management, Urban Planning and Construction requested the ministries and institutions that are the authorities in charge of state and provincial land administration to implement the following:
1. All cadastral surveys of the parcels shall be carried out and verified by the Cadastral Administration, which is the only competent unit in measuring the demarcation of the parcels in accordance with Articles 229 and 235 of the Land Law.
2. The Capital and Provincial Administration shall assign the Capital, Provincial Department of Land Management, Urban Planning, Construction and Cadastral Affairs to measure, determine the norms and verify with the cadastral database system.
3. All land survey data for the purpose of requesting the Royal Government's policy to grant ownership and leasehold rights of the state private land shall be sent to the General Department of Cadastral and Geography of the Ministry of Land Management, Urban Planning and Construction, which is the unit that manages the cadastral database system throughout the country. Check and verify in advance.
4. All leases of state private land must be registered and issued as private state land titles first.
The following is a letter from Deputy Prime Minister Chea Sophara: Lt. Gen. Thet chaired a meeting to disseminate information and instructions from the Ministry of Interior on eliminating excessive noise caused by all types of vehicles.
(Phnom Penh): On the afternoon of January 18, 2021, Lt. Gen. Thet, Deputy Commissioner General and Commissioner of the Phnom Penh Municipal Police, chaired a meeting to disseminate the guidelines of the Ministry of Interior on the elimination of excessive noise by all vehicles. Type.
The meeting was attended by the Deputy Commissioners, the 14 District Police Inspectors and other relevant officials, as well as comments on the practical implementation of the challenges of the Deputy Commissioner in the implementation of the work. On the seizure of cement processing vehicles, which often cause noise to the rest of the people.
Next, the Commissioner also gave many good suggestions to the meeting to implement the announcement of the Ministry of Interior properly, not to implement more than the instructions.
On the other hand, the users of the cement recycling vehicles will be educated and fined according to the law, enforce the road traffic law and bring the vehicle to be stored at the competent place for 3 days. In addition, the General Commissioner ordered all district inspectors to educate all vehicle repair and processing locations to cooperate without having to process any cement that causes a lot of noise to the rest of the people.
Finally, the Commissioner advised all district inspectors to pay attention to co-ordinating forces to facilitate traffic at all congested destinations, especially mobile traffic to assist at all destinations. Solve congestion.
Please note that the implementation of educational instructions and fines for vehicles that make noise, the authorities will cooperate with the Ministry of Environment to use the machine to measure the volume caused by all types of vehicles.
On the morning of January 08, 2021, Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of the Ministry of Interior, ordered the Special Police Force in Phnom Penh to cooperate with the Ministry of Public Works and Transport to identify large motorbikes that cause noise to the people. Citizens.
The order of Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng came after Samdech observed that there were cases of some gangsters riding big motorbikes, processing the cement pipes with the wrong technical characteristics of the original format, and there was a loud noise that disturbed the people, especially Samdech himself. Also disturbed by the sound of the cement pipe.
Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng noted that in the past, these big motorbike riders were riding fast and some of them disturbed the local people and sometimes disturbed the sleep of the leaders, so the police officers had to monitor and cooperate. With the Ministry of Public Works and Transport to identify and address all these motorcyclists.
After the above order, the police launched an operation to seize these motorcycles, but some authorities used their rights and jurisdiction beyond the border, leading to strong criticism on social media.
Therefore, on January 11, 2021, Lt. Gen. Thet ordered the police force of 14 districts in Phnom Penh to suspend the seizure of motorbikes with loud cement pipes, causing temporary disturbance to the people.
In a voicemail message sent to the Phnom Penh Municipal Police, Lt. Gen. Thet stated that the suspension was pending a new order from General Dr. Neth Savoeun, the National Police Commissioner General, to avoid any clashes with residents because some motorbikes did not. No processing, that is, the original set comes from the factory.
Lt. Gen. Thet saw that after an order from Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of Interior, and Gen. Dr. Neth Savoeun, to seize a motorcycle to repair a cement pipe, there was a disturbance, some officials followed the instructions. And there are some pictures in the house, which is against the rules.
