(Phnom Penh): The General Department of Taxation and the General Department of Customs and Excise of Cambodia on the morning of January 18, 2021, held a ceremony to officially launch the function of integration (connection) data automation system between the two units.
The ceremony was presided over by Dr. Chou Vichit, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Economy and Finance, on behalf of Dr. Aun Porn Moniroth, Deputy Prime Minister, Minister of Economy and Finance, Kun Nhem, Royal Government delegate in charge of the Director General of the General Department of Customs and Excise of Cambodia.
Also present were Mr. and Mrs. senior officials of the Ministry of Economy and Finance, General Department of Customs and Excise of Cambodia and General Department of Taxation, as well as members of the Joint Working Group and Technical Working Group on the Automation of Information Systems The two general departments total about 50 people.
The Technical Team for Automation Connecting Systems has developed and finalized the technical specifications by launching the Soft Launching of the Data Automation System Integration Function between the two General Departments on November 25, 2020.
This integration function will allow both departments to retrieve data from the information technology systems of the General Department of Taxation or the General Department of Customs and Excise in accordance with immediate needs with high transparency and security.
Data to be shared through the automation system integration function and on request include:  * Enterprise registration information
