According to Mr. Eang Sophalleth, Samdech Techo Hun Sen's personal assistant, during the meeting, Samdech Techo Hun Sen and the Ambassador discussed and noted the improvement in relations between the two countries.
She stated that in her diplomatic mission, she will work to strengthen the existing cooperation to a greater extent.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen shares the views of the Indian Ambassador that Cambodia-India relations have a long history. In particular, that relationship is progressing steadily. Samdech Techo recalled that in the 1950s, India was a country that supported Cambodia in the independence process, and in the 1980s, India was the first country to recognize the Cambodian government, while the United Nations still recognized Pol Pot's government of Democratic Kampuchea. .
According to Samdech Techo Hun Sen, in the 1980s, India not only recognized the government of the People's Republic of Cambodia, but always supported and provided rice and human resource development to Cambodia, as well as helped to repair the temples in Cambodia to this day.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen also emphasized that now is the time for the two countries to work to strengthen and deepen the cooperation between the two countries. Samdech Techo said that one of the keys to good relations between the two countries is to boost investment and trade between the two countries.
In order to expand the scope of investment opportunities of the two countries, Samdech Techo Hun Sen asked India to consider the possibility of establishing a free trade cooperation agreement between the two countries as soon as possible.
In this morning's meeting, Samdech Techo and the Ambassador of India discussed the preparation of the visit of His Majesty the King of Cambodia, His Majesty King Norodom Sihamoni to India at an appropriate time in the near future. The relationship between the two countries will be even better.
