A committee of priests and Buddhists erupts in protest over the re-appointment of Venerable Eng Phalla
(Kratie): Venerable Eng Phalla was re-appointed by Samdech Preah Sang Neay Non Nget to be the Chief Bishop of Wat Vihear Thom Sorsor 100 in Sambo District, Kratie Province after an explosion involving the management of the pagoda budget. The decision to re-appoint Venerable Eng Phalla as the new chief abbot of the 100 Pillars pagoda has led to protests and dissatisfaction from Buddhists at the foot of the pagoda, as well as the committee and the abbot of the pagoda.
In August 2020, Buddhists protested and demanded the removal of the head of the Vihear Sorsar 100 pagoda from Venerable Eng Phalla, claiming that he had used the pagoda's lack of transparency and personal resources. Original.
After the eruption and protest, Samdech Sangkha Director Non Nget decided to terminate the position of Venerable Eng Phalla from the Chief Bishop of Wat Preah Vihear Thom 100 Pillars and suspended his position from Sambo District Sub-District.
After a period of silence on January 8, 2021, a new appointment was made by Samdech Sangkha Neay Non Nget, re-appointing Venerable Eng Phalla as the Chief Bishop of Wat Vihear Sorsor 100.
This decision made the Acharya, the pagoda committee, and the Buddhists at the foot of Vihear Sasor 100 pagoda unhappy and protests erupted again. Acha, the committee and the Buddhists gathered again to protest this morning, January 17, 2021.
Venerable Eng Phalla was claimed by Buddhists at the foot of the pagoda that he was not a descendant of Buddhists in Sambo district. He is scheduled to become the prelate of Wat Vihear Sasor 100 in 2016.
Ta Mon, the first abbot of Wat Vihear Sorsor 100, told Fresh News that the abbot, the committee and the Buddhists erupted in protest because Venerable Eng Phalla, after taking over as the pagoda's chief priest, had destroyed some historical achievements in the pagoda. And perform various tasks voluntarily without consulting with the committee or the abbot of the pagoda.
He also dumped a pond that was hundreds of years old, although Deputy Prime Minister Men Sam An, Minister of National Assembly-Senate Relations and Inspection, did not allow it.
In addition to the destruction of historical achievements in the pagoda and the management of various works arbitrarily, there is also the issue of managing the pagoda's budget, lack of transparency and lack of clear information.
Mr. Ta Somon described that the suffix that the pagoda received was taken by Venerable Eng Phalla and managed by himself.
The abbot described that each year the pagoda can earn up to 300,000 dollars, but finally owe more than 300,000 dollars to build in the pagoda. According to Mr. Solomon, this is an irregularity in the management of the pagoda budget.
Mr. Somon claimed that he and the committee of Buddhists at the foot of the pagoda did not accept Venerable Eng Phalla to be the chief inspector.
Yim Steng, a 70-year-old Buddhist at the foot of the pagoda, also strongly opposed the return of Venerable Eng Phalla to the pagoda.
