May you all be healthy and free from disease. "With prayers for a healthier, happier world and freedom from suffering." Pursat Provincial Governor Inspects Social Land Concessions in Phnom Kravanh District
(Pursat): Mr. Mao Thunin, Governor of Pursat Province and Honorary President of the Provincial Veterans Association, on January 16, 2021, inspected the location of social land concessions, both residential and agricultural land, in Say Village, Prongel Commune, Phnom Kravanh District. Lottery handed over to 628 families of veterans in the province.
The visit was attended by the Deputy Director of Provincial Administration, the Director of the Provincial Department of Social Welfare, the Director of the Provincial Department of Social Affairs, Veterans and Youth Rehabilitation, the Commander of the Provincial Military Operations Area and many local authorities. More.
According to Mr. On Sothea, Director of the Provincial Department of Land Management, Urban Planning, Construction and Cadastral Affairs, the above-mentioned social fitness land is planned to be handed over to 628 families of veterans, divided into two stages, including:
* Phase 1: On January 21, 2021 at the Provincial Hall under the chairmanship of Senior Minister Kun Kim, Secretary General of the Cambodian Veterans Association, 366 families * Phase 2: 262 families in the near future Families get 70x150 meters of residential and agricultural land, equal to 1 hectare 5A.
Mr. Mao Thunin said that the provision of land for social welfare is a consideration and care for the well-being of families and veterans who have worked hard to fulfill the mission of defending the motherland to achieve peace until today. .
Seeing this great sacrifice, the head of the Royal Government of Cambodia under the leadership of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, as well as the provincial administration, prepared residential and agricultural land as a token of gratitude to our veterans. He hopes that after receiving the social land concession, all the family members and veterans will take control and cultivate crops to improve the family's livelihood.
On the same day, he continued to inspect the construction site of the paved road connecting the town of Chheu Tom commune, Krakor district to the Chrak Laeang waterfall resort, which is 14 kilometers long, using the provincial budget.
