The following is a letter from residents complaining to Chbar Ampov district governor: Ms. Hun Mana and Mr. Dy Vichea donated to two poor families in Banteay Meanchey and Battambang
(Phnom Penh): Mrs. Hun Mana and Mr. Dy Vichea donated food, supplies and money to two elderly and needy families in Banteay Meanchey and Battambang provinces.
The donation was handed over to the two families on January 16, 2021 by the humanitarian team of Ms. Hun Mana and Mr. Dy Vichea led by Mr. Chin Bunthoeun, together with the local authorities.
The families who received this gift: First, 101-year-old Ms. Im Lat lives with an orphan and two young grandchildren in a helpless house in an old shack in Say Samorn village, Chamnom commune, Mongkul Borei district. Banteay Meanchey Province. Grandma's granddaughter is a widow with a small business just to feed her.
The donations provided to her family include: 500,000 Riels, groceries, clothes, shoes and a large set of kitchen utensils, as well as the team of Tevta House to study the location of the construction of Tevta House to facilitate In the daily life of this miserable family as well.
Today, Om Lat is getting worse and worse, unable to do any work, living with her widowed granddaughter, Toeum Serey, who traps wild rats for sale in the dry and wet seasons, earns a little money. Only a little to feed the family, then the neighbors living in the local community have compassion to help feed the food and water daily.
The second family is Mr. Yan Heng, 58 years old, living alone on the land of the old village in Weak village, Rokar commune, Sangke district, Battambang province.
The donations provided included: 500,000 Riels, a lot of groceries, clothes and a large set of kitchen utensils, as well as repairing the balcony and pouring cement around the house. Artificial legs for uncle to facilitate daily commute
Yan Heng, a former soldier, was evacuated to a camp in Thailand and was hit by a landmine, lost one leg and lost consciousness, but he never caused fear or disturbed the lives of others. Today, he lives in a small house in the village near his sister's house, and his sympathetic relatives and neighbors always take him by the way, giving him food to eat with love.
Dr. Heng Vanda elected as the new Chairman of the Board of Directors of the Higher Education Association
(Phnom Penh): Dr. Heng Vanda, Director of Vanda Institute, was elected Chairman of the Board of the Cambodian Higher Education Association for the sixth mandate 2021-2023. This is the second mandate for Heng Vanda to be the Chairman of the Board of Directors of the Cambodian Higher Education Association.
Separately, Dr. Ly Chheng was elected Chairman of the Executive Committee in the new mandate.
The election ceremony of the Chairman of the Board of Directors and the Chairman of the Executive Committee for the sixth mandate 2021-2023 was held on the afternoon of January 15, 2021. The ceremony was presided over by Dr. Sean Borath, Honorary President of the Association, Dr. In Viracheat, Senior Advisor of the Association and General Professor Dr. Seng Phally, Senior Advisor of the Association, and was attended by Mr. Oknha, a member of the Board of Directors. Of the Association as well.
According to the association, the election of the chairman and chairman of the executive committee of the sixth mandate was smooth, transparent and fair. The 20 members of the Board of Directors voted in favor of Dr. Heng Vanda as Chairman and Dr. Ly Chheng as Chairman of the Executive Committee for the new term 2021-2023.
General Prof. Dr. Seng Phally, Senior Advisor of the Association, congratulated Dr. Heng Vanda and Dr. Ly Chheng on being elected Chairman of the Board and Chairman of the Executive Committee for the new term today.
Dr. In Viracheat, Senior Advisor of the Association, congratulated and praised the management and progress of the Association of Higher Education Associations of Cambodia. He added that the education sector is one of the key priority areas that has driven the development of the country.
The delegation presented a congratulatory wreath to Dr. Heng Vanda, the new Chairman of the Board of Directors and Dr. Ly Chheng, the new Chairman of the Executive Committee, and took a group photo at that time.
It should be noted that the Cambodian Higher Education Association currently has 116 member institutions, which regularly elects a new Chairman and Executive Chairman every three years, elected by the 22 board members. UPDATE: Indonesia quake death toll rises to 56, 820 injured
