Iran tests long-range missile amid tensions with US
Tehran: Iran's Revolutionary Guards test-fired a long-range missile during the fourth large-scale military exercise amid heightened tensions with the United States ahead of Donald Trump's term as president. United States on January 20. This was released by Reuters on Sunday, January 17, 2021.
Iran test-fired a long-range ballistic missile during a military exercise on Saturday, which also tested dozens of fighter jets. According to the Iranian military, the missile had a range of 1,800 kilometers and hit a target set in the northern part of the Indian Ocean.
The Donald Trump administration recently sent fighter jets and bombers to the Middle East, raising concerns among military experts that the outgoing president could order the US military. Launch any attack on Iran on the last day he leaves the White House.
