(Phnom Penh): The Ministry of Health on the morning of January 17, 2021 issued a press release confirming the discovery of three more Cambodian workers who had just traveled from Thailand infected with Kovid 19 while 3 patients He was treated and released from the hospital.
The three Cambodian workers infected with Kovid 19 include:
1: A 34-year-old Cambodian man living in Preah Sdach District, Prey Veng Province traveled from Thailand to Cambodia on January 15, 2021. He is currently being treated at the Banteay Meanchey Provincial Referral Hospital.
2. A 26-year-old Cambodian woman living in Sangkat Poipet, Poipet City, Banteay Meanchey Province, arrived from Cambodia on January 12, 2021 and is currently being treated at the Banteay Meanchey Provincial Referral Hospital.
3. A 33-year-old Cambodian woman living in Rukkiri district, Battambang province, traveled from Thailand to Cambodia on January 13, 2021 and is currently being treated at Oddar Meanchey Provincial Referral Hospital.
For the three healing patients, including:
1. A 33-year-old Cambodian woman living in Spean Kandal village, Bavel commune, Bavel district, Battambang province, traveled from Thailand to Cambodia on January 05, 2021.
2: A 21-year-old Cambodian woman living in Chroy Smao commune, Thmor Kol district, Battambang province, traveled from Thailand to Cambodia on January 05, 2021.
3. A 29-year-old Cambodian woman living in Nimit 3 Village, Nimit Commune, O'Chrov District, Banteay Meanchey Province, arrived from Cambodia on January 5, 2021.
Please note that the above three women were cured with two negative Kovid-19 test results and were released from Banteay Meanchey Provincial Referral Hospital.
