(Kandal): Mr. Ek Sun Raksmey, Deputy Prosecutor of Kandal Provincial Court, led the working group of Kandal Provincial Court to disseminate the law and other strategies for effective law enforcement to all relevant officials at the district level. Ang Snoul on January 15, 2021 in order to participate in the effective implementation of the law to avoid misconduct.
He said that this program is aimed at disseminating the Code of Criminal Procedure, the Criminal Code and other issues related to practical implementation so that all civil servants in the army can work for the people so that they can not be illegally cut. Reduce local conflicts, reduce conflicts and so on.
Many of the main objectives mentioned in this meeting include the following:
* Second: Judicial police officers, when there is an actual crime, must immediately report to the prosecutor in the case of arrest, release, release of people must seek permission from the prosecutor according to Article 89 and Article 96 of the Code of Criminal Procedure. In the case of arresting judicial police officers who do not report to the prosecutor, it leads to the crime of detaining people illegally, and if the perpetrators are released, it is also illegal.
* Third: Village chiefs and commune chiefs must participate in the proceedings with judicial police officers when necessary, such as in the case of house searches, confiscation of evidence related to crimes, and this participation must be verified with judicial police officers first. Will sign.
* Fourth: Judicial police officers must be clear in writing minutes, searching, confiscating exhibits, making clear records, especially summary reports must be concluded correctly so that the victim does not become a perpetrator. While in this case, the Attorney General of Phnom Penh also instructed the judicial police officers on the clarity of the case or report.
* Fifth: About the signature by the village-commune chief and the stamping by the clerk on various documents, be very careful to understand the background of the story clearly before confirming all the documents, such as land, death, age And so on.
* Sixth: Judicial police officers must have a list of management related to the crime, record the time of detention, crime and release time from prison. On the other hand, village chiefs and commune chiefs must also have a record book to monitor the perpetrators, because all those subjects are people living in our commune village.
* Seventh: Judicial police officers in all departments must have technical officers to manage documents, correspondence and facilitate the suppression of advanced crimes.
At the same time, the Deputy Prosecutor also asked all local officials in Ang Snoul district to participate in this work to implement the law effectively.
