Ambassador Mikami Masahiro added that the two new projects include:
Japan's Kusanoni Grant began in Cambodia in 1991 to support Cambodia's efforts to develop and rebuild the country at the grassroots level. The project aims to protect vulnerable people from a number of factors, such as poverty or misfortune, which can directly threaten their lives, livelihoods and dignity, as well as promote community self-reliance.
It should be noted that since 1991, the Government of Japan has provided more than 63 million US dollars to local authorities and NGOs to implement 640 Kusanoni projects throughout Cambodia.
