(Kratie): The body of an adult dolphin weighing nearly 100 kg was found dead on the evening of January 14, 2021, with a 15-centimeter net about 60 meters long, which the perpetrator hid in the water. Deep at Kaing Prahok, in Kampi Dolphin Canyon, Kampi Village, Sambok Commune, Chit Borey District, Kratie Province.
Immediately after receiving this information, Mr. Kim Ky and the group of boatmen for the tourists immediately went to inspect the dolphin's carcass and cut off the mosquito netting and brought the dolphin's body to the group. River guard work at Kampi Post.
According to the team's inspection, the dolphin carcass was swollen and had 15 cm of netting wrapped around the base of the tail and the entire body of the dolphin.
After examining the dolphin's body, the team concluded that the dolphin had died as a result of being caught in a fishing net.
After examining the dolphin carcass, the team weighed, measured and photographed with the following summary data: The dead dolphin was a male dolphin, 198 cm long, weighing 85 kg, estimated age 12 to 15 years, swollen condition, death time is about 3 days.
The bodies of the dolphins were stored in a freezer, dissected for medical analysis on January 15, 2021, and stored in a freezer at the WWF office in Kratie province.
This is the second dolphin to die in 2021 from January 1 to 14, including one baby dolphin and one adult dolphin.
Mr. Mok Ponlok confirmed to Fresh News on the evening of January 15 that from January 1, he made a plan to work in cooperation with local authorities, police, administrative posts, protected areas and fishing communities. Forever, but there are still corrupt suspects stealing nets in the canyon, destroying dolphins.
He added that the police work hard, but the perpetrators take the opportunity when the patrols sometimes, the police patrol day and night do not go to the criminals to the night to destroy more. Authorities are currently searching for the culprits in order to send the case to court for sentencing. US Secretary of Health's decision to resign over recent violence at Congress
