The King and Queen Mother send condolences on the passing of King Norodom Yuvneath (Video inside) (Phnom Penh): His Majesty King Norodom Sihamoni, King of Cambodia and Queen Norodom Monineath Sihanouk, the Queen Mother of Cambodia, sent a message of condolences on the passing of King Norodom Yuvnath.
In a condolence message from the King and Queen Mother, received by Fresh News on January 15, 2021, it reads: "I am saddened to learn of the arrival. The death of His Majesty King Norodom Yuvneath, Personal Adviser to the King of the Kingdom of Cambodia, on January 14, 2021, at the age of 78 in the United States.
I would like to express my deepest condolences and condolences to the concubines and their families and all the relatives and friends of the deceased. The death of King Norodom Yuvnath is the loss of a wonderful husband, father and grandfather, beloved sons, daughters, grandsons, granddaughters, as well as relatives and friends.
I would like to pray for the soul of Samdech Preah Borom Rama Norodom Yuvneath to go to death, do not mourn.
