Samdech Chao Feang Kong Sam Ol sends congratulatory letter to Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng on the occasion of his 70th birthday
(Phnom Penh): Samdech Chao Feang Vor Vieng Chey, President of Srengkar Kong Sam Ol, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of the Royal Palace, sends a congratulatory message to Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of Interior, on the occasion of his 70th birthday on January 15. This year 2021.
The following is the letter from the King: Cambodia exported more than 70,000 tons of fresh peppers, an increase of more than 27%
(Phnom Penh): As the government sets out policies to increase agricultural productivity, during the 19 1940 Kovid crisis, Cambodia could export more than 70,000 tonnes of fresh peppers, an increase of more than 27 percent.
According to data from the General Department of Agriculture of the Ministry of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries, fresh pepper exports in 2020 will reach 70,546 tons, an increase of 27.08 percent compared to 555,513 tons in 2019.
Mr. Chhim Vachira, Director of the Battambang Provincial Department of Agriculture, confirmed that the area under pepper cultivation in Battambang Province by 2020 will also increase in some districts. He said that the area under vegetable cultivation (all kinds of vegetables and peppers) in Battambang province in 2020 will increase to more than 1,000 hectares, and this increase is due to the government's policy to strengthen and expand the potential. Agricultural products.
He said that despite the Kovid 19 crisis in 2020, the price of peppers was much higher than last year and the market was not difficult.
He added that the Department of Agriculture and provincial authorities always encourage farmers to increase the cultivation of other crops to supply market demand. In addition, there is a push for farming as a business venture or contract trading.
This year, the area under pepper cultivation will be better than last year, because in 2020, 96 farming communities signed contracts with companies or collectors directly.
Mr. Prum Vit, Deputy Director of the Battambang Provincial Accounting Situation Office, confirmed that the area under pepper cultivation in 2020 in Battambang province is 196 hectares and more than 536 tons have been collected.
Kim Huot, director of the Battambang Provincial Department of Commerce, said that although the yield of fresh peppers in Battambang in 2020 did not increase much, but for the export of fresh peppers to Thailand through Battambang is more than 32,000 tons. .
