Rong Chhun was arrested on July 31, 2020, after committing the crime of inciting unrest during a visit to the Cambodian-Vietnamese border in Tbong Khmum province. While visiting the provincial border, Mr. Rong Chhun issued a statement to the public that the new border post between Cambodia and Vietnam had entered Cambodian territory about 500 meters.
Immediately after the allegations, the Cambodian Joint Border Affairs Committee dismissed Rong Chhun's statement as false and exaggerated. The Joint Committee on Border Affairs considers Rong Chhun's broadcast to be malicious in order to mislead the national and international public by making baseless allegations about the Royal Government's border work.
On August 1, 2020, the Phnom Penh Municipal Court issued a temporary detention order for Rong Chhun on charges of "inciting serious social security disturbances" under Article 495 of the Kingdom Penal Code. Cambodia.
