(Tbong Khmum): Deputy Prime Minister Chea Sophara called on the people of Krouch Chhmar district, Tbong Khmum province to jointly maintain lakes, dams and canals at their localities to grow crops. At the same time, he recommended to farmers that farmers should not sell their fertile land, because the sale of this land earns money only once, but if left to rent or grow crops will get a lifetime income.
The Deputy Prime Minister told the people, especially the village / commune authorities, to study clearly how to dig canals and dams to store enough water to be able to use enough in each area, while the working group is always ready to help as requested. Blessings of the base.
Taking that opportunity, the Deputy Prime Minister also addressed the land issue in the area next to the lake to the people by using a good win-win strategy and encouraged the people to help buy cows that people raise.
Separately, in Chhouk commune, the team drew water to save rice at Kliv and Boeung Kadey by rehabilitating canals to draw water from the same lake, which can irrigate more than 1,500 hectares. National University of Battambang organizes roundtable and press conference on the potential and strategic plan of the University
