Minister Mam Bun Heng Inspects 19 Kovid Patients in Banteay Meanchey Province
The Minister brought greetings and appreciation from Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia to the leaders, civil servants and staff of all hospitals who have worked hard to provide health services to 19 Kovid patients as well as Other diseases with high responsibility and good professional ethics.
The Minister expressed his deep gratitude to all the staff and health workers who are providing health services to 19 Kovid patients at the hospital, as well as those who are serving the people at the Chaktaly Sak Center. Experienced and in the community who have worked hard to provide a high level of professional ethical service.
He also pointed out that the fact that Banteay Meanchey province has found a large number of 19 Kovid patients reflects the strong efforts of staff, health officials and all relevant institutions to prevent the transmission of 19 Kovid virus. To spread to communities in the country.
He expressed his appreciation to all health officials and staff who have taken great care to protect themselves from being infected by health workers while serving the people in the past and instructed all health workers to continue. Good cooperation, high level of attention while working, especially when working to provide services to the people.
Four major tourism poles and more than 200 development projects are included in the draft Kep Tourism Development Master Plan
(Phnom Penh): The Inter-Ministerial Commission to Develop a Master Plan for Tourism Development in Kep Province has completed its research study in this southwestern province by compiling a "Draft Master Plan for Tourism Development in Kep Province" in Four major tourism poles and 251 development projects have been included in the draft master plan.
After compiling the draft document, the Inter-Ministerial Commission convened a meeting to review, discuss and provide additional input to the draft master plan. The meeting was chaired by Mr. Thong Khon, Minister of Tourism and Chairman of the Inter-Ministerial Commission at the Ministry of Tourism on January 14, 2021.
In the above meeting, Minister Thong Khon stated that the purpose of the master plan for the development of tourism in Kep is to develop Kep into a "high-end luxury tourism destination" with consideration. Attractiveness, regional and global competitiveness, in particular, must ensure equality, equity, transparency, sustainability and innovation.
The Minister said that the master plan for the development of tourism in Kep is an important strategic document that can help restore and promote tourism in Kep during the Kovid-19 crisis as well as in the post-Kovid-19 crisis. Well.
The meeting presented nine key strategies in the draft master plan for tourism development in Kep, including:
In the above nine core strategies, there are 49 detailed strategies, divided into 98 activities, equivalent to 251 projects.
Ny Phally, Undersecretary of State at the Ministry of Tourism and Chairman of the Secretariat of the Inter-Ministerial Commission, said that the Inter-Ministerial Commission has identified four major tourism development poles for Kep, including the current Kep city, Angkor, Phnom Vly and Archipelago.
